(Moscow) - The head of the Russian delegation leading talks with Ukraine said on Sunday that the Moscow side would wait for a response from Kiev.
A Russian delegation arrived in Belarus on Sunday to open talks with Ukraine in the face of an escalating war. It could be the first talks between Russia and Ukraine since Moscow launched a military operation on February 24.
According to Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov, a delegation from Russia, including officials from the Foreign and Defense Ministries, as well as President Putin's office, arrived in Belarus on Sunday for talks. With its Ukrainian counterpart in Gomel.
But Ukrainian President Recep Tayyip Erdogan has denied holding talks in Gomel, accusing Belarus of joining Russia in invading Ukraine. He added that Ukraine remains open to negotiations with Russia and wants peace, but suggested holding talks in a country or location other than Belarus.
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy on Sunday continued to dismiss talks with Russia in Belarus, saying Belarus was cooperating with Russia in the invasion of Ukraine. However, the Ukrainian side has stated that it wants peace and is always ready to participate in talks with Russia in locations or countries other than Belarus.
According to Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov, the Russian delegation, which includes officials from the Foreign and Defense Ministries, as well as President Putin's office, arrived in Belarus on Sunday for talks with the Kremlin. Ukrainian partner in Gomel.
