TOP NEWS: ASEAN calls on all parties to the Russia-Ukraine conflict to exercise maximum restraint and seek dialogue to prevent the situation from escalating
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN, on Sunday morning, February 27, 2022, issued a statement calling on all parties to the Russia-Ukraine conflict to exercise maximum restraint and seek dialogue. From the ability to prevent conflicts from escalating.
The statement said ASEAN foreign ministers were "deeply concerned" about the development of the situation and the armed conflict in Ukraine.
In this statement, ASEAN called on all parties concerned to exercise the utmost restraint and do their utmost to continue the dialogue through all channels, including diplomatic means, to prevent the situation from escalating. "Reduce tensions and find a peaceful solution in accordance with international law, the principles of the UN Charter and the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia."
ASEAN also expressed confidence that the parties to the Russia-Ukraine conflict have not run out of opportunities for peaceful dialogue to prevent the situation from escalating out of control. For the sake of peace, security, stability and harmonious coexistence, it is the responsibility of all parties to uphold the principles of mutual respect for sovereignty, territorial integrity and equal rights of the people. All nations.
