(Oddar Meanchey): The Philippine Ambassador to Cambodia, Mary Amelita Aquino, paid her first visit to Anlong Veng Local Historic Site on February 26, 2022.
At 8:00 am, the Ambassador and the Philippine Military Attaché arrived at the office of the Anlong Veng Peace Center with a warm welcome from Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of the Anlong Veng Peace Center. After that, Dr. Ly Sok Kheang presented the action plan of Anlong Veng Peace Center, the map of Anlong Veng district and the project to build a fence along the Dangrek mountain range.
Afterwards, the delegation traveled to the hideouts of Pol Pot and Khieu Samphan at Kbal Tonsong, located on Dangrek Mountain, 24 km from the roundabout of Anlong Veng District. Along the way, there are beautiful views of the forest and many reservoirs left over from the Khmer Rouge era.
Apart from the forest landscape, you can also see the lush green plantations of the villagers and the daily life of the Cambodian people along the Cambodian-Thai border. Pol Pot's hideout was built in 1993 after Khmer Rouge leaders chose its last strategic and strategic location.
The delegation also visited Pol Pot's hideout. The Ambassador learned about the history of the covert movement and guerrilla warfare when Anlong Veng became the last Khmer Rouge stronghold.
The delegation also returned to Ta Mok's former meetinghouse on the ridge of Dangrek Mountain, which has now become the Anlong Veng Peace Center. The house was built in 1995 to house Khmer Rouge leaders such as Pol Pot, Khieu Samphan, Nuon Chea, Son Sen and several brigade commanders.
The site of Pol Pot's cremation was the third point of the visit. At that time, the Ambassador also listened to the history from the trial of Pol Pot by the People's Court and the project to build the roof of Pol Pot tomb that will start soon.
The conversation between the Philippine Ambassador and the director of the Anlong Veng Peace Center lasted about 30 minutes. At 2 pm, the Philippine Ambassador to Cambodia and the Philippine Military Attaché paid a courtesy call on General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of the Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Chairman of the "Anlong Veng Victory Stupa" subcommittee.
The delegation then proceeded to the Ta Mok Museum, or the former Ta Mok House, built in 1993. Today, the former Ta Mok house is an important place in Anlong Veng district that can attract national and international tourists to visit.
Finally, the Philippine Ambassador, including the Deputy Attorney General, expressed his pleasure to welcome you to the Anlong Veng Historic Site.
