He emphasized that Battambang is a province bordering Thailand, serving the exchange of goods between Cambodia and Thailand. In addition, this northwestern province has a rice mill, a cement factory and stone and sand transportation activities. These business activities make road transport very busy and there are also significant overweight transport offenses.
Regarding the crackdown on overcrowding, Mr. Soeum Bunrith, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, said that Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Provincial Board of Governors, paid close attention to cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works to crack down on all overcrowded vehicles. Weight determined by law.
The deputy governor also claimed that Mr. Sok Lou had issued a very strict order to all law enforcement officers, both civilian and armed forces, especially officials at the weighing station, to enforce the law in the most transparent and fair manner. In particular, avoid colluding with overweight carriers, otherwise they will be removed from office and take disciplinary action.
"Absolutely do not intervene or intervene for companies that carry more than this limit. If there is any conspiracy, we will remove the official from the weighing station immediately. His Excellency the provincial governor has a strict policy on this point. This is the confirmation of Mr. Soeum Bunrith.
Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport confirmed that Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, was determined to fight overweight. In particular, strongly oppose any intervention in the release of seized vehicles.
