Phnom Penh and 3 Cities of Cambodia Receive ASEAN Environmental Sustainability Cities Award and Certificate of Clean Land, Clean Water and Clean Air
(Sihanoukville): The Ministry of Environment presented awards and certificates to Phnom Penh and three other cities that received the ASEAN Environmental Sustainable Cities Award and the ASEAN Clean Land, Water and Air Recognition Certificate achieved at the meeting. The 16th ASEAN Environment Ministers, organized by Indonesia on October 21, 2021.
Cambodia has received 3 certificates: Kep is a city of clean air, Phnom Penh is a city of clean water and Sen Monorom is a city of clean land. Separately, Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province received the ASEAN Environmental Sustainability City Award 2021.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, said at the ceremony held on the afternoon of February 25, 2022 that the award and certification are due to peace and political stability. .
The Royal Government of Cambodia has been continuously promoting sustainable development and providing warmth, peace and well-being to the lives of our people by identifying green development as an important principle in its economic and social development planning. Achieve sustainable development goals that will contribute to maintaining national economic growth, improving environmental quality and reducing poverty.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra added that in order to achieve its mission to ensure a clean and green city, the Ministry of Environment has set out a vision with four main pillars: institutional modernization, biodiversity conservation and protection of natural resources. Protect the environment and sustainable development, including the policy of safe villages and communes.
Regarding environmental protection, the Ministry of Environment has taken a number of measures to prevent environmental pollution, focusing on soil, water and air quality. Which is an important indicator in awarding the ASEAN Urban Environmental Sustainability Award and the ASEAN Urban Environmental Sustainability Certificate.
He said that in 2011, the ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting decided to expand the certification of ASEAN Environmental Sustainability Cities for large cities and small cities according to the categories of indicators: cities with fresh air, cities with clean water and cities. There is clean land.
It should be reminded that for Cambodia, Phnom Penh received the ASEAN Urban Environmental Sustainability Award in 2008 and 2011, Battambang received in 2013, Kep received in 2017 and Sihanoukville received in 2021 recently.
Meanwhile, Siem Reap received the water certification in 2013, Pursat received the water certification in 2017 and for 2021. Phnom Penh has been certified with clean water, Sen Monorom has been certified with clean land and Kep has been certified with fresh air, which is the pride of our nation.
