Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and Singapore International Foundation Launch Mental Health Care Strengthening Project
Over the next two years, Singapore International Volunteers (SIVs), a specialist physician who includes a multidisciplinary team of mental health professionals from the Singapore Institute of Mental Health, will work directly with Cambodian doctors. 50 people to share knowledge, skills and best practices in this field.
Of these Cambodian doctors, 12 will be selected to participate in further training to qualify as Master Trainers. These doctors will join Singapore International Volunteers (SIVs) to teach other doctors.
This training model will empower Cambodians and be able to make a lasting and sustainable impact on the wider community. At least 30,000 people in Cambodia are expected to benefit from the project being completed by 2024.
Most of the Cambodian trainees will be psychiatrists and emergency physicians, as well as psychiatrists, nurses, social workers and general practitioners. This training will focus on how to manage psychiatric emergencies and treat patients with emotional distress and anxiety.
Participants will attend a number of online seminars and study tours to Singapore when travel is permitted. Led by SIV Volunteers, participants will also jointly develop a training framework and a national management protocol for psychiatric emergencies.
Two public meetings will also be held to raise awareness and understanding of mental health issues. This will reduce stigma and enable people to seek help when they need it.
The Mental Health Services Strengthening Project is the third SIF mental health care initiative in Cambodia. The project follows the success of a previous capacity building project in Phnom Penh when SIVs, a specialist doctors, trained Cambodian healthcare professionals in the field of child mental health (2002-2004). ) And counseling for children at risk (2007).
The Mental Health Services Strengthening Project in Phnom Penh also commemorates another great event, the 20-year friendship between the SIF Foundation and Cambodia, to improve lives and build lasting friendships between people. Singapore and the people of Cambodia.
At the global level, the project contributes to the third goal (health and well-being) and the seventh goal (Global Partnership for Sustainable Development) of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.
