German support comes as Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Cambodian Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, pays an official visit to the Federal Republic of Germany on February 23, 2022. This is the first visit in 25 years since the last exchange visit in January 1997 to promote better friendly relations and expand cooperation in all fields between the two countries.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs on Myanmar, Cambodia and Germany have agreed on the need to implement a five-point unanimous agreement to help the country return to normalcy.
The German Foreign Minister also expressed Germany's willingness to participate in providing humanitarian assistance to the people of Myanmar.
Mr. Prak Sokhon will pay a visit to Myanmar in the second week of March in connection with the mission to meet with stakeholders and humanitarian assistance. He was appointed Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair in 2022, when Cambodia will chair ASEAN. The visit of the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair follows the opening visit of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen in January 2022.
According to Mr. Prak Sokhon, the agenda of his upcoming visit is in line with the five points of the consensus set out at the ASEAN Summit in April last year, including a meeting with Stakeholders.
During his visit in the middle of next month, he plans to meet with Min Aung Lan, Myanmar Foreign Minister and other dignitaries, which the Nay Pyi Taw administration will facilitate.
