After reviewing and discussing all the above documents in detail, the NEC has revised and agreed on the content for use and dissemination in the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022. Anlong Veng Peace Center Organizes Student Study Tour on "Peace and Human Rights"
(Oddar Meanchey): The Anlong Veng Peace Center of the Documentation Center of Cambodia on February 23, 2022 organized a study tour on "Peace and Human Rights" in Anlong Veng District.
The study tour starts at 2:00 pm with the aim of "raising awareness of the history of Democratic Kampuchea and the history in the Anlong Veng community" with 16 young people (11 females and 5 males) from Trapeang Prasat district, 5 And 11 people from Anlong Veng district came to participate.
The study tour starts from the headquarters of the Anlong Veng Peace Center, next to the O'Chik Bridge, towards the former Ta Mok Central House on Dangrek Mountain, now the Anlong Veng Peace Center.
The truck carrying the group of youths traveled slowly along the Dangrek mountain range, with many small and large plants growing on either side of the road. After that, the youth and the Anlong Veng Peace Center team arrived at the Anlong Veng Peace Center.
In the office of the Anlong Veng Peace Center, there is an exhibition of pictures related to the visit of the Chinese delegation to Cambodia and the pictures of the last time the Khmer Rouge forces integrated into Anlong Veng district in 1998. In addition to these pictures, there are many other books on display by the Anlong Veng Peace Center team for visitors to view and read.
The guide began to give a detailed presentation to the youth group about the Anlong Veng Peace Center, or Ta Mok's former central house, which was built in 1995. This house was designated as a meeting place for important Khmer Rouge leaders such as Pol Pot, Khieu Samphan, Nuon Chea, and other Khmer Rouge brigade commanders.
Today, the Anlong Veng Peace Center, or former Ta Mok Central House, is a library and information center for national and international guests, as well as a study office for those who wish to do research both inside and outside the country.
Soon, the youth group traveled to Ta Mok Museum. Upon arrival, the youth and the Anlong Veng Peace Center team visited the paintings, photographs, and scenery around the Ta Mok House Museum for the purpose of exploring the history of the Khmer Rouge.
Before the study tour was over, the youth group also expressed their opinions and interests.
Holinda, a 17-year-old student from Hun Sen Trapeang Tao High School, said: “I am very happy to be part of this study tour. It was a visit that gave me and other young people a great deal of insight into the history of Democratic Kampuchea. "The important thing is that I can come to this location in Anlong Veng district and listen to the origins and history of each historical site."
The visit ended at 5 pm on the same day and a group photo was taken in front of the Ta Mok Museum as a souvenir. Ministry of Tourism Introduces New Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) Procedures for New Supermarkets for Supermarkets, Small Markets, Public Markets and Disorderly Markets
