(Oddar Meanchey): On the morning of February 23, 2022, the office of Anlong Veng Peace Center welcomed 16 students (5 boys and 11 girls) from Hun Sen Trapeang Tao High School and Hun Sen Trapeang Prasat High School to participate in the forum. Learn about "History of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979)".
This forum is designed to raise awareness of the history of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979) and key theories related to peace.
The young people of the two high schools welcomed each other with friendliness and understanding, even though the schools of the two groups of students were far apart.
During the meeting, the working group of Anlong Veng Peace Center paid special attention to the implementation of welfare measures to prevent and avoid the new development of Omikrong through the implementation of the Ministry's three-pronged and three-pronged measures. Health.
The Anlong Veng Peace Center team measured the temperature, sprayed alcohol, cleaned the students' hands, kept the gaps and opened the windows for adequate ventilation.
After completing the survey, there was a presentation on the history of Democratic Kampuchea and a collaborative lecture to find out the main chapters in the book "History of Democratic Kampuchea" and the definition of genocide by Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of the Peace Center Anlong Veng.
Images of these genocides deliberately portrayed hatred and prejudice, which led to the almost complete destruction of ethnic groups, races, or other religious groups, with a tendency to paint. The intent of these atrocities seems to reflect and exhort students to learn from the experiences of their society and to return to unity and to live in harmony with the diversity of humanity in society.
Behind the classroom forum, all 16 students, or one hundred percent, have increased their knowledge and understanding that preventing genocide in any way is really important for individuals, communities and society through practical examination. On each student's survey paper.
