President Putin's speech to the Russian people, both in Russia and in Ukraine, before launching an attack on Ukraine
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Before launching a military operation against Ukraine on February 24, 2022, President Putin made a key statement on February 22, 2022 to the Russian people in Russia. And in Ukraine, with the full text as follows:
Dear Russian people!
The topic of my speech was the events in Ukraine and why it is important for us and for Russia. Of course, my appeal must also be sent to our compatriots in Ukraine.
The situation in Donbas has worsened again. And today I speak directly to you, not only to evaluate what is happening, but also to tell you about the decisions that have been made about the next possible steps in this direction.
Let me reiterate that Ukraine is for us not only a neighbor, it is an important part of our own historical, cultural and spiritual space. They are our comrades, our relatives, among them are not only colleagues, friends, old colleagues, but also relatives, they are the ones who continue with us with love and resin blood together. .
For a long time the inhabitants of the historical territories of southwestern Russia called themselves Russian and Orthodox. So it was not until the 17th century, when parts of these territories were united with the Russian state, and then.
For us, in principle, we all know about this, we are talking about a well-known fact. At the same time, in order to understand what is happening today, to explain the reasons for Russia's actions and the goals we have set for ourselves, it is necessary to include the history of the issue.
Then, after the Great Patriotic War, Stalin annexed Ukraine into the Soviet Union and transferred to Ukraine some territories formerly belonging to Poland, Romania and Hungary. At the same time, in return, Stalin offered Poland part of German territory in 1954, Khrushchev for some reason withdrew Crimea from Russia and also ceded it to Ukraine. In fact, this is how the territory of the Soviet Union, Ukraine, was formed.
But now I want to emphasize, especially in the early days of the Soviet Union. I think this is very important for us.
Moreover, we know the position and words of US leaders on actions in eastern Ukraine, do not rule out the possibility of Ukraine joining NATO if the country can meet the conditions of the North Atlantic Alliance and eliminate corruption in Country.
They talked, made verbal assurances, and everything was empty. We then assured that the accession of Central and Eastern European countries to NATO would improve relations with Moscow, reducing concerns about the serious historical heritage of these countries. Even create a belt of friendly countries to Russia.
Russia fulfilled all its obligations, including the withdrawal of troops from Germany and from Central and Eastern European countries, and thus contributed greatly to overcoming the legacy of the Cold War. We have repeatedly proposed various cooperation options, including the Russian-NATO Council and the OSCE.
The only answer he has is not because of our political regime, it is not about anything else, they just do not need a big independent country like Russia. Here are the answers to all the questions. This is the origin of traditional US policy toward Russia. So attitude to all our proposals in the field of security.
As a result, its military infrastructure allies came to the Russian border. This has become one of the main causes of the European security crisis, which has the most negative impact on the entire international communication system and leads to mistrust.
The situation continues to deteriorate, even in the strategic sphere. Therefore, in Romania and Poland, as part of the US project to develop a global missile defense system, anti-missile sites are being deployed. It is well known that the missiles located here can be used for Tomahawk intercontinental ballistic missiles - attack systems.
And of course, they also intend to continue to follow the famous saying, "Dogs, but the rules continue." I will immediately say that we do not agree with this and put a disagreement. Russia, meanwhile, has always advocated and believed that the most difficult issues must be resolved through political and diplomatic means at the negotiating table.
In addition, we are made aware that only members of the North Atlantic Alliance can have legal security.
Last December, we presented to our Western partners a draft treaty between the Russian Federation and the United States on security guarantees, as well as a draft agreement on security measures by the Russian Federation and NATO member states.
The United States and NATO have many words to say. There are also valid opinions, but all these trivial matters are just an attempt to close the issue and turn the discussion aside.
These basic requests of ours are ignored. I would like to reiterate to the Western partners that the formula has been learned that each country is free to choose the means to ensure its security and to enter into any military alliance, that is, their position has not changed. Similar statements have been made about NATO's "open" policy.
I want to be honest, in the current situation, our proposal for equal dialogue on fundamental issues is really unresponsive by the United States and NATO when the level of threat to our country That is growing rapidly. Russia has every right to take retaliatory measures to ensure its security, that is what we will do.
In fact, not a single day has passed since the shelling of a Donbass residence. Large armies were formed, consisting of drones attacking heavy equipment, rockets, artillery and rockets. The killing of civilians, the official closure of the mockery of everyone, including children, women, the elderly, has not stopped. As we say, it has no end.
How long can this tragedy continue? How long can you endure this? Russia has made every effort to defend the territorial integrity of Ukraine and throughout the year has persevered and endured the implementation of UN Security Council Resolution 2202 of 17 February 2015, in which Consolidated Minsk measures dated 12 February 2015 to resolve the situation in Donbas.
Everything is useless. The president and deputies have changed, but the zealous nationalist nature of the ruling regime in Kiev itself has not. It was the complete result of the 2014 coup and those who then followed the path of violence, bloodshed and lawlessness and did not know any other solution to the Donbass problem except the military.
I urge the Federal Council (Parliament of the Russian Federation) to support this decision and then ratify the Treaty of Amity and Mutual Assistance with these two republics. Both documents will be prepared and signed in the near future.
And from those in power in Kiev, we demand an immediate end to hostilities. Otherwise, all responsibility for the continuation of the possible bloodshed will fall entirely on the regime of Ukraine.
Announcing the decision made today, I have confidence in the support of the Russian people, all the patriotic forces of the country.
