(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, High Representative Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, on February 24, 2022, presided over the celebration of the 23rd Anniversary of National Day. Understand the mine on February 24 in Preah Vihear province.
This day is to continue to promote education on the dangers of landmines, cluster munitions and explosive remnants of war in all its forms, which Cambodia has been celebrating every year since 1999. The gathering is to express condolences and sympathy. And sadness at the loss of life, disability, and family breakdown caused by landmines and explosive remnants of war in Cambodia, as well as around the world.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch also thanked the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration and authorities at all levels for their excellent cooperation in organizing this event and confirmed that this is the first time. The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to select Preah Vihear Province for the National Day, which was first organized in 2016.
At the same time, the Senior Minister highlighted the glorious historical achievements for the demining work for nearly 30 years, and the Royal Government of Cambodia continues to work tirelessly and with great ambition to set a clear vision and goal. A Cambodia Without Mines 2025 ”and there is a strong hope that Cambodia will be able to do so with high commitment and joint commitment.
He added that despite efforts to clear mines and munitions, the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war remain constant, and the contribution of education activities to reduce mine risk, cluster munitions and Explosive remnants of war are a necessary task and play an important role in reducing the hazards and adverse effects of these explosives in communities.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch also called on the people to unite to end the tragedy of landmines, cluster munitions and war remnants from Cambodia and the world.
