Indonesia calls for talks but refuses to impose sanctions on Russia
JAKARTA: Indonesia on Thursday called for talks and a diplomatic solution after Russia decided to launch an attack on Ukraine, which the West considers an act of aggression. This is according to the release by CNA on Thursday, February 24, 2022.
"Indonesia is deeply concerned about the conflict situation in Ukraine, which could pose a threat to population security and stability in the region," an Indonesian Foreign Ministry spokesman told a news conference. "We urge all parties concerned to prioritize negotiations and diplomacy to end the conflict as well as find a peaceful solution."
Indonesia has told its citizens in Ukraine to gather at the Indonesian embassy to prepare for evacuation if necessary. But according to the spokesman, Jakarta will not impose sanctions on Russia.
The Prime Minister of Malaysia led a delegation to meet the King of Cambodia at the Royal Palace
(Phnom Penh): During his official visit to Cambodia on the evening of February 24, 2022, the Prime Minister of Malaysia, Ishmael Sabribin Jacob, led a high-level delegation to meet with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia. Royal Palace.
The Prime Minister of Malaysia led a high-level delegation to Cambodia on the afternoon of February 23, 2022 for a two-day official visit at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
During the visit, he laid a wreath at the Independence Monument and at the shrine of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the "King of Cambodia", the former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. He also held bilateral talks with Samdech Techo Hun Sen and paid a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia.
The Malaysian Prime Minister's visit is to strengthen and expand bilateral relations and cooperation, as well as exchange visits on regional and global issues. During the visit, Cambodia and Malaysia also issued 14 more statements. The Ministry of Tourism held the second executive working group meeting to evaluate and manage the safe tourism destinations in Siem Reap.
The second meeting was held to assess and manage the safe tourism destination of Siem Reap, which is a priority tourist destination of Cambodia, as the new virus Omikrong is making the situation of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia is entering a new stage. There needs to be a thorough assessment of Cambodia's safe tourism destinations, especially Siem Reap.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Thong Khon stated that the identification of areas or destinations for safe tourism must be based on four achievement indicators, including: First: the rate of vaccination aimed at building community immunity; Second: the rate of Kovid patients. 19- Medium and severe and morbidity and mortality of Kovid-19 patients. Third: Ability to respond and treat and manage potential risks from new strains of the virus.
On behalf of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Samdech Heng Samrin expressed his pleasure and warm welcome to the presence of the Prime Minister of Malaysia and the delegation in Cambodia. Samdech considered that the current visit will further contribute to the strengthening of good relations, friendship and good cooperation between the two nations, which has existed for more than 60 years.
In addition to thanking Malaysia for its support to Cambodia in its pursuit of peace and development, the National Assembly President requested the Malaysian side to further promote investment, trade and tourism from Malaysia to Cambodia. At the same time, Samdech requested the Prime Minister of Malaysia to examine the possibility of continuing to help train human resources for Cambodian civil servants and students in order to contribute to the development of the country.
Mr. Ismail Elbribin Jacob informed Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin about the results of this morning's working meeting with the Prime Minister on strengthening cooperation between the two countries in the fields of economy, trade and technology.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin emphasized that the Cambodian and Malaysian legislatures have also cooperated a lot through mutual support in regional and global inter-parliamentary forums such as AIPA and IPU.
Mr. Ishmael Sabribin Jacob thanked the National Assembly President for promoting cooperation between the two parliaments through the Cambodia-Malaysia Parliamentary Friendship Group. At the end, the Prime Minister invited the President of the National Assembly to lead a high-level delegation of the National Assembly to visit Malaysia at any convenient time. Spokesman for the General Commission: 737 more vehicles were inspected and fined on February 24, 2022
