Rice Federation: Malaysia is the largest country in ASEAN that buys Cambodian rice, in 2021 bought more than 40,000 tons for 32 million dollars
According to the Rice Federation of Cambodia, in 2021, Cambodia exported 46,181 tons of fragrant rice to the Malaysian market, valued at approximately US $ 32.07 million. Exports are third, followed by China and France.
"In Malaysia, most older people have known the reputation of Cambodian fragrant rice since the pre-war period, when Cambodia used to export it there," said Lon Yeng, secretary general of the Cambodian Rice Federation. At that time, Cambodian fragrant rice, "Somali" rice, which is now packaged under the name "Somali" is still popular in the Malaysian market.
