(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Malaysia, Ishmael Sabribin Jacob, on February 24, 2022, announced his intention to help Cambodia in establishing a halal food industry in Cambodia.
This statement was made at a joint press conference after the meeting between the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Malaysia at the Peace Palace on February 24, 2022.
"I am pleased to hear that developments in the halal industry are encouraging," he said. "Malaysia is ready to help Cambodia build an ecosystem of halal food."
He said that Malaysia has many experts in the field of halal industry, and Malaysia welcomes more Cambodian companies to Malaysia to gain skills and knowledge to create a halal industry.
On that occasion, the Prime Minister of Malaysia also expressed his desire to cooperate with Cambodia to support efforts to increase youth relations in both countries, especially in the field of entrepreneurship.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia established the Committee on Product Review of Cambodia on November 4, 2016, with the Chairman of the Committee on Product Review of Cambodia as the Minister of Commerce and the Vice-Chairman and members representing ministries and institutions. Involved in martial arts, and especially representatives of the elite leadership of the Islamic community of Cambodia.
The Committee for the Inspection of Halal Products of Cambodia has a halal product specialization team as a technical and Islamic assistant on halal work to inspect the technical standards and monitor the provision of services, production or packaging of Cambodian halal products and to certify the technical standards of Cambodian halal products with approval. From the Minister of Commerce.
It should be noted that the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Malaysia in 2021 was 501 million US dollars, an increase of 13% compared to 2020.
