Ministry of Justice and WCS Hold First Training on Wildlife Crimes for Cambodian Prosecutors and Judges
(Phnom Penh): WCS and the Department of Research, Dissemination and Legal Training in the Civil Sector of the Ministry of Justice have organized a training course on "International Wildlife Trafficking Skills for Cambodian Prosecutors and Judges".
The training was held in Phnom Penh from 21 to 25 February 2022 under the chairmanship of Ms. Khieu Sophany, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Justice and Dr. Ken Serey Ratha, Director of WCS Cambodia.
The training is divided into two sessions, each lasting two and a half days, and prosecutors and judges from 25 provinces, a total of 50 participants in both courses.
This is the first training course organized for prosecutors and judges in the Kingdom of Cambodia in order to build the capacity of prosecutors and judges to have more basic knowledge about wildlife trafficking and to strengthen their skills in prosecuting wildlife trafficking crimes. Effective.
The course is funded by the US Department of State's Anti-Drug and International Law Enforcement Agency.
"International wildlife trafficking is one of the major threats to biodiversity conservation," said Dr Ken Serey Ratha.
