Ministry of Social Affairs Holds Sub-National Consultation Workshop on Gathering Entities on Draft Law on Child Protection of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has organized a two-day consultation workshop to collect input on the draft law on child protection of the Kingdom of Cambodia online, on February 24-25. 2022.
The workshop was attended by stakeholders from eight provinces: Kampong Speu, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampot, Kep, Takeo, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng, and all relevant partner organizations with technical and financial support from the United States Agency for International Development (USAID). International Development (USAID) through UNICEF and Plan International for the drafting of the Child Protection Law, as well as our two-day workshop.
In the past, we have held several consultative workshops at the national and sub-national levels to review and provide input on the content and contents of the draft law, with some gradual revisions. And by both advisors. The two-day consultation workshop is a continuation of the review and comment on the content of the draft law on child protection.
