Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey Requests Private Security Agencies in Boreys and Condos to Cooperate in Providing Information to Authorities in Suspected Crime at Their Locations
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the National Police General Commission, on the morning of February 24, 2022, requested all private security agencies, especially those guarding Borey and condominium destinations, to cooperate in providing information. Inform the authorities in case of suspicion that their location has a crime.
During the opening ceremony of the 33rd private security agency training course, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey emphasized that recently, the crimes that often occur in the city and condominiums are drug offenses and cases of illegal detention. Or kidnapping, etc. Therefore, in case of suspicion that these crimes have occurred, it must be reported to the authorities immediately and the authorities will keep it a secret.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said, "I would like to ask the private security agencies in the Boreys and condominiums to report the crimes in their Boreys, especially the drug crimes that have been cracked down on in the past. That. "We cooperate in case of suspicion to report to the authorities so that we can use repressive measures in a timely manner."
The director of the department stressed that the private security sector is inextricably linked. The private security sector must have high quality and benefits for the protection of security, safety and public order, so all private security agencies must have the capacity to understand and Have a clear profession as a full-fledged private security agent.
Therefore, the General Commission of the National Police, which has the Private Security Management Department as its staff, organized this refresher course for the main purpose of understanding the duties and obligations of the private security sector on maintaining security, order and strengthening the capacity of private security agencies. Improved to be more effective in protecting social security.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey sincerely commended and encouraged all private security agencies who have taken care to protect the security, safety, order, property, life of the people and participated in disseminating and implementing village policy. Safe communes, especially private security agencies, have joined the blockade of Phnom Penh to prevent Kovid 19 from causing major targets in the past.
He added that this is the 33rd time that the Department of Private Security Management has organized a training course for private security agents for private security agencies to serve and not serve.
In this refresher course, participants will gain knowledge on the main topics that are encountered and faced on a daily basis in the performance of work, such as: the role and responsibilities of private security agencies, how to protect the goals of the road traffic law. Land How to provide assistance and cooperate with the authorities, understanding of the Criminal Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure, measures to prevent fire and evacuation from fire and cooperation to protect the scene.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey strongly hopes that all participants will pay attention to listen to Veal Khmin explain and apply this knowledge to fulfill their role in a positive way to effectively protect the public and private interests. And our entire society.
