(Phnom Penh): The mother and the victim jointly thumbprinted a complaint to Judge Song Bonnarith to the Ministry of Justice because the judge decided to release the perpetrator who raped the victim.
Pursuant to the complaint dated 22 February 2022, Ms. Chan Srey Mom, the mother and daughter of the victim, filed a complaint for justice to Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, against Mr. Song Bunnarith, Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. And Chea Srey Mom, a clerk at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, who was unfair to them.
The decision to file a complaint for justice now comes after Phnom Penh Municipal Court Investigating Judge Song Bunnarith issued an order placing Chea Socheat alias Sokhom under judicial supervision. Provisional detention) on the afternoon of February 22, 2022.
The victim stated that the accused, Chea Socheat alias Sokhom, 67, a retired military medical officer, raped the 16-year-old girl in January 2020 in Prey Khla village, commune. The boy is from Bati district, Takeo province.
Please be informed that the accused Chea Socheat alias Sokhom was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on February 19, 2022 in connection with the above crimes, according to the victim's complaint. .
Deputy Prosecutor Moth Dara, representing the prosecution, opened an investigation and decided to charge the perpetrators of rape committed during January 2020 at Prey Khla village, Komara Chea commune, Bati district, Takeo province, according to Article 239 of the Code. Criminal and will send the case to Mr. Song Bonnarith, the investigating judge to proceed with the procedure.
Regarding the release of Chea Socheat alias Sokhom, Deputy Prosecutor Plang Sophal, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, told reporters that he had not yet received any information on the appeal from the prosecution. On the decision of the investigating judge yet.
