Please be informed that the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on February 22, 2022 issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia from February 23 to March 1, 2022.
The Ministry of Water Resources has stated that during the week of the notification, the Kingdom of Cambodia will be affected by high to moderate pressure from China (China) to moderate to weak. Such a situation will make the coastal areas:
* Minimum temperature is 21-23 ° C * Maximum temperature is 26-32 ° C * There may be light rain. Minister: Ministry of Commerce pays high attention to the rice sector, seeks all means to help make it more competitive
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that the Ministry of Commerce always pays high attention to the rice sector, trying to find all ways to help this sector to be more competitive.
The Minister made the remarks while presiding over the 2021 Annual Review Ceremony and the 2022 Action Plan of the Cambodian Rice Federation on the afternoon of February 23, 2022.
The Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation to all the leaders and members of the Cambodian Rice Federation who have worked hard to implement and achieve the work in the past year and set goals for the coming year.
The Minister said that the Cambodian Rice Federation has played an important role in the rice sector in Cambodia and has worked closely with the Ministry of Commerce, especially Green Trade of the Ministry of Commerce and has contributed significantly to stabilizing rice prices. Domestic markets, especially in the region, have been closed in the past 19 years and have contributed to the export facilitation movement.
In fact, in 2020 and 2021, the Ministry organized an in-depth and comprehensive study on the cost of production to rice export to the market under the cooperation and financial assistance of the Cambodian Agricultural Chain Program by Australia (CAVAC). ) This study will be a necessary basis for developing strategies and incentive plans for making our Cambodian rice sector more competitive.
The minister said efforts to open up markets for rice and processed products sourced from rice have been active through the inclusion of these items in the list of goods, free trade agreements and bilateral negotiations. With countries, especially China, which is a growing market for Cambodian rice exports, covering up to 50% of total exports in 2021 and in 2022 is likely to continue to increase.
This increase is due to the high commitment from the Chinese side through the signing of the Sixth Memorandum of Understanding in the amount of 400,000 tons, which the Minister of Commerce himself received permission from the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. Of Cambodia authorized to sign in November 2021 and effective from January 2022 onwards.
The MoU will pave the way for Cambodia's rice exports to run smoothly. We have now observed that rice exports to China in January 2022 will account for more than 50% of total rice exports. .
The Minister stressed that the Ministry of Commerce not only considers the export of one-sided rice, but also strives to help smallholder farmers to be better prepared, especially to promote agricultural contracts between farmers. Small-scale mills that are being implemented through AIMs and are also financially supported by the Royal Government and IFAD.
The Minister submitted some recommendations to the Rice Federation of Cambodia as a basis for better planning and implementation of its action plan as follows:
1: Continue to strengthen internal unity, adhere to the statutes, rules, regulations and ethics well among all members of the federation to be a complementary force on the supply of exports and solve challenges Various.
2: Consider arranging for the consolidation of export consortiums for large markets with high volume demand, which was previously supported by the Ministry of Commerce and approved by Samdech. Prime Minister Techo through a letter from the Ministry of Economy and Finance in mid-2019 before the election of the new Board of Directors of the third mandate of the Cambodian Rice Federation.
3: Continue to work with international partner organizations and relevant institutions to develop collective brands, geographical marks and common brands on various types of rice that respond to the situation of market development, which the Ministry of Commerce is ready to Provide cooperation on this work.
4: Continue to work closely with Green Trade of the Ministry of Commerce to prevent inflation in rice prices to ensure supply and food security to the people.
5: Continue to actively cooperate with the General Department of Trade Promotion to bring the types of rice and rice products with branded and clearly registered existing and appearing in the future to be displayed. Dominance and cooking show as done at the World Expo in Dubai, United Arab Emirates.
6. Discuss with associations or federations of countries in the ASEAN region to consider and lead to the establishment of an ASEAN Rice Federation that can easily communicate and find markets together.
