Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, pointed out that due to the difficult situation related to Kovid 19 disease in 2021, the plan to expand the electricity supply to the villages that do not have electricity has been delayed or delayed.
According to the report of the Electricity Authority, as of the end of 2021, the border of licenses issued by distribution license holders to invest and develop the public and private electricity distribution network in 14,151 villages equal to 99. .88% of the total number of villages in the country.
According to the Electricity Authority, of the 13,818 villages that have already built the network, 13,705 villages receive sources from the national network, 111 villages receive sources from neighboring countries, and 2 villages receive sources from Wi-Fi. Small. "Of the 350 villages that do not yet have access to electricity, most are located in islands, floodplains during the rainy season, no roads, floating areas, remote areas with scattered populations."
According to the President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, from 2020 to 2021, the number of power outages and the quality of electricity in some areas have been significantly reduced, but some areas still continue. There are some areas that are new challenges, so stability and quality issues remain challenges for the Electricity Authority of Cambodia to address and address.
In addition, Mr. Yim Piseth stated that some other challenges still exist, such as debt, purchase of electricity, delays in expanding supply to areas without electricity, recording information on power outages. Fully implemented.
Mr. Yim Viseth stated that the Electricity Authority of Cambodia has two main tasks to be implemented, including: the development of electricity supply and the second: the improvement of electricity services to consumers.
He said that the goal of the development of electricity supply in Cambodia is to consolidate the integrated power sources and then divide and develop the power source into the system in order to ensure that Cambodia has more electricity sources. According to the growth of demand.
In addition, Mr. Yim Piseth stated that some other challenges still exist, such as debt, purchase of electricity, delays in expanding supply to areas without electricity, recording information on power outages. Fully applied, etc.
The President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia added that to achieve this vision, the Ministry of Mines and Energy has identified three active plans to implement:
First, to promote investment, development, increase production capacity, transmission and distribution of electricity to consumers in accordance with the plan.
Second, to improve the provision of electricity services to consumers, making sure that the electricity supply is adequate, sustainable, reliable, high quality and affordable.
Third, to strengthen the management mechanism for the development and provision of electricity services more effectively, focusing on strengthening institutional mechanisms, investment mechanisms, business mechanisms, environmental mechanisms and cooperation with regional and international partners. And expand economic and trade cooperation between the two countries
