General knowledge: Which country has the most troops?
In addition to the more than 2 million active-duty soldiers, China also has more than half a million reservists and half a million conscripts.
The Chinese People's Liberation Army is divided into five categories: the Army, the Navy, the Air Force, the Rocket Army (prior to 2016, originally known as the Artillery Army) and the Strategic Aid Army. The Chinese People's Liberation Army is also divided into five regions: the Western Zone, the Eastern Zone, the Northern Zone, the Southern Zone and the Central Zone.
After China is India with 1.39 million active troops, equivalent to 1.34 million US troops. North Korea has 1.28 million troops.
