(Phnom Penh): Investigating Judge Song Bonnarith of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has reportedly decided to release one of the accused in connection with a rape case. The release took place on the afternoon of February 22, 2022 yesterday.
Mr. Song Bunnarith decided to place the accused Chea Socheat alias Sokhom, 67 years old, under judicial supervision (not in pretrial detention) after Deputy Prosecutor Mot Dara, representing the prosecution, opened an investigation and decided Charged with the perpetrator of rape committed during January 2020 in Prey Khla village, Komarachea commune, Bati district, Takeo province, according to Article 239 of the Penal Code.
Regarding the release of the accused, Chea Socheat alias Sokhom, Deputy Prosecutor Plong Sophal, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, told reporters that he had not yet received information on the appeal from the prosecution. The matter on the decision of the investigating judge is still under investigation.
