Please read the announcement of Electricite du Cambodge below: This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed and discussed with the Prime Minister of Malaysia at the Peace Palace.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, February 24, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, officially welcomed the visit of Mr. Ishmael Sabribin Jacob, Prime Minister of Malaysia, and discussed the work.
The reception and discussion will be held at the Peace Palace. After the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Malaysia will hold a joint press conference.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Dato 'Ismail Sabribin Jacobs will discuss bilateral relations and cooperation, including trade and investment, socio-economic, defense and security, and Socio-economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis. The two Prime Ministers will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern.
On January 25, 2022, Mr. Dato 's Ishmael Bin Jacob had a video conference with Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
It should be noted that Mr. Ishmael Sabribin Jacob arrived in Cambodia on the afternoon of February 23, 2022 to pay his first two-day visit to Cambodia on February 23 and 24. The visit was made at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to strengthen bilateral relations and cooperation, as well as exchange views on regional and international issues.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during his visit to Cambodia, the Malaysian Prime Minister will pay a courtesy call on His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, at the Royal Palace. Courtesy to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
The Prime Minister of Malaysia will also lay a wreath at the Independence Monument and at the shrine of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the "King of Cambodia", the former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Please note that Cambodia and Malaysia established diplomatic relations on August 31, 1957. The two countries attach great importance to strengthening good relations and cooperation with each other. In order to strengthen good relations and cooperation with each other, the senior leaders of the two countries regularly exchange visits with each other.
The size of investment and trade between Cambodia and Malaysia is also remarkably large. The report shows that the trade volume between the two countries in 2021 reached more than 500 million US dollars. The main goods that Cambodia imports from Malaysia are: fuel, tubes and hoses, brake pads and spare parts, tires, woven fabrics, beverages and processed foods from flour.
In particular, the main goods that Cambodia exports to Malaysia include: clothing, grain, electric motors, rice, nuts and brown meat. Malaysia has always been the number one exporter of ASEAN rice from Cambodia. In the first 11 months of 2021, Malaysia imported more than 40,000 tons of rice from Cambodia.
According to the report, from 2014 to 2021, Malaysian investment in Cambodia amounted to more than 14 million US dollars.
Cambodia and Malaysia also have cooperation in many other areas, such as security and defense, education, culture and health.
