On the occasion of closing the meeting to review the results of the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed all civil servants to reduce unnecessary expenses because the Royal Government is lacking funds while fighting against Kovid 19. .
At this point, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, to manage all expenditures very strictly at this stage, while the Royal Government needs more funds to fight Kovid 19 in Now.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to ask you to save money, where to spend, where to spend, where not to spend, stop spending or do not spend or delay spending to ensure To have a balance between head out and head in, not to lose too much balance, making it difficult for us to save money.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister continued that if the construction plan can be postponed, it must be postponed temporarily, and the sub-national level as well, not just submit a request to the Minister, so the Minister was reluctant to send it. Decided by the Prime Minister.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "Some plans, if delayed, will be postponed." I urge the Minister of Economy and Finance to strictly manage this point, because I can not run out of reserves for the fight and just spend. "I would like to ask all of you here not to make a request, and those below should not raise their hand to the reluctant minister and sign to the Prime Minister to be sent to the Minister of Economy."
At the same time, Samdech Techo also expressed his frustration with a unit that he did not name, by submitting a request to the Royal Government to ask for funds to buy two cars to go to the base, but the request was rejected on the grounds that The Royal Government needs more money to spend on necessary work than to buy these two cars.
The head of the Royal Government reminded that in the absence of Kovid 19, the state revenue came in three parts, two percent for work expenses and the remaining one part for savings, but at this stage it is more expensive than before.
Although the Royal Government has increased the amount of expenditure required by various state institutions to reduce spending, but Samdech clearly stated that the Royal Government has not lacked the budget to pay the salaries of civil servants, that is, still open. Normally, it is open twice a month. In addition, payroll for retired officers continues to be paid. In addition, financial support for the poor in the Kovid stage continues to be normal.
In addition, the Royal Government continues to feed 19 Kovid patients who are being treated in hospitals and those in the Chattalysak Center.
This guideline was issued on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2021 and raise the work direction for 2022 of the Ministry of Interior on the evening of February 23, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order for Cambodia to maintain peace both now and in the future, on behalf of the Royal Government, Samdech would like to provide the following guidelines:
First, to continue to work together to safeguard peace, political stability, independence, territorial integrity, national sovereignty, protection of the King, and protection of the constitutional monarchy. And strengthening the rule of law in accordance with the Constitution and the laws in force.
Fourth, the competent forces must increase traffic law education measures for the people, increase traffic signs and order on the streets in cities and towns to reduce traffic accidents and ensure the safety of traffic.
Sixth, we must continue to increase immigration control, prevent illegal immigration, terrorism, and cross-border crime of all kinds, and continue to strengthen mechanisms to control the presence of illegal aliens in countries that have committed crimes in order to take legal action. And legal documents of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Ninth: We must continue to work together to implement the Royal Government's measures to fight Kovid-19 by continuing to promote the Kovid-19 vaccination, which is a key measure linked to the consistent implementation of the "3 3" measures. Protect "regularly" and adhere to the lifestyle and work with Kovid-19 in a new normal path.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also encouraged the Royal Government to work at the grassroots level to increase support activities at their respective localities and to participate in solving challenges and promote local development for the betterment of people's lives. Shout up.
Samdech praised and highly appreciated the leadership of the Ministry of Interior, the National Police Force, civil administration officials, prison officials and sub-national administrations who have worked hard to achieve proud achievements in 2021. Samdech is optimistic about the achievements and commitment of the Ministry of Interior to achieve the work direction in 2022.
