China accuses US of fueling tensions, fears over Ukraine crisis
BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Wednesday directly accused the United States of escalating tensions and fears over the crisis in Ukraine. The allegations come just hours after Washington announced sanctions against Moscow and given Ukraine more weapons to counter Russia. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday evening, February 23, 2022.
Japanese government provides $ 1.8 million grant to two demining organizations in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has provided a grant of US $ 1,799,166 to two demining organizations, a grant for a Japanese NGO project.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan and a representative of the Japan Mine Action Organization at the Embassy of Japan on the afternoon of February 23, 2022.
First: $ 900,787 for a project to support infrastructure reconstruction with cluster munitions clearance in Stung Treng Province, known as RSCS Project (Year 2) Recipient Unit: Japan Mine Action Organization (JMAS) .
Under this project, JMAS will clear 470 hectares of cluster munitions and transfer effective and safe methods of cluster munitions clearance to the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC). The project will also provide mine risk education to local people. In addition, agricultural experts will train farmers on agricultural management and technology.
At the same time, the Japanese ambassador confirmed that the Japanese government has started granting grants to Japanese NGOs since 2002 to support Japanese NGOs' economic and social development projects in developing countries or regions. To date, the Embassy of Japan has provided assistance to more than 140 projects in Cambodia through this program. Each project contributes to improving the quality of life of the Cambodian people.
The Japan Mine Action Organization (JMAS) has been carrying out demining projects since 2002 in collaboration with the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) and has cleared thousands of landmines and unexploded ordnance. In addition, since 2019, JMAS has provided agricultural assistance to improve the livelihoods of people living in areas where landmines and unexploded ordnance have been cleared.
Through these two projects, it is hoped that CMAC's demining and UXO skills will be further enhanced, and that the casualties of people affected by landmines and unexploded ordnance will be further reduced and people's livelihoods improved. People in mine-affected areas will be richer.
"I see that Cambodia has been developing rapidly lately, but there are still some challenges that need to be addressed to improve the quality of life of the people, such as poverty reduction and social development, including Health and educational environment. This is the additional emphasis of Mr. Mikami Masahiro.
