In order for the celebration of the 24th National Cultural Day on March 3, 2022 to run smoothly in the new normal, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced the following:
1. The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts shall cooperate with other ministries, institutions, local authorities, organizations, associations, communities and the private sector operating in the field of culture in order to jointly promote the national culture widely, both directly and through social media.
2. The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts shall act as the Secretariat in preparing the propaganda and dissemination documents for the celebration of the National Cultural Day and shall instruct all Departments of Culture and Fine Arts in the Capital and Provinces to organize the celebration of the National Cultural Day in their localities at the same time. March 3, 2022 By organizing live programs and social media, banners, slogans in public places and posters at major locations.
3: The Ministry of Information must organize a comprehensive program to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3 through national and private media, including radio, television, newspapers, magazines and related documents, to inspire the public to be more aware and actively involved in the preservation and promotion of values and Develop national culture, social morality and social harmony without discrimination on the basis of political, religious or racial discrimination.
4: The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must cooperate in disseminating the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day to students by following the new normal path.
6: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation shall instruct all Ambassadors, Consulates and Honorary Consuls of the Kingdom of Cambodia abroad to participate in organizing programs to celebrate the National Cultural Day, both on social media and / or by other means. Available.
7. The Ministry of Cults and Religions must inspire the movement of monks and all believers to organize the dissemination of the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day in temples, religious centers, Vipassana centers and other shrines by following the new normal path.
8. The Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of National Defense must have a plan to guide the grassroots to maintain security and public order on the occasion of the National Cultural Day on March 3 to be effective and highly responsible.
9. APSARA Authority, Preah Vihear National Authority and Sambo Prei Kuk National Authority must disseminate important achievements related to conservation, value promotion and sustainable development in World Heritage sites and other cultural sites to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3.
10. Capital and provincial administrations must support the Department of Culture and Fine Arts in organizing celebrations and outreach activities in their territories, focusing on educating the masses, especially among the youth to have a stronger spirit. In participating in preserving, protecting and promoting national cultural values.
11: All homes, all ministries, institutions, local authorities, schools, factories, public and private enterprises must participate in the celebration of National Cultural Day in a new normal way and in other ways, such as raising national flags, flags, banners, slogans, paintings, arts, culture and / or Appropriate activities at its location as well as on social media on March 3, 2022.
