The following is the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Senior official of Phnom Penh Capital Hall: The distribution and collection of garbage from Phnom Penh is much better.
(Phnom Penh): In Phnom Penh today, the storage, distribution and collection of garbage from Phnom Penh is better, that is, after three garbage transport companies are competing with the participation of The private sector and the people as well.
This was confirmed by Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, as he received a trash can from Coca-Cola Cambodia on Samdech Techo Hun Sen Park in Chaktomuk Sangkat, Daun Penh District this morning. February 23, 2022.
Mr. Nuon Pharath said that the participation of the private sector and the people is the effort of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, especially to educate the people to know how to sort solid waste according to its type. Let Phnom Penh be more beautiful than the current level.
He said that in the last stage in Phnom Penh, there are three garbage collection companies competing on garbage collection, which makes Phnom Penh more beautiful and environmentally better. In addition, the private sector and the people have also actively participated in the administration of Phnom Penh, which makes Phnom Penh more beautiful and have a good environment that makes people happy.
It should be noted that in that program, Coca-Cola Cambodia handed over 50 sets of garbage bins, equivalent to 150 bins to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to be placed in some public park locations in Phnom Penh. Cambodian diplomat: "Multilateralism" as a mechanism for peace and development
(Paris): Speaking at the Ministerial Forum for Indo-Pacific Cooperation in Paris, France on February 22, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, stressed that multilateralism Popularism is a mechanism for peace and development. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which was received by Fresh News.
The Deputy Prime Minister also expressed his satisfaction with the promotion of the ASEAN-EU Strategic Partnership and looked forward to the ASEAN-EU Anniversary Summit to be held this year to celebrate the 45th anniversary of relations. Conversation partner.
He stressed that greater economic interdependence will reduce the risk of conflict, and those countries need to further strengthen regional and inter-regional economic cooperation.
The Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair also welcomed the completion of the ASEAN-EU Comprehensive Air Transport Agreement and looked forward to the future achievement of the ASEAN-EU Free Trade Agreement.
Regarding concerns on regional peace and security, the Deputy Prime Minister also briefed the forum on developments in Myanmar. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Myanmar in early January was aimed at resolving the stalemate. And the practical approach of the ASEAN Chair Special Envoy to the implementation of the Five Point Consensus.
The plenary session was followed by three roundtables on digital connectivity and technology, global challenges (climate, biodiversity, oceans, health) and security and defense issues.
On the sidelines of the Roundtable on Security and Defense, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon reiterated Cambodia's position on modernizing the Ream Naval Base for the purpose of national defense in accordance with the Constitution.
Ministry of Education and National Authority for Combating Drugs Receive Award from Southeast Asian Tobacco Control Coalition
The award ceremony is organized by the Southeast Asian Tobacco Control Coalition (SEATCA) via video and has the participation of all 10 ASEAN countries working in the field of tobacco control, including the Ministry of Institutions. ASEAN members such as the Thai Ministry of Health, Singapore and the Philippines and the Indonesian Ministry of Education, Culture, Research and Technology also received the award.
The directive comes after a number of tobacco companies sponsored educational institutions for the purpose of promoting their company name and products to students.
