* Second, the Mine Authority must continue to coordinate with national and international operators and stakeholders to identify areas or locations that are at risk from landmines, cluster munitions and explosive remnants of war in order to conduct timely disaster prevention education. Both to develop educational messages and educational methods more effectively in the context of the affected communities and the attitudes of the vulnerable.
* Fourth, the Mine Authority, relevant ministries, institutions, donor countries and development partners should continue to explore innovative ways to mobilize resources, especially to promote the participation of the private sector in the process of achieving a vision of a mine-free Cambodia by 2025.
