The following is the message on the occasion of the 23rd anniversary of the National Mine Awareness Day: Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of closing the meeting to review the work of the old year and the work direction of the new year of the Ministry of Interior
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of February 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2021 work review meeting and the 2022 work direction of the Ministry of Interior. On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen gave a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Remarks at the Closing Ceremony of the 2021 Annual Meeting and 2022 Work Orientation of the Ministry of Interior
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to attend the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Interior this year after missing last year due to Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praises the leadership of the Armed Forces of the Ministry of Interior for participating in the fight against Kovid 19 to reopen Cambodia now
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commends the Ministry of Interior and the Armed Forces for performing seven tasks well
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen provides 9 guidelines to the Ministry of Interior, National Police Force, relevant ministries and institutions to prevent crimes and serve the local people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks the provinces with a large Muslim population to take care of a Khmer-Muslim deputy governor
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this is not a quota, but a facilitation for a province with a large number of Cambodian Muslims. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers that this is not a quota, a compromise for harmony in the province and a policy framework
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that provinces with a large number of Cambodian Muslims must submit a proposal to the Ministry of Interior
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expresses his condolences to local officials who have struggled and worked hard after more transfers
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the provinces with many Khmer Muslim brothers are not many, including Kampong Cham, Kratie, Kampong Thom, Pursat, Kampot and Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests to jointly support revenue collectors for the state, such as the Customs and Taxation Unit
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that since Samdech issued an absolute order not to have duty-free cars, the state has collected $ 51 million in revenue, of which about half have not been collected yet.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for support for all tax collection, and without the support of local authorities, we can not collect all taxes
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that as long as the CPP is in power, it will not levy taxes on farmland, and if future generations of CPP leaders dare to levy taxes, Samdech will curse them.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalls the story of Tirachchan village in Kampong Chhnang province, where Cambodians revolted and killed France because of the tax on farmland
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Requests Businesses to Pay Taxes According to the Law and Authorities Must Support Tax Collection
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Requests Ministries, Institutions and Sub-National Authorities to Pay Attention to Budget and Reduce Expenditure in the Context 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen issues an order to postpone all unnecessary projects of the state that have not yet started construction, waiting to pass the 19th Kovid stage
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that on February 25 and 27, new vaccines will arrive in Cambodia as ordered
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalls the Royal Government's decision not to continue recruiting officials in the context of Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that it is fortunate that Cambodia was able to earn $ 470 million in January, but this money is not enough for our expenses
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed outrage over a unit requesting to buy a car to go to the base, but Samdech has already rejected this request
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks lower-level officials not to submit proposals to their ministers to ask the Prime Minister for unnecessary expenses, where they should be spent, where they should not be spent, where they should not be spent. Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that sometimes the Prime Minister is very reluctant about these unnecessary requests, and the officials who make those proposals are very good at arguing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all members of the government are aware of the amount of state revenue that Samdech Banh gives at the end of each month
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the cost of supporting the people affected by Kovid, the cost of vaccines and other expenses to prevent Kovid 19 is not over in Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that sometimes the Prime Minister is very reluctant about these unnecessary requests, and the officials who make those proposals are very good at arguing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns to burn another 5,000 tax evading vehicles if they refuse to pay taxes as requested by the Royal Government
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks all civil servants to reduce costs because the budget is short and Samdech Techo issued an order to postpone all unnecessary projects of the state that have not yet started construction, waiting to pass the Kovid 19 phase.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the necessary expenses are vaccines and medicines for Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on companies to pay taxes to the Royal Government
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that if the economic bomb explodes and nearly 17 million people will all go, then we must ensure our stability
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reacts to Agriculture Minister Veng Sakhon about raising pork prices in Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen is angry with Agriculture Minister Veng Sakhon for never cooperating with any minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen questioned that if the Cambodians supply enough pigs, as Minister Veng Sakhon said, how can the price of pork go up?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is optimistic about the Ministry of Interior's commitment to implementing the plan for 2022.
Spokesman of the General Commission: 684 more vehicles were inspected and fined on February 23, 2022
According to the spokesperson, as of February 23, 2022, traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 34,896 vehicles, including 26,352 motorcycles and 8,544 vehicles.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmets, cell phones, overtaking license plates and sign offenses. In particular, speeding vehicles, violating signs, no driver's license, no license plate, drunkenness, overdue belts, business belts and telephones.
Please note that for February 23, 2022, traffic accidents throughout the country also occurred 6 times, in which 2 people died, 5 people were injured (4 people were seriously injured). During the 54 days, there were 548 traffic accidents, resulting in 311 deaths and 745 injuries (483 serious injuries).
Taiwan is shocked by the situation in Ukraine
However, Taiwanese officials said the island authorities had not observed any irregularities by Chinese military forces. Taiwan has always been monitoring the activities of the Chinese military, especially the Chinese Air Force, as 2021 was recently considered the year when China sent the largest number of fighter jets over the island. It was the most stressful time in 40 years.
On Wednesday, Taiwan's President Tsai Ing-wen told a task force meeting that Taiwan must step up its vigilance on regional military action and address the issue. Also for disseminating false information from abroad. However, she did not mention the name "China" at the meeting.
China has not yet commented on Taiwan's fears, but on Tuesday Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi and his US counterpart Anthony Blinken met by telephone to discuss the crisis. Ukraine and Taiwan issues. "Incorporating Taiwan into a strategy to counter China is becoming a completely false message," Wang told Blinken.
Wang's remarks come after the United States in early February made further commitments to provide resources and diplomatic support to the Indo-Pacific region. Washington has also said it will work with relevant partners inside and outside the region to ensure stability and peace in the strait that divides between Taiwan and China.
