On the occasion of leading the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and the direction of the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that through his own Facebook is to receive requests and problems of many local people to ask. Samdech to intervene to solve and Samdech sent this problem back to the local authorities to solve for the people.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng claimed that it was good for the leaders to receive such requests or problems directly from the people, but on the other hand, it showed that the people were not comfortable with the local officials, so they sent This information comes to the top to help intervene.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "I would like to ask the capital-province as well as all units under the Ministry of Interior to contact us and contact the people so that the people can contact us and solve the problem there." Unless we resolve not to go beyond our means. "But if the problem is within our capacity, we have to work hard to solve it."
According to Samdech Krala Hom, another reason why people report such concerns to Samdech is because they do not trust the local authorities or the authorities do not solve all these problems for them or ignore them and consider it a normal problem.
At this point, Prince Sar Kheng emphasized, "I have encountered a lot and sometimes too many problems, they do not pay much attention, so I suggest that no matter how small the problem, we are officials. Do not give up. Must collect all to check.
The head of the Ministry of Interior reminded that in the past, anonymous letters were not valued, but now this is not the case, even if the informant is anonymous, as long as the information is true, it must be addressed. The prince said that the reason why he was anonymous was because he did not dare to come forward because it was sensitive and when he went out, it could affect his safety.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that when Samdech received all this information through Facebook, his team organized to distribute all the information to each unit within the jurisdiction to forward to the basic level. Resolve. Samdech continued that some places have been resolved and sent the report back that it has been resolved, but some places did not send the report back.
In this regard, Samdech clarified that all units and institutions under the Ministry of Interior, when they receive the report or report, must deal with it and respond immediately, not leave it silent.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng seems to be wondering that it should not be a little small at the local level to jump to the upper level at all, but local officials should pay attention to solve for the people and the leaders to solve any problem that is not large Solve such basic issues.
(Kampot): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, on the night of February 18, 2022, visited to solve the road dispute of two families in Kampong Kreng village, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province. The governor's search for a solution to the people's disputes tonight led to the admiration and admiration of the governor.
Recently, Ms. Min Ko Anna, not wanting to have to pass in front of her house just built for living, she closed this road more than 40 meters, which is the entrance to the back of the land and keep the entrance from the front For common use. The road closure of about 40 meters did not affect the access to Ms. Hak Lina's land, because the road from the front that was maintained was able to access Ms. Hak Lina's land.
The roadblocks that Ms. Hak Lina had asked to travel led to the conflict and led to the intervention of the provincial governor.
Mr. Mao Thunin spent more than two hours to mediate on this issue. He allowed the people who heard about the land history in the area to confirm it one by one and also allowed both sides of the conflict to present their requests.
Residents of the area have all acknowledged that the disputed road was purchased by Min Ko Ana and arranged for access to their land.
However, after more than two hours of negotiations, Ms. Hak Lina's side refused to accept and demanded that Ms. Min Ko Ana's side reopen the 40-meter-long road.
As the two sides could not reach an agreement, Mr. Mao Thunin ordered the provincial officials to survey the actual land area of both parties according to the land plan set by the authorities and find time to resolve the dispute with the parties again.
However, the people who attended the mediation that night expressed strong support for the resolution proposed by Governor Mao Thunin.
Regarding this route, Ms. Hak Lina also complained to the Kampot Provincial Court. However, the court did not oppose the construction of the road fence.
