(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, in a meeting with the Seventh Committee of the National Assembly on the morning of February 22, 2022, reported on the implementation of the strategic plan for education, especially in the Kovid crisis. 19 Emphasis on turning the Kovid-19 crisis into an opportunity to create digital education.
At the same time, he highlighted the great achievements of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, including: digital education, distance education, the establishment of a digital platform, the installation of MoEYS E-Learning program and the reception. Success in organizing the high school diploma exam on December 27, 2021.
With the above achievements, the Minister took this opportunity to express his gratitude and appreciation to all teachers, education staff, leaders of public and private educational institutions who have worked together to maintain the quality, equity, environment and education as a whole. Life for students.
"Without Kovid-19, the ministry may not have been able to reach digital learning and teaching practices," he said. "Starting from the consensus, our professional teachers have cooperated and agreed to provide free teaching, which allows the Ministry to process education digitally."
