BEIJING: The Chinese embassy in Ukraine on Tuesday issued a warning to all Chinese citizens to stay away from the volatile region, but did not tell them to consider leaving Eastern Europe as the situation escalates. Strong. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, February 22, 2022.
On Monday, Russian President Vladimir Putin escalated tensions by ordering the deployment of troops to two separatist areas in eastern Ukraine under what he claimed was peacekeeping. There, after recognizing the two regions as independent states separate from Ukraine.
"The situation in eastern Ukraine has undergone significant changes," the Chinese embassy in Ukraine said in a statement. "The embassy urges all Chinese citizens in Ukraine to pay attention to safety guidelines issued by local authorities and to avoid travel to volatile areas."
In February, several countries, including the United States, Britain and Germany, urged their citizens to leave Ukraine immediately due to concerns about Russia's invasion of Ukraine. .
