(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) in collaboration with the Embassy of Indonesia in Cambodia and the Indonesian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia on 22 February 2022 organized the Cambodia-Indonesia Investment Dialogue at the Council for the Development of Cambodia and broadcast Live via video to discuss promoting investment cooperation as well as disseminating new investment laws to Indonesian investors in Cambodia and abroad.
Indonesian Ambassador Sudar Manhaseng hailed some recent achievements by the Royal Government of Cambodia, such as the free vaccination of people at a remarkably high rate, which has made the epidemic of Kovid-19 can be controlled and the investment environment can be improved through the adoption of a new investment law, which was promulgated on October 15, 2021.
He praised the promotion of Cambodia-Indonesia relations, while Cambodia is actively striving to play an active role as chair of ASEAN in 2022 to ensure regional peace, which is a precondition for development and attract investment to the region in particular. Cambodia.
The Ambassador said that the Indonesian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, which was officially established on September 23, 2021, and the Indonesian Embassy in Cambodia will cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions in Cambodia to promote Indonesian investment. More Cambodia.
Indonesia's Minister of Investment and Maritime Affairs Luo Binsar Panjaytan noted the progress of bilateral investment cooperation between Indonesia and Cambodia over the past two decades. He commended the Council for the Development of Cambodia for drafting the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with the proactive approach to promoting, facilitating, guaranteeing, protecting and maintaining investment in all aspects.
He believes that through this dialogue, the Indonesian business community will better understand and deepen the new investment law and will help promote more Indonesian investors to invest in Cambodia.
The Delegation highlighted the commitment of the Council for the Development of Cambodia to provide investment facilitation and investment maintenance services to investors, especially Indonesian investors who decide to invest in Cambodia. Cambodia Securities Exchange launches CSX Trade Mobile App for Listed Securities Trading
This mobile application was developed entirely by the technical team of the Stock Exchange of Cambodia, following the pattern and maintaining the main functions available in the mobile trading system (MTS), but with the addition of security features, special design is Add master system capabilities to be able to get more commands faster.
Through this mobile app, investors can place orders to sell securities, check securities transactions, check securities and cash balances, as well as check market data, listed company information, and more market information.
The development of this mobile application is another new step in the Cambodia Securities Exchange to ensure the response to the development needs of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, the increase in the number of listed companies and the number of investors that this mobile application will be a driving force. Further to promote trading growth and liquidity in the Cambodian stock market.
Mr. Sieng Thirith said that by the end of 2021, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia had issued a total of 30,798 investor identification numbers, of which 30,649 were individual investors and 149 were legal entities.
In addition, Mr. Sieng Thirith stated that the securities market in Cambodia in the context of the spread of Kovid 19, with a total market capitalization of about 2.43 billion US dollars, of which the total trading volume in 2021 increased by 386 % And daily trading volume increased by about 382% compared to 2020.
Taking this opportunity, he also asked all investors to download this program and participate in the trial together and provide feedback to improve so that the Cambodia Securities Exchange can be improved before the official launch of the plan. Held next May.
