Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Opening Ceremony of Boeung Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant
(Phnom Penh): On February 22, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Boeung Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant on an area of 3 hectares. The hectare is located in Prek Ta Kong 1 Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
During the groundbreaking ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in about one month, three infrastructure projects were inaugurated and opened under the cooperation between Cambodia and Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is not easy in the development phase and need to find a suitable location for the release of wastewater.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Phnom Penh Capital Administration for cooperating with Japan's JICA in the construction of the Choeung Ek Lake Wastewater Treatment Plant.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the presence of Boeung Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant now is due to the good relations between Cambodia and Japan, which 2023 is the 70th anniversary of this relationship.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the sending of the Self-Defense Forces to Cambodia 30 years ago is a memorable memory that must be done to commemorate the anniversary of this trip.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's progress cannot be separated from the contribution of friendly countries, including Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the relationship between Cambodia and Japan is deeper and the cooperation is bigger.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is not only waiting for Japanese assistance, but also efforts to attract Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not understand the suggestion that the port of Sihanoukville could become a debt trap like the port of Sri Lanka while the port of Sihanoukville was being built by Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Ambassador, Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Minister of Defense, Commander-in-Chief of the Japanese Armed Forces for welcoming Dr. Hun Manet.
