Fuel prices in Vietnam reach record highs
These prices are higher than the highest level ever experienced in July 2014. Monday's fuel price hike is the fifth in a row since December 10, 2021.
According to the Ministry of Industry and Trade and the Ministry of Finance, which is responsible for controlling Vietnam's oil prices, the price of oil components has risen by nearly 6% since February 11.
Meanwhile, global crude oil prices have fallen slightly as news of recent diplomatic efforts to resolve the crisis in Ukraine has allayed concerns about oil supplies.
Vietnamese authorities adjusted fuel prices on February 1, 11 or 21 to reflect global oil price fluctuations after delays.
