Mr. HUN Manet: The virtues of each party member are the success factor of our party
(Preah Vihear): Mr. HUN Manet, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Youth of the Central Cambodian People's Party, on February 20, 2022, announced the composition of the Preah Vihear Provincial Party Youth Working Group.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. HUN Manet stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leaders and members of the Cambodian People's Party, led the construction of Cambodia out of poverty and poverty, and at that time, the international community became known as an insecure area as a minefield. They are afraid but now it has become a prosperous, peaceful island and a popular country both regionally and globally.
In this sense, the youth, who are the core force and the successor force of the party, have the duty to contribute to ensure the sustainability of the country's leadership by working hard, adhering to the ideals of patriotism, upholding the great national interest and daring to make all kinds of sacrifices. For the peace, stability and peace of the people, as well as the unification of the forces of great unity to build and develop the nation to prosper.
According to Mr. HUN Manet, the youth is the successor cell that the Cambodian People's Party has taken care to organize, nurture and build capacity on a regular basis and from the very beginning to ensure the sustainability and excellence of leadership and participation. The duty of the party on all socio-political affairs in the cause of serving the nation, the motherland and the people from one generation to another.
Therefore, as the younger generation, we have three main tasks: to continue to maintain the achievements of the previous generation of leaders, to build more new positive achievements in the present, and to lay a solid foundation for the next generation.
Mr. HUN Manet emphasized that the virtues of each party member are the success factor of our party, and whether in the form of a group or as an individual, we must continue to do good deeds, serve the people, be honest with the people and be with the people in all circumstances.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Prak Sophoan Neary, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on February 21, 2022, appealed to all pregnant women and mothers to live in the context of Kovid 19.
The call was made during the National Maternal, Child and Child Health Day program under the theme "Strengthening the provision of reproductive health services, maternal and child health and the provision of Kovid-19 vaccine to pregnant women and mothers." "Breastfeeding."
On the occasion of National Mother, Baby and Child Health Day, she called on all pregnant women and mothers to:
1: All pregnant women should consult with a doctor / midwife at a health center or hospital near your home 4 times regularly according to the doctor's advice, tetanus vaccine and The Kovid-19 vaccine provides access to all preventive services, especially voluntary blood tests for HIV, syphilis, hepatitis B, to jointly eliminate mother-to-child transmission.
2: Please give birth at a health center or hospital with a doctor or midwife who has been properly trained and to check the health after delivery, both mother and baby to get the vaccine to prevent all 11 diseases on time. Monitor your child's health and growth until he or she is two years old.
3: Breastfeed exclusively from birth to 6 months of age and provide all kinds of nutritious supplements (porridge, all ingredients), along with continued breastfeeding until infancy. Must be at least 2 years old.
4: Take the baby to the hospital immediately when you see any danger signs of respiratory disease, diarrhea or other diseases and take the baby or young child who is thin or does not gain weight at all to consult and receive treatment. Hospital.
5: Choose contraception for the health of mother and baby.
6: All pregnant women, mothers who are breastfeeding should strictly follow the "3 prevent 3 prevent" measures and guidelines of the Ministry of Health and go to get the vaccine against Kovid-19. In turn and on time for everyone.
At the same time, she called on the leaders, civil servants, health workers, all service providers, including branches - sub-branches of the Cambodian Red Cross and the national elite working group to support the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government to be effective. Achieve sustainable development goals.
Air Force Commander: Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is firmly committed to maintaining peace, security, stability and national interests
(Phnom Penh): General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Air Force, stated that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) is firmly committed to playing a core and leading role in maintaining peace, security and stability. And national interests.
General Soeng Samnang said this at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work in 2021 and work direction for 2022 of the Air Force Command on Monday morning, February 21, 2022.
At the ceremony, General Soeng Samnang emphasized that national defense is one of the priorities that the Royal Government always considers carefully to ensure peace, security, stability and enhance national prestige on the international stage.
The Commander-in-Chief of the Air Force told Air Force officials that the security situation for Cambodia has changed steadily due to changes in the domestic situation and the impact of geopolitical and security developments, among other factors. More in the region and the world.
For General Soeng Samnang, these changes require careful attention and consideration in the formulation of defense policies and defense strategies to respond to all opportunities, challenges and threats to national security. Present and future.
"In the past, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has prevented and prevented timely and effective acts of terrorism and destabilization of all kinds. "The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is firmly committed to the successful implementation of the Royal Government's defense policy and will continue to play a key and leading role in maintaining peace, security, stability and national interests." This is the confirmation of General Soeng Samnang.
The Commander of the Air Force also emphasized that in the past, the Air Force has performed its duties with a high sense of responsibility for the destiny of the nation, loyalty and protection of the Royal Government, maintaining trust and Citizen support.
