CBC and RUPP join hands to equip higher education professionals in data science and engineering to Cambodian students
The signing of the Memorandum of Understanding between the two parties on February 21, 2022 is to provide opportunities for qualified Cambodian students to receive scholarships for associate degrees in data science and engineering at the Royal University of Phnom Penh. CBC has decided to provide $ 80,000 in four-year tuition fees to eight engineering and data science students at RUPP.
In addition to full tuition coverage for scholarship recipients, CBC will also be working with the Faculty of Engineering to provide professional development, presentation, and research support for students in data science and engineering programs. This is intended to give students the skills they need to be ready in the marketplace when they graduate.
"RUPP really needs the participation of all institutions to produce human resources for the country," said Dr. Chet Chealy, RUPP Rector. "For today's signing ceremony is a model and a testament to the participation of the private company, KREDIT BURE (Cambodia) in the production of human resources for our society."
"I would like to express my sincere gratitude to Ms. Chea Serey and Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Executive Director and KREDIT Buro (Cambodia) Team, for their full support and risk during this Kovid initiative. We would like to thank the team of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, the Office of International Relations and the Faculty of Engineering for their hard work in organizing this Memorandum of Understanding.
The MoU was signed by Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Chief Executive Officer of KREDIT Bourro (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. and Dr. Ou Ravi, Vice Rector of RUPP. The CBC has also assisted RUPP over the last year by providing sector consulting to develop education programs tailored to the specific needs of the job market.
Dr. Nguon Phan Pheakdey, Dean of the Faculty of Engineering, said, "Through the Royal Government's budget in the project to improve higher education, and especially under the guidance and support of the Rector of the Faculty of Engineering, the Ministry of Education. Youth and sports to receive students majoring in engineering and data science for the academic year 2021-2022.
He added, "For today's signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, KREDIT BURE (Cambodia) has provided scholarships (for eight students) for four years with a total budget of 80,000 (approximately 320 million Riels). ). Taking this opportunity, I would like to call on all students to register for the scholarship.
Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Chief Executive Officer of KREDIT Bourro (Cambodia) Co., Ltd., stated, “As a company that provides data analytics technology services, we know from the beginning that the technology sector is very fast. "Therefore, in order to keep pace with the rapid development of the economy and technology, we need to integrate the private sector with the education sector, such as universities."
"We are pleased to welcome this collaboration as part of our corporate social responsibility work, which provides financial and professional support to students, and at the same time we seem to be helping to prepare you," he said. "It is ready to be a pillar in the financial and economic sectors."
