The first is to require law enforcement officials and practitioners to first understand what is intellectual property? What are the legal conditions and protections?
Second, it requires the victims to have an understanding of the procedures for exercising their rights properly, that is, at least to make them understand that they should file a complaint to any institution. How to find evidence when you encounter an infringement of intellectual property.
Third, it is required that court officials, including prosecutors and judges, as well as lawyers, be aware of the provisions of the Intellectual Property Sector as well as the Anti-Counterfeiting Committee, which is responsible for cracking down on such violations. .
Of course, the Ministry of Justice, the main body for legal and judicial work, has always coordinated with the relevant institutions to make the legal norms in the Kingdom of Cambodia clearer and the law enforcement more effective in line with policy. Of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Regarding the implementation of the law on intellectual property, the Ministry of Justice has always been in a position to support in all forms to promote, train and coordinate to achieve common goals for the benefit of our Cambodian society.
