(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, together with local authorities, on the afternoon of February 21, 2022, invited Krong Pali to open the construction site of Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant of Phnom Penh Sewerage Development Project. Located in Prek Ta Kong 1 Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
After the Krong Pali ceremony to ask the owner of the water, the owner of the land to ask for happiness and prosperity, tomorrow morning, February 22, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant. Once.
The Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, Mr. Sam Piseth, confirmed that the construction project of Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant will be built as a pumping station to send wastewater to Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant with a total pumping capacity of 2 units. 468 cubic meters per hour is located in the lower part next to the drainage pump from the Boeung Trabek pumping station.
Construction of a road for maintenance of a canal with a width of 10 meters and a length of 1,690 meters for digging sewers and drains to Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant with 7 meters of AC rubber, connecting from road 271 forever On Neak Oknha Moha Pheakdey Boulevard, Hun Neang dug a 0.3-meter-long, 1,840-meter-long steel sewer pipe to drain sewage from the sewage pumping plant to the Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant.
Mr. Sam Piseth also confirmed that the project to build the Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant was signed by the governments of both countries "Cambodia-Japan" on October 3, 2019 and then JICA. Signed a grant financing agreement with the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia on November 1, 2019.
It should be noted that in the program on February 22, tomorrow, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will also temporarily suspend traffic by not allowing all kinds of vehicles to cross the section of Neak Oknha Moha Pheakdey, Hun Neang Boulevard (30 meters) from Kang Blvd. Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (St. 271) to Samdech Hun Sen Blvd. (St. 60 meters), that is, until this program is completed and then open to normal traffic.
