Read the full announcement: Cambodian cashew nuts will be on display at the World Food Fair in Japan next month
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian cashew nuts will be presented at a major food fair in Osaka, Japan in March, which will help expand the Cambodian cashew market, especially to attract investors to invest in mango processing plants in Cambodia. Currently, two Japanese companies have come to invest in the construction of a cashew processing plant in Cambodia.
He expects that after the display of Cambodian cashew nuts at a major food fair in Japan will help both promote the quality of cashews and attract Japanese investment to build factories in Cambodia.
"In the past, Japan imported 10,000 tons of processed cashew nuts from some countries, especially 95% from India and 5% from Vietnam," he said. "The main goal of the two Japanese companies is to capture 30% of the market for Cambodian cashews."
He added that in the past, Japanese companies have tested Cambodian cashew nuts and found that in Cambodia's M23 cashew nuts contain omega-28 oleic acid up to 28% more than other countries in the world.
The president of the Cambodian Cashew Association confirmed that Cambodia has now attracted two Japanese companies to invest in the construction of cashew processing plants in Cambodia. Both companies, including TPJ, have plans to invest in a processing plant in Kampong Thom province, and recently another Japanese company has announced plans to open a cashew processing plant in Preah Vihear province.
In 2021, Cambodia imported about 30 tons of cashew nuts to the Japanese market.
