The Ministry of Health issued additional guidelines on strengthening the implementation of health measures to combat and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus, especially in the community.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on February 20, 2022, issued additional instructions on strengthening the implementation of health measures to combat and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus, especially in Omikrong. In the community. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News.
A: Quick test, isolation, treatment and communication Information 1: Quick test for Kovid-19 antigen
2: Isolation for treatment
* Isolation: Kovid-19 patients should be isolated in a clean and well-ventilated area and maintain good personal hygiene by applying three protective measures (wear a mask, wash hands, and keep clean). 1.5 meters or more) to avoid transmission of Kovid-19 virus to family members and others.
Kovid-19 in-home care must follow standard operating procedures for the management, care and treatment of Kovid-19 at home (which the Ministry of Health has already issued frequent reminders) and Report to the local authority where you live.
Kovid-19 patients with moderate or severe resistance: Although many scientific studies have shown that the new mutant virus omega-19 is relatively mild, we must not overlook the possibility of Kovid virus invasion. -19 which can cause serious accident or death.
Kovid-19 Omega patients may also have symptoms that can lead to severe symptoms such as fatigue or shortness of breath, which require timely hospitalization. Do not try to treat at home when there are symptoms such as anxiety, fatigue or shortness of breath or no improvement in health status after treatment at home for a while.
3: Information communication
Individuals who perform a self-test for Kovid-19 on their own and obtain a Kovid-19 positive result must notify their direct contact with a person who has been exposed to a positive K-19 virus before testing for Kovid-19. It tests quickly for the Kovid-19 antigen and is careful to monitor further health, as well as to avoid transmitting the Kovid-19 virus to others.
Individuals diagnosed with Kovid-19 virus should report it to the local authority or medical team, especially the director of the provincial health department in the area where the individual lives, to continue treatment procedures, monitor and prevent transmission to others.
B: Sanitation and participation in the implementation of 3 measures to prevent and 3 not to be consistent
* Everyone must participate in the implementation of 3 measures to prevent and 3 not to stick, such as: - To maintain personal hygiene by applying 3 protection (wear a mask, wash hands and keep a distance of 1.5 meters or more) to Avoid transmitting Kovid-19 virus to family members and others
In daily life, reduce its activities to a minimum, such as:
* Reduced or not in a closed position, not enough ventilation * Reduced or not meeting with too many people * Does not directly affect people who come to meet or talk a lot.
Please note that if all three of the above activities occur at the same time, there will be a high risk of transmission of Kovid-19 virus in clusters or in groups.
Clean with disinfectant on common or public areas and all equipment or utensils that are touched by multiple people.
C: Involvement of Kovid-19 vaccination boost dose
Please join the nationwide Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for both the basic and booster doses and the Kovid-19 vaccine for all ages 3 to under 5 to increase resistance. Severe cases of Kovid-19 virus or the development of a serious disease that can save lives.
Encourage organizers and participants to take a quick self-test for Kovid-19 antigen before attending a rally at a minimum and not to attend any event if the individual is unsafe or has Suspected symptoms of Kovid-19 disease.
