(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Mony, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of State Property and Non-Fiscal Revenue, explained the revenue from the gold mining sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Mony said that in relation to revenue management, the Ministry of Mines and Energy is the ministry responsible for issuing licenses to companies to explore and exploit gold in Cambodia.
Mr. Net Mony said that the collection of mineral revenue is an inter-ministerial declaration between the Ministry of Mines and Energy and the Ministry of Economy and Finance related to the determination of land rent and royalties to be paid into the state budget.
According to the official of the Ministry of Economy, the Ministry of Mines is the one who collects the revenue of this mine and then records it as the revenue of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, which acts as an inter-ministerial working group.
Mr. Neth Mony stated that today Cambodia has seven mining companies licensed by the Ministry of Mines and Energy.
The seven gold mining sites are located in the following provinces: Kratie 1, Preah Vihear 2, Mondulkiri 2, Ratanakiri 1 and Battambang 1.
He added that so far the government has received $ 14 million in revenue, of which $ 5 million is tax and customs revenue.
Mr. Neth Mony said that in relation to this rate, in the inter-ministerial prakas, which has the Ministry of Mines, Energy and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, is to set a 3% commission on revenue from the sale of gold products and fees. Land as well.
