For these peoples, in addition to their close cultural ties, traditions and beliefs, many Russians view Kievan Rus as the center of Kiev today and are considered a common ancestor. After the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, Ukraine gained independence, but in the eyes of Russian nationalism, it was considered an accidental loss.
Here, if you look at the history of Ukraine, you see that the danger comes from the Russian nationalist ideas of the past. Therefore, rewriting the history between the two nations on the basis of science is a good harmony, especially the Kremlin should not write alone.
