Neak Oknha Kith Meng led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to visit the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone to learn more about the development and investment process in this large industrial park.
(Phnom Penh): Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the new President of the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone (PPSP), on February 18, 2022, led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to visit the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone in Phnom Penh. The purpose is to find out more about the development and investment process in this largest special economic zone in Cambodia.
During this visit, the Duke, President and Vice President, as well as members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, listened to the history as well as the major investment projects in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, which has more than 100 large factories and more than 3 employees. 40,000 people.
It should be reminded that on December 17, 2021, InterGestick (Cambodia), a subsidiary of Royal Group, purchased 45.09% of the total shares of Phnom Penh SEZ Plc (PPSP-Special Economic Zone). Phnom Penh) and has become an overwhelming majority of shareholders in the company that develops this industrial park.
On January 26, 2022, at the Extraordinary General Meeting of Shareholders (EGM) of the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, Duke Kith Meng was elected as the new Chairman of the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone (PPSP). Being the first chairman of the largest special economic zone in Cambodia is the greatest honor of the President Duke.
This stock investment is an important step for the development of the Royal Group. With this new business, Duke President hopes that we will bring new technology systems, management, business strategy and more investors to continue to develop special economic zones. We work together to bring the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone to another great attraction.
With an area of approximately 357 hectares, the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone has brought in more than 95 manufacturers and services from 12 countries, as well as more than 80 international companies from 15 different countries to invest in the region. In 2021, the export of goods from factories in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone amounted to 673 million US dollars.
