Cambodia-Japan Joint Joint Committee Meeting to Improve Investment and Business Environment By the end of January this year, Japan has invested 2.9 billion USD in Cambodia
This bilateral meeting is part of the Investment Conservation Mechanism, which has been established since 2009 under the framework of the Agreement between Cambodia and Japan on the liberalization, promotion and protection of investment, signed by Samdech Techo Director. Prime Minister and former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe on June 14, 2007.
In the spirit of jointly improving the investment and business environment in Cambodia, this meeting provided an opportunity for Japanese investors to raise challenges and suggestions to the Royal Government.
Taking this opportunity, the Delegation Minister highlighted the new Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which was recently approved and promulgated on October 15, 2021, which is becoming another strong legal basis of Cambodia to attract Invest and promote economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Minister also thanked JETRO and Mizuho Bank for their responsible participation in organizing a successful seminar on new investment laws for Japanese investors and achieved fruitful results yesterday. November 11, 2021.
In addition, the Minister highly appreciated and appreciated the investment activities of all Japanese investors in the non-textile manufacturing sector, which has played an important role in contributing to the diversification of Cambodia's economic base and human resource development in Cambodia. Cambodia.
Mr. Masahiro Mikami expressed his appreciation and gratitude to all relevant ministries and institutions for their past efforts with a high sense of responsibility in coordinating and providing a gentle response to concerns and requests. Blessings of Japanese investors for providing excellent care and warmth to Japanese investors.
He stressed the need to continue good cooperation between Cambodian government institutions and Japanese investors to achieve success in business and investment activities in Cambodia, which will play a positive role in attracting Japanese investors. Invest more in Cambodia.
The Ambassador expressed his commitment to continue to cooperate with the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting and attracting direct investment from Japan to Cambodia towards the economic progress and prosperity of both countries.
It should be noted that as of the end of January 2022, the Council for the Development of Cambodia welcomed and registered 147 investment projects of Japanese companies with a total investment of about 2.9 billion US dollars.
