General knowledge: The official name of Bangkok and the reasons for moving the capital
Before the founding of the capital in Bangkok, Thailand now had the capitals of Sukhothai and Ayutthaya. After liberating the country from Burmese rule in 1768, King Thaksin established a new capital in Thonburi Fourteen years later, the Buddha moved the capital from Thonburi to Bangkok.
The biggest reason for moving the capital from Thonburi to the east bank of the river was to prevent further Burmese army attacks, as before the capital was invaded, there was also a large Chao Phraya River to block.
Today, the city is popularly known as Bangkok or Thep or Rattanakosin (Ratanakosin) and is now the capital of Thailand, 240 years old.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, emphasized that the Royal Government wants to see the garment sector move towards high-value and value-added goods. High.
In order to increase the value added of the garment sector, the Royal Government has been developing a strategy to develop the garment sector, which is expected to be implemented soon.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Vongsey Visoth presiding over the public forum on macroeconomic management and financial law for management 2022 on the morning of February 18, 2022.
A senior official at the Ministry of Economy said that the Royal Government of Cambodia's hope was due to the first factor: that the system of Cambodia's garment industry was moving forward with significant contributions to the national economy and the second: Neighbors are starting to have problems with the garment sector, so investors and buyers see Cambodia as a good place to increase investment.
According to Mr. Vongsey Visoth, today 95% of garment factories in Cambodia are foreigners, only 5% are Cambodians, so the Royal Government wants to see more Cambodians invest in the garment sector.
Dr. Phan Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that the garment sector is an important economic hub for Cambodia. In the past 2-3 years, the Royal Government has been developing a strategy for the development of the garment sector since 2020. The strategy for the development of the garment sector is to see the Cambodian garment sector have high added value and be able to produce goods that are better and provide more revenue.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Economy, the garment sector development strategy has been prepared and will be decided soon.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, Cambodia's garment exports in 2021 more than 11.389 million dollars, an increase of 15%, despite the outbreak in 2021, leading to the closure of Phnom Penh. And disruption to the production chain.
Around the good growth of exports, experts in the garment sector expect that Cambodia will continue to maintain good growth in garment exports in 2022, orders for garments will increase from about 15% to 20%.
