Commerce Minister Tells Officials to Absolutely Avoid Informal Fees
(Banteay Meanchey): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, told his subordinates to pay attention to fulfill their duties and responsibilities to meet the needs of business people, traders and traders. The Minister specifically warned officials to strictly avoid demanding informal fees.
The Reminder of the Minister of Commerce was made during a meeting with officials of the Department of Commerce and branch officials of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression (CPPCC) in Banteay Meanchey Province on 17 February. 2022 ago.
"All officials must continue to work closely with local authorities to promote the Royal Government's in-depth reform program, especially the Ministry of Commerce's deepening trade policy," he added. "Karma aims to facilitate exports and facilitate the provision of public services to the people."
"All officials must strictly avoid demanding informal fees from traders, producers, exporters and other services, which is contrary to the content of the joint declaration on public service between the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance," he said. .
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak also instructed his subordinates to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease by getting vaccinated in all doses and being extra careful to maintain the social gap and to implement In accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
