More than 1,000 turtles and ducks smuggled from Vietnam illegally intercepted in Kandal province
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Economic Crimes Police Office, in cooperation with Kandal Fisheries Administration District Force, detained a white Samsung car with license plate number 2A-0318 at the intersection of National Road 1, Banteay Dek Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province in connection with the case. Suspected importing turtles and ducklings from Vietnam without permission.
According to the authorities, the driver of the car was named Som Saroeun, 28 years old, residing in Thnal Peam village, Ang Sre commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province. Svay Rieng province was arrested on February 15, 2022 recently.
Ly Socheat, Deputy Commissioner for Economic Crimes Planning, told Fresh News Agency on February 18, 2022 that after investigating the crime of importing live animals without permission, he organized a force. And cooperated with Kandal Provincial Fisheries to stop the above vehicle and check the evidence as described above.
He said that the turtle exhibits were kept at the Central Fisheries Administration to follow the procedure. The ducklings were handed over to a veterinarian in Takhmao City to follow the procedure.
