Scientific knowledge of why the Beijing Winter Olympics lay artificial snow
BEIJING (Reuters) - Recently, some foreign media outlets have fabricated rumors that the use of artificial snow at the Beijing Winter Olympics was "unsustainable" and as a result was "taught" by fans. Internet with in-depth knowledge.
In fact, the use of artificial snow is not only environmentally friendly but also manageable, safer and better than natural snow! Artificial snow is widely used in many Winter Olympics, such as in Sochi and Pyeongchang.
Thanks to the efforts of the artificial snow science researchers of the Beijing Winter Olympics, there are such good capabilities that make it possible for athletes to achieve better, safer! See cartoons to increase knowledge:
1: Artificial snow has a serious impact on the environment, this is a rumor before
3: The problem has come out, why use artificial snow instead of natural snow? In fact, artificial snow is easier to use than natural snow.
4: You may think that if you can only use natural snow, if not snow, what to do?
5: Because of this, snow sports in international sports, especially the Winter Olympics, generally use artificial snow to pave the road. Artificial snow can help us get rid of dependence on natural snow. Very understandable. So why are some winter track races still using artificial snow in areas with year-round snowfall and more snowfall?
