Nine A-level students in Ratanakkiri province receive money and a computer from the provincial governor
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, this morning, February 17, 2022, handed over 9 computers and 300,000 Riels each as an incentive to 9 outstanding students who passed the A-level exam. High school exam session in the school year 2020-2021 ago.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun also thanked the relevant authorities, teachers, parents, guardians of all students who have dedicated their physical and mental strength to help promote and train more children at home, learning and distance learning through the system. Online, these are the strongest sacrifices in the context of the spread of Kovid 19 to make students become good citizens, bamboo shoots and a strong pillar for the nation.
Please be reminded that the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination on December 27, 2021 in Ratanakkiri Province has 2 examination centers, including 11 Anlong Primary Examination Centers in Science and 41 exam rooms in Samdech Ov Samdech Mey High School in Social Sciences.
(Phnom Penh): The Khmer Will Party on February 17, 2022 issued a statement expressing interest and appreciation for the visit of Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Deputy Commander of the Army. Holds Japan from 14 to 17 February 2022.
According to a statement obtained by Fresh News, the Khmer Will Party is pleased to celebrate the dialogue between Dr. Hun Manet and Japanese Foreign Minister Yohim Sahayahi, with Japan announcing its support and participation in the Cambodian elections in 2022 and 2023. Same as in the 2018 election.
The Khmer Will Party is also celebrating the anniversary of the Japanese peacekeeping operation in Cambodia, the first overseas operation of the Japanese Self-Defense Forces within the framework of the United Nations. The Khmer Will Party is happy to support the outcome of the agreement between the Cambodian and Japanese Army Chiefs, who pledged to work together to further strengthen ties.
The Khmer Will Party, chaired by Kong Monika among young Cambodian politicians, has been invited to visit and learn about the experiences of Japanese political parties, especially the first official visit abroad, especially in Japan. Of Dr. Hun Manet after the Cambodian People's Party supports the future candidate for Prime Minister.
The Khmer Will Party is pleased and supports the Cambodian-Japanese side for Japan's free and open Indo-Pacific Strategic Initiative for Peace, Stability, Development and Prosperity in the region and the world.
The Khmer Will Party claims that it is very happy and proud that Cambodia has two great powers in Asia, China and Japan, that have played a role in helping to rebuild Cambodia wholeheartedly and regularly after the Paris Agreement of October 23, 1991 and the election year. 1993.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan Meets Malaysian Foreign Minister at Islamic Center Phnom Penh
The meeting was held at the Islamic Center in Phnom Penh, which was attended by senators, members of the National Assembly, Secretaries of State, Undersecretaries of State, Advisers to the Office of the Council of Ministers, Generals, Brigadier Generals and other officials who are the leaders of Cambodian Islam.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan, representing the entire Muslim community, expressed his pleasure at today's meeting.
On that occasion, he also mentioned the achievements that the Islamic community of Cambodia has received from the Royal Government of Cambodia under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Islamic community has full rights to live and practice their religion. In addition, the Islamic community of Cambodia also has the opportunity to serve in the Royal Government.
He added that in 2015, the government also provided the Cambodian Islamic community with 1,500 state teachers. In addition, the Cambodian government has given the Cambodian Muslim community the right to set up a Cambodian halal institution with the support of Malaysia and other countries.
The Malaysian Foreign Minister also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for granting full rights to the Cambodian Muslim community regardless of race or religion. He added that the Cambodian Muslim community is a model community for ethnic Muslim communities in all countries in the world, because the Cambodian Muslim community has good relations with the Royal Government and has sufficient capacity to serve the motherland.
