Police in Sihanoukville Continue Mobile Patrols on National Road 4 to Enforce Road Traffic Law
(Preah Sihanouk): Police forces in Preah Sihanouk Province have cooperated in continuing mobile patrols on National Road No. 4 to enforce the law on land traffic, speeding, drunken driving, overtaking in dangerous situations, drugs and reversing drivers.
The operation took place on February 17, 2022, led by Brigadier General E Sokha, Deputy Commissioner of the Sihanoukville Provincial Police, to receive a plan of order, led by the Office of Road Traffic and Drug Crimes in collaboration with the District Police Inspectorate. Prey Nup mobile patrol on National Road 4.
The purpose of this operation is to tighten the implementation of the law on road traffic, control the speed of alcohol, overtaking in dangerous situations, drugs and drivers reversing traffic to prevent any crime and reduce accidents that occur eventually. On National Road 4 to reduce traffic accidents, protect the lives and security of people traveling on the road.
As a result, the above-mentioned joint police force inspected 47 heavy truck drivers without any traffic offenses and tested 47 drunk drivers with negative results.
In addition, the police also checked the drugs of 47 drivers of heavy trucks, 2 positive results, 2 minor, the reason for not using for more than 3 months, the force of the specialized office has made a contract to stop the use of drugs and handed over to the owners The educational vehicle continues to guide and then return.
Minister of Labor urges investment in youth skills development and employment
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, has urged more investment in the development of youth employment and employment skills, and this investment also requires attention to quality and quantity. Work to promote current and future social development.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng emphasized that the evolution of technology and globalization, as well as demographic and climate change, are major trends that are bringing about changes in the world of work, and this also offers many new opportunities. But these changes also bring challenges for people to gain skills, as well as challenge the private sector to adapt to these changes sustainably.
At the same time, the Ministry has been promoting the implementation of the Strategic Plan for Employment and Vocational Training Development 2019-2023, especially the second key strategy "Modernization of technical and vocational education and training system" to build a skilled workforce. Clear professionalism, innovation and high competitiveness that can meet the needs of the local and regional labor market.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has issued some new guidelines to the Capital-Provincial Administration and the Department of Tourism to manage the business of adult entertainment centers (karaoke, entertainment, bars, discos, bars and beer gardens) effectively and help prevent the spread. Kovid-19 is also a new type of omega-3.
The introduction was made at a meeting on the management of adult tourism resorts after the reopening of business on February 17, 2022, chaired by Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Tourism, with the participation of Mr. Director of the Department of Tourism and Deputy Governor of the capital-province with the implementation of tourism safety rules and procedures for the implementation of minimum standards (SOP) in the new normal path for the tourism service business.
It should be informed that after November 30, 2021, the Royal Government has allowed the business of adult tourism center to reopen. After obtaining this permission, the karaoke business, entertainment club business, bar-discotheque business, beer garden business, a total of 845 locations reopened as of January 2022.
In order for the management of the adult tourism business to be effective and to prevent the spread of the new Kovid-19 virus, Mr. Tith Chantha has put forward the following recommendations:
1: Request the Capital-Provincial Administration with responsible responsibilities and the Department of Tourism to implement thoroughly by continuing to strengthen the implementation of tourism safety rules and procedures for the implementation of minimum standards (SOP) along the new normal trajectory and promote the business of full-fledged tourist resorts. To apply for a tourism license.
2: The Department of Tourism shall inspect and guide the karaoke business places, clubs and clubs that are too small and can not follow the safety rules, it is advisable to organize the business location properly.
3. The Department of Tourism shall prepare a report on the implementation of tourism safety measures on a regular basis to the Capital-Provincial Tourism Development Committee, the Ministry of Tourism and the relevant specialized departments.
4: The Department of Tourism shall establish the conditions of tourism safety rules to the extent that small businesses can apply in accordance with the actual business situation, but require some necessary conditions such as vaccination against Kovid-19 wearing a mask, heat, spraying alcohol, maintenance Safety gap, hygiene, etc.
5: The Department of Management of Tourism Services, Sports and Tourism should monitor and monitor the implementation of the business of adult tourism centers, such as:
6. If any business establishment does not follow the tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOP) in the new normal course, the Capital-Provincial Administration shall take measures to temporarily suspend business operations for improvement. Ukraine accuses Russian-backed rebels of firing on a kindergarten
