In the first month of this year, the General Department of Taxation collected 288 million USD for the national budget, an increase of 32.70%
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that in January 2022, the tax revenue collected by the General Department of Taxation was 288.23 million USD compared to January. 2021 saw an increase of approximately $ 71.03 million, equivalent to 32.70%.
For 2022, in order to ensure the effective implementation of tax revenue collection management in accordance with the financial law plan for the management of 11,419.13 billion Riels (approximately 2,819.54 million USD), the General Department of Taxation will continue to strengthen Implement fiscal policy and administrative measures, including the following key measures:
* Continue to pay attention to and strengthen the implementation of the recommendations of the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance as the direction for further implementation for 2022 of the General Department of Taxation at the meeting to review the results of tax collection for 2021 on January 26, 2022
* Strengthen the implementation of tax debt collection and measures to tighten tax debt, especially potential large tax debt by identifying priority debt and enterprises in areas not affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak.
* Continue to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request for temporary suspension or reopening, with measures to inspect the location of the enterprise directly, monitor the filing of declarations and strengthen the audit of documents.
* Continue to strengthen and pay attention to enterprise closure applications and audits for enterprise closure requests
* Strengthen the management of income tax collection for 2021 by continuing to organize training seminars on income tax and submit online tax returns (E-Filing) to taxpayers accurately and timely. * Continue to strengthen tax registration and updating enterprise information
* Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of billing rules among taxpayers to ensure efficiency and transparency in the management of tax revenue collection.
* Continue the preparation of the new fiscal law by launching discussions at the relevant ministries and institutions to ensure that the organization is comprehensive and interconnected, as well as responsive to the growth of the national economy, ensuring clarity, efficiency, legitimacy and consistency. Of Tax Revenue Management
* Continue to strengthen the implementation of the obligation to install beer and non-alcoholic beverage meters of domestic production enterprises (Flowmeter) in accordance with Prakas No. 010 MEF.PrK dated 12 January 2021 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to ensure Transparency and fair competition in the Kingdom of Cambodia
* Continue to reform human resources and continue to strengthen the implementation of labor law and be gentle but firm, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and tax revenue management * Continue to implement the necessary measures as set out in Circular on the implementation of the Law on Finance 2022 and continue to implement with attention to the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
