Kampong Thom Provincial Red Cross Holds a Workshop to Summarize Work Results and Experience of the Project "Expansion of Emergency Preparedness and Response in Sanitation and Water Supply for 5 Years"
(Kampong Thom): Mrs. Lum Kuntheary, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Vice Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, this morning, February 17, 2022, chaired a workshop to summarize the work and experience of the project "Expansion". Ability to prepare for and respond to emergency water sanitation ”for 05 years 2017-2021 at the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampong Thom province.
Ms. Lum Kuntheary said that this workshop was held to exchange experiences on water sanitation work, as well as to strengthen the capacity and enhance the water sanitation work that the four branches of the Cambodian Red Cross have been implementing during Five years, from 2017 to 2021, through discussions and exchange of experiences for the preparation of action plans for implementation to achieve good results in accordance with the indicators.
She also stated that after receiving the project "Strengthening the capacity to prepare for prevention and response to emergency water sanitation" from the national level, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampong Thom province has given priority to four districts to implement the project in Kampong Svay district. Stong, Santuk and Baray districts cover 23 communes with 138 villages.
During the five years of project implementation, in addition to training, the branch staff of the branch has been involved in raising awareness through the distribution of humanitarian donations, organizing various programs, and outreach. A total of 10,461 people (7,762 females) participated in the awareness raising project on emergency preparedness, response and emergency water supply.
Ms. Lum Kuntheary also developed an implementation plan for 2022 and subsequent years for the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampong Thom province to be ready for the five target locations: Stung Sen, Taing Kork, Sandan, Prasat Sambo and Prasat Balang districts. . Mr. Vongsey Visoth highlighted Cambodia's commitment as ASEAN chair in 2022 at the G20 meeting of finance ministers and central bank governors
