(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Thursday night, February 17, 2022, issued a special message to his compatriots, confirming the decision to vaccinate children from 3 to 5 years old.
In this special audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated the reasons for this decision as follows: More than 20 percent get the disease. To be honest, even my 21st grandson, who was less than two years old, was infected. "So we need to inject children between the ages of three and five."
Samdech Techo added, "It is necessary to protect our children from being infected with the new Omikrong virus, Kovid 19." "So we have no better choice than to give the basic dose as the first dose and the second dose for children under 5 years old, from 3 to under 5 years."
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, there are an estimated 700,000 children between the ages of three and five. Samdech Techo called on parents and guardians to bring their children to be vaccinated at places where vaccinations are organized by the health department and local authorities.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Ministry of Health and the National Vaccination Commission, as well as the Department of Health and other relevant departments to facilitate the vaccination process for children from 3 to 5 years as soon as possible and make it safe. Most.
Through this measure, Samdech Techo expressed the hope that Cambodian children will avoid the catastrophe of health problems caused by 20 to 25 percent of children to the use of ventilators.
"Vaccines are the best option to ensure that they are immune and free of disease," he added. "If there is an infection, it does not lead to serious and life-threatening."
Samdech Techo expressed his belief that with the experience already, all sectors and all levels, especially people and children receive the first full dose of vaccine safely.
