Announcing the new Chief of Stung Treng Provincial Prison, Mr. Prach Sophy, replacing Mr. Chhun Dara
(Stung Treng): On the morning of February 17, 2022, Mr. Pao Hamphan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Stung Treng Provincial Prison Director. Mr. Prach Sophy will replace Mr. Chhun Dara, who will be transferred to the General Department of Prisons, Ministry of Interior.
The inauguration ceremony was held at Stung Treng Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Chhem Savuth, Director General of the General Department of Prisons, Ministry of Interior, Mr. Chheang Lak, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng. As well as heads of relevant departments around the province.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Province, mentioned that the leadership of the Deputy Chief and the officials of the Provincial Prison have paid attention to fulfill their roles and responsibilities in strengthening the management of the development of physical infrastructure, including the promotion of education, rehabilitation, and vocational training. Livelihoods and occupations of inmates in prisons have been consistently achieved.
At the same time, Mr. Svay Sam Eang expressed his regret for the case of the detainee who broke into the wall of the provincial prison and escaped for a short time recently, but was searched and found under Strict orders of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
This case should be considered as a lesson and experience that the new director and deputy director of the new prison should strengthen the management of the prison in a strict, thorough, clear and highly effective way to ensure that gambling or inactivity does not recur.
Mr. Pao Hamphan said that all prison officials must be united, have good internal unity, have good relations with various units, especially the judiciary, must respect their role, must not take their role and use the position and ethics of prison officials. No.
Mr. Prach Sophy, who has just taken office, is committed to following the example of the elders, striving to innovate, help develop the unit further to achieve the strategic goals of the General Department of Prisons and implement the ethics of the General Department of Prisons. Prison officials cooperate with internal solidarity and relevant units to ensure security, safety, education, and rehabilitation of detainees.
