Chinese government to increase support for small companies in industry
BEIJING: China will take steps to stabilize industry and increase financial support for small companies, the cabinet has said. According to Reuters.
Reuters quoted the Chinese Cabinet as saying that China's industrial recovery was not strong as the services sector was hit harder by the Kovid-19 outbreak.
"Industry and services provide the backbone of sustainable economic development and employment," he added.
The new measures will include additional tax exemptions and medium- and long-term loans for small companies, Reuters reported.
The economy faces a number of challenges, including a chronic slump in the real estate sector and tight Kovid-19 disease management, which has hurt consumer confidence and spending.
Official output released showed that China's industrial output rose just 4.3 percent in December from 3.8 percent in November.
The Chinese cabinet added that China will continue to stabilize commodity prices.
"Taxes are necessary as the government raises the price limit for diesel to 30 baht per liter by the end of May," he said.
