Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Japan pays tribute to Lt. Gen. Hun Manet by sending a special plane to visit directly (Video inside) (Kratie): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, thanked the Government of Japan for providing In honor of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander-in-Chief of the Cambodian Army, for sending a special aircraft directly to pay a visit to Japan.
The statement was made by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the inauguration of seven bridges in Kratie and Prey Veng with the assistance of the Government of Japan on February 16, 2022. .
During his visit to Japan from February 14 to 17, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet met with many of Japan's top dignitaries, including the Prime Minister, the Minister of Defense, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, the Chief of Staff of the Self-Defense Forces and the Commander-in-Chief of the Self-Defense Forces. And so on.
Addressing the forum in front of the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that on Wednesday morning, February 16, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet met with the Prime Minister of Japan.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he emphasized that this is a great honor for Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, and since 2010, in 2018 and 2022, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet has officially met with the Prime Minister of Japan. 3 already.
In front of the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that the assistance that came from his work to foreign friends was to build bridges, roads, canals, schools, hospitals and other infrastructure in the country. Take all that help to complete the prince's kitchen, so be aware of this.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I have been criticized as a government that is good at begging, good at begging, but I did not ask to finish my kitchen." "I ask to build bridges, roads, canals, schools, hospitals and other things to serve my people."
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia's progress is inseparable from the support of all development partners, especially Japan. In fact, the achievements of seven bridges in Kratie and Prey Veng provinces, which are now officially inaugurated, are with the assistance of the Government of Japan through JICA.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, through Japanese Ambassador Mikami Masahiro and JICA Representative, thanked the Government of Japan for funding the construction of these seven bridges, including five in Kratie and two in Prey Veng. More. He said that this bridge has connected Cambodia to a good infrastructure network.
These seven bridges are an urgent project to rebuild bridges in flood-prone areas in Kratie and Prey Veng provinces, with a total length of 670 meters and a total length of 3,424 meters. About 35 million US dollars.
It should be noted that in addition to Japan, which has provided assistance to Cambodia in the restoration and development of infrastructure in the country, China is also a country that has provided a lot of assistance to Cambodia. In addition, there are also many countries and development partners who always and continue to provide development assistance to Cambodia.
