(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, February 16, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled to Kratie for the second time for the month of February. The visit to Kratie this morning to preside over with Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, inaugurated 7 bridges in Kratie and Prey Veng with the assistance of the Government of Japan worth about 35 million USD.
During the inauguration ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure at the achievements of the seven bridges with the assistance of the Government of Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is fortunate for Cambodia to receive the attention of Japanese friends to provide assistance for the construction of seven concrete bridges.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Japan has provided loans and assistance for the construction of more than 1.4 billion US dollars in infrastructure.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the opposition always summoned the leader to ask for that request to build roads and bridges for the benefit of the people, not to finish Samdech's kitchen.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the selection of local officials is the choice of the Ministry of Interior, but also through the Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this year the Deputy Minister of Defense of Japan came to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Government of Japan for sending a special aircraft to receive Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Commander of the Cambodian Army.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that on the morning of Wednesday, February 16, Dr. Hun Manet met with the Prime Minister of Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that three Japanese Prime Ministers have allowed Dr. Hun Manet to pay a courtesy call in 2010, 2018 and 2022. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers this permission to be a demonstration of a special relationship between Cambodia and Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants a war between Cambodia and Japan. But the exercise involved disaster relief.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks the Japanese government for supporting Samdech's visit to Myanmar. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that Myanmar's problems cannot be too hard or too soft.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech has no need to spend money to buy the Sun Hak Peace Prize. No one can buy the award committee.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that he will not give up his efforts to solve Myanmar's problems.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reacted to those who said that his visit to Myanmar was a risky diplomacy. Samdech Techo asked if anyone had died due to Samdech's visit?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if this continues for at least another five years, Myanmar's problems will not be resolved. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has said that trying to defeat the military will not solve Myanmar's problems.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on all provincial authorities to provide an environment for political parties to be recognized by the Ministry of Interior for political activities. Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on all political parties to abide by the law in force or the law set by the National Election Committee.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not cause violence, conflict, injury or death due to the election.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for continued efforts to combat Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the meeting program with A-level students and Thida doctors was postponed due to the Kovid 19 pandemic.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the rate of injections is slow. Samdech Techo calls for speeding up the dose.
