The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan and representatives from both organizations on the afternoon of February 14, 2022.
Of that amount, US $ 266,428 has been provided to the Association for Relief and Rescue of Japan (AAR Japan) to implement the "Environmental Education Promotion Project for Children with Disabilities through Strengthening Local Practices, Modeling and Development." Environmental Education Assessment System (Year 3).
Another $ 398,566 has been provided to the Golden Heart NGO to implement the "Four-Year University Physical Education Curriculum Project at the National Institute of Physical Education and Sports (Year 3)."
Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan, thanked both organizations for participating in the Japanese Government Initiative.
