BEIJING, Feb. 12 (Xinhua) - During a telephone conversation with Russian President Vladimir Putin, US President Biden reiterated that if Russia "invades" Ukraine, the United States and its allies will cause Russia Pay a heavy price.
Surprisingly, as Russia and Ukraine have repeatedly stated that they do not want a war, but as countries outside the region, the United States has been inflating an atmosphere that is "almost exploding." Weapons. US officials and the media are working together to make you feel that the United States is "afraid that Russia and Ukraine will not take up arms."
Although the United States has raised the fear of a series of wars, many international opinion analyzes that the risk that the crisis between Russia and Ukraine could turn into a war is minimal because all parties are well aware that war is imminent. Uncontrollable risks.
In the end, why has the United States repeatedly inflated the threat that Russia will "invade" Ukraine? The first reason is that the United States is trying to expand Russia's "threat" to cause strategic tensions in Europe in a way that causes European countries, especially Eastern Europe and the former Soviet republics, to be more obedient.
Currently, the evolution of the Ukraine crisis seems to be an American theatrical performance that adds a series of scenes. But American tricks can not fool the world. America's insane performance will make the world see more clearly: the biggest security risk in the world is the United States, which is stuck both inside and outside the country, and knows how to use all these tricks.
