(Phnom Penh): Cambodia organized the first "Social Protection Week" with the theme "Towards the Development of a Social Protection System for All" co-organized by the National Council for Social Protection and the United Nations in Cambodia. . This "Social Protection Week" takes place for 3 days, from 15 to 17 February 2022.
The organization of the Cambodian Social Protection Week is aimed at raising awareness and importance of the social protection system in Cambodia, disseminating new achievements and providing opportunities and forums for stakeholders to discuss work. Promote the development of the social protection system in Cambodia to another level, both in terms of policy level and technical level.
"During the 19 epidemic of Kovid, all social protection programs and programs will be implemented without fail," he said. Currently, the government spends more than $ 30 million a month to implement this social assistance program.
"Social Protection Week" is a day held in many countries around the world to strengthen the awareness and importance of each country's social protection programs and policies to contribute to the well-being of the general population through Improving the living standards of the people, especially the poor and vulnerable, as well as promoting economic growth in an equitable and sustainable environment.
In addition to organizing this forum, the Royal Government has also established other working mechanisms in order to promote and enhance the principles of good governance in the social protection system to improve the implementation of social protection policy. Be transparent and accountable.
Under the good cooperation between relevant ministries and institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners, national and international organizations and relevant civil society organizations, Cambodia expects to further promote the development of its social protection system, which will contribute significantly to Build a harmonious society and promote sustainable economic growth, environment and equity in line with the Royal Government's poverty reduction policy.
