ADB approves $ 95 million loan to help Royal Government of Cambodia purchase 19 Kovid vaccines
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has approved a $ 95 million loan to assist the Royal Government of Cambodia in the process of vaccinating 19 people against measles from 2022 to 2023, including an annual booster shot for you. Vaccinated and basic immunizations for children under 5 years of age.
Cambodia has achieved great success in controlling the spread of Kovid 19 by 2020. But an outbreak in 2021 caused a major upheaval to the health care system and resulted in the closure of many schools and businesses that year.
Cambodia has fully vaccinated about 80% of the population of 16.7 million since the start of the national vaccination campaign on February 10, 2021. On average, more than one in five Cambodians, or 21.8%, received a booster dose.
The above project is an additional support for ADB-related assistance to Cambodia over the past 19 years. On July 8, 2020, the ADB provided a $ 250 million loan to help the government reduce the serious social, economic and economic impact of the epidemic. In addition, ADB will also provide about 1.7 million personal protective equipment to Cambodia in 2021.
