Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs clarifies the establishment of the National Internet Gateway after a series of misinterpretations by foreign media (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Spokesman of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia on 15 February This 2022 has issued a statement on the establishment of a national Internet gateway.
The statement by the Foreign Ministry spokesman came after a series of misinterpretations, especially by some foreign media, of the purpose of establishing a national Internet gateway in Cambodia.
"A spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation noted with frustration the continued misinterpretation by some foreign media about the purpose of the gate," a statement from Fresh News read: "The national internet in Cambodia, despite many explanations and clarifications by the competent authorities of Cambodia."
In order to further clarify these misconceptions, the spokesperson clarified the following notes on the issue:
The Royal Government, in order to facilitate and control the Internet connection and strengthen national security and tax collection, as well as maintain social order and protect national culture, established an inter-ministerial committee in 2019 on the establishment of a national Internet gateway to study and explore. Methods for establishing this essential mechanism.
The committee, through the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, a professional body, has launched a comprehensive study of infrastructure models from around the world and found that almost all countries have separate Internet portals and regulations. From each other.
The sub-decree on the National Internet Gateway, signed on 16 February 2021, was transparently prepared and consultations were held with experts in the field, private operators and relevant institutions. Many times.
The establishment of a national Internet gateway, which is common in almost every country around the world, acts as an effective tool to increase national revenue collection on the basis of transparent, equitable and honest competition between the state and telecom operators. In addition, it contributes to the prevention of cybercrime, such as illegal use of cross-border networks, illegal online gambling, and online fraud.
The mechanism does not have any provisions as alleged to allow the collection of user data and restrict freedom of expression. The government will separately draft a law on the protection of personal data once the draft law on cyber security is finalized.
Allegations that the establishment of a national Internet gateway allows the Cambodian authorities to monitor and monitor all online activities, seize and restrict digital communications, as well as collect, store and share personal data of users. Risks to the right to freedom of expression, including the right to seek, receive and share information and ideas, as well as the right to privacy, are baseless allegations.
On the contrary, the Royal Government respects the right to privacy and freedom of expression of individuals and protects personal data, all of which are enshrined in the Constitution, the International Covenant on Human Rights, ratified by the Civil Code, the Criminal Code and the Telecommunications Law.
Foreign Ministry announces results of video meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Norwegian Foreign Minister
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia on the afternoon of February 15, 2022, announced the results of the video meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Minister Anniken Huitfeldt. Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Norway held yesterday.
Regarding the situation in Myanmar, the two Foreign Ministers stressed the urgent need to mitigate this complex crisis, especially by accelerating the implementation of the five-point unanimous agreement reached at the ASEAN Leaders' Meeting on April 24, 2021.
Mr. Prak Sokhon briefed Ms. Anniken Huitfeldt on Cambodia's efforts as ASEAN Chair, including the recent visit to Myanmar by Prime Minister Hun Sen and Cambodia's next steps, and thanked Norway. Prepared for his presentation on Myanmar at the UN Security Council on January 28, 2022.
Regarding bilateral relations, Mr. Prak Sokhon reiterated Cambodia's gratitude to Norway, a country that has long been a supporter of Cambodia's demining goals and a key donor to the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
