Mr. Prach Chan: The NEC is ready to ensure the smooth and successful organization of Commune / Sangkat Council elections.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee, confirmed that the NEC has prepared and prepared the master plan, the work calendar and updated the regulations and procedures, as well as other legal documents to Ensure that the organization of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate 2022 runs smoothly and successfully.
This statement was made by the Chairman of the NEC in a meeting with stakeholders on 15 February 2022 with the aim of announcing the launch of the "Commune / Sangkat Council Election". 5 years 2022 "coming.
According to the law, commune council elections are held annually through universal suffrage. The date of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election shall be determined by the Prime Minister at least nine months before the election day at the request of the Minister of Interior.
As in the calendar of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, which has been distributed, from now until the election day, we have a lot of work to do with all stakeholders from Political parties, organizations, associations, journalists, relevant national institutions, including the people as voters. The work must be done in stages and have a clear start and end date.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Prach Chan summarized the following important work:
* First: Voter List Preparation
The NEC has just completed the preparation of the 2021 voter list, which started from September 12, 2021 until February 12, 2022, which was recently validated by the NEC. The official voter list for 2021. The official voter list for 2021 will be used for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, which will take place on Sunday, June 5, 2022.
* 2: Registration of political party candidates
In order to stand for the upcoming 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council elections, political parties registered in accordance with the Law on Political Parties must complete an application for registration of their candidates at the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission (CEC). From March 4 to 6, 2022.
* Third: Election Campaign
Campaigning refers to a number of public actions to persuade voters to support a candidate or political party. Campaign activities must be carried out responsibly, with dignity, security, safety, order, and in coordination with the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission (CEC) and local authorities. The election campaign period is 14 days from May 21 to June 3, 2022.
* Fourth: Voting and vote counting
As mentioned earlier, the date of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election is to be held on Sunday, June 05, 2022. On election day, polling stations are open at 7:00 am and end at 3:00 pm. After the polls close, the polling station shall become a polling station.
Pursuant to Article 123 of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election Law (CEC), the counting of ballots shall take place at each polling station in the Commune / Sangkat after the closing of the election and the exclusion of election records. However, any polling station could not count the ballots at its polling station due to the case of the president or the insecurity and the NEC decided to have the NEC conduct the counting of ballots at the NEC office or somewhere. Which is safe.
* 5th: Announcement of election results
The election results are prepared and announced in three stages:
B: Operation to monitor and summarize the provisional results of the commune elections
Agents of political parties and stakeholders can also monitor the verification process and summarize the results. The inspection, including the resolution of the complaint or objection, shall not exceed 5 days from the date of receipt of the "Special C package and C bag" of the relevant commune. After the verification, the NEC shall send the provisional results to the NEC.
* C: Review of election results and announcement of election results
