The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) may begin discussions on a roadmap and timeline for Timor-Leste to join in the first quarter of 2022. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News.
Timor-Leste's application for ASEAN membership was discussed by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, with Mr. LIM Jock Hoi, Secretary-General of ASEAN, in a video conference on 14 February 2022. .
Cambodia has been at the forefront of supporting Timor-Leste to become a member of ASEAN. In order to become a member of ASEAN, Timor-Leste has also made efforts by establishing diplomacy to strengthen relations in all ASEAN member countries, despite its limited resources.
In the past, fact-finding missions in Timor-Leste on the political-security pillar have been completed, leaving only the economic and cultural pillars due to the Kovid-19 pandemic.
Please be informed that ASEAN was established on August 08, 1967, 53 years ago. If Timor-Leste could become a member of ASEAN, Timor-Leste would become the 11th member of the 10-nation bloc.
Since 2007, Timor-Leste has shown its efforts to become the 11th member of ASEAN, and in fact, the official application for membership was made in 2011, while Cambodia is determined to support This country.
