(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance, the staff of the Royal Government, on February 14, 2022, announced the release of 100 million dollars to two state-owned banks to help promote agriculture and small and medium enterprises. .
Through this special financing program, enterprises in the agricultural and agro-industrial sectors are able to strengthen their businesses and improve their production chains in order to strengthen competitiveness, maintain food security and boost exports in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis. .
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that the Cambodian government prioritizes the development of small and medium enterprises, especially enterprises in key sectors such as agriculture, agro-industry, food processing, manufacturing, assembly and tourism. An important policy.
The Deputy Prime Minister added that small and medium enterprises not only contribute to supporting Cambodia's economic growth and job creation, but also play an important role in increasing the resilience of the national economy to the crisis. In fact, small and medium enterprises account for about 98% of all businesses in Cambodia and contribute about 58% of GDP and employ about 73% of the total labor force in Cambodia.
