(Svay Rieng): Police in Rumduol district, Svay Rieng province, arrested a private doctor for questioning on the case of an injection that caused a boy to have seizures, bite his tongue and burst into tears, and died immediately on the spot.
The private doctor who was detained by the police is named Vat Chanthan, 36 years old, a doctor living in Kandal village, Svay Chek commune, Romduol district. The victim was a 7-year-old boy named Chiek Nadeth, a student living in Thmey Village, Svay Chek Commune, Romduol District.
Dr. Chea Sophoan, Executive Director of Svay Teap and Romduol districts, confirmed to Fresh News Agency in Svay Rieng province this morning, February 14, 2022, that the doctor was arrested by the Romduol district police force. 12:35, 12 February 2022 at Kandal village, Svay Chek commune, Romduol district, after injecting a boy to death.
He said the private doctor had a valid permit from the provincial health department to open a care and treatment room, which expired in 2023, and that the child had a fever and was being treated with paracetamol and paracetamol. Silen suspected drug reaction caused the boy to die.
According to the Romduol district police, while the man, a private doctor, had removed the needle, the child suddenly had seizures, bit his tongue, and burst into bubbles, causing his sudden death, much to the surprise of his family.
After examining the body, the police made a note and handed it over to the family for the traditional ceremony. The suspect was detained at the Romduol District Police Inspectorate to proceed with legal proceedings.
