Samdech Techo Hun Sen leads a delegation back to Cambodia, bringing great pride for the nation and people of Cambodia (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at around 8 pm on Sunday, February 13. This 2022 led the delegation back from South Korea to Cambodia safely, bringing with great pride for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation from Cambodia to visit and attend the World Peace Summit in Seoul, South Korea on February 10, 2022.
The 8th Visit to South Korea After Cambodia and South Korea formally established diplomatic ties in 1997, in addition to the visit, Samdech Techo was co-chaired the World Summit this year. 2022 on Peace on the Korean Peninsula with Ban Ki-moon, former UN Secretary-General and Dr. Hak Jahan-moon, Co-Founder of the Global Peace Federation (UPF).
Samdech Techo shared Cambodia's experience in finding peace, building peace and national reconciliation, emphasizing that war cannot end war, so he reaffirmed the importance of peaceful dialogue and win-win negotiations. End the war.
After extensive discussion on 13 February, the Summit unanimously adopted two outcome documents: "Seoul Resolution 2022: Towards Peace and Sustainable Prosperity on the Korean Peninsula" and the Initiative Samdech Techo Prime Minister on "Two States Towards One Nation: One Peninsula, One People, One Culture".
In addition to co-chairing the World Summit on Peace, during his visit, the Prime Minister also met with South Korean President Moon Jae-in, Parliament Speaker Park Geun-hye, and Ban Ki-moon. Former UN Secretary-General Kim Jong Un and Dr. Hak Jahan Moon, Co-Founder of UPF.
The Prime Minister also received the Sunhak Peace Prize 2022 at the Sunhak Peace Award Ceremony.
The handing over of the 2022 Sun Hak Peace Prize to Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a historic event for Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen receiving the 2022 Sun Hak Peace Prize, an international award for individuals who have won Sacrifice your life for the cause of peace and inspire mankind to seek world peace.
In the ceremony of honor and pride for the whole nation of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his heartfelt tears to commemorate the bitter journey of life, losing a wife, losing a child, hugging a child, not knowing a father in the cause of the motherland. Civil war crisis.
On that forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his deep appreciation for peace. Samdech Techo said that there is no peace, no hope. No peace, no development. No peace, no respect for human rights and no democracy.
According to Mr. Sous Yara, a Cambodian Member of Parliament who participated in the program, Samdech Techo's speech at the award ceremony not only moved the Cambodian people but also made the participants in the program. Very emotional, too.
National leaders, civil servants, the armed forces, students and people from all walks of life expressed their joy and happiness for the honor that Samdech Techo received and brought to the nation of Cambodia. They considered that the honor that Samdech Techo received now was most worthy of his great efforts and sacrifices for the nation and the people of Cambodia. Russia continues to find more than 197,949 new Kovid cases per day
