Understand the business: Experts on the proper use of credit and encourage regular consultations with banking or microfinance institutions (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Microfinance expert Mr. Soeung Simon, CEO The General Manager of Sambath Finan Microfinance Institution has been informed about the proper use of credit and encouraged to seek advice from the bank and regularly because counseling is necessary.
Mr. Soeung Simon emphasized that when it comes to using credit, it is very important because most of the customers fail is using credit incorrectly and do not dare to seek advice from the bank. The customer needs to carry out the credit, what the customer needs to use is to use what is requested by the bank.
Mr. Soeung Simon said that customers should use as requested, if not used as requested, he can ask for advice from the bank again. And do not use what we want, we have to think about the impact and ask for advice from the bank regularly, because counseling is very necessary.
For Kaing Tong Ngy, a spokesman for the Microfinance Association, the key to clients' success in using credit is having a good balance in managing their money, and on the contrary, unsuccessful clients generally do not have it. Clear habits in managing money, including not being able to save.
As a guide, Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy encourages clients who use loans successfully, please consult with the bank or microfinance by providing information about its reality, the bank or microfinance will provide suggestions that help clients grow. .
At the same time, Mr. Soeung Simon mentioned five factors that borrowers face failure, including:
Factor 1: Credit users provide some information to financial institutions that are not transparent (inaccurate), sometimes withholding information or may expand their income to obtain large amounts of credit.
Factor 2: The client does not dare to take advice from banking and financial institutions what he is facing.
Factor 3: Some clients, when difficult, do not dare to seek advice by running to the private sector (private lenders) to solve the problem of high interest rates increase debt.
Factor 4: Customers do not have a business sustainability plan and income is uncertain. In addition, without reserves to deal with financial crises.
Factor 5: Most start-ups come from the younger generation, starting with a desire and not having a full analysis and starting a big business beyond their capabilities.
