The following is the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The Ministry of Environment is committed to achieving carbon neutrality by 2050 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on the morning of February 13, 2022 shows a short video clip that An aerial view of the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary while Minister of Environment Say Sam Al and his team travel by helicopter to view the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary.
Prey Lang covers an area of 431,683 hectares, covering four provinces: Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom.
The Ministry of Environment said that with the improvement of protection and conservation of natural resources, Cambodia has sold credit on the voluntary market in the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary and the Cardamom Mountains. Cambodia is also implementing a carbon credit project at the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng province and has been preparing procedures for the sale of carbon credits in other areas.
Other wildlife sanctuaries in Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri Stung Treng provinces are in the process of preparing to sell carbon credits to international markets. According to the ministry, from 2016 to 2020, Cambodia received $ 11.6 million from the sale of carbon credits.
Companies have decided to buy carbon credits from Cambodia because Cambodia has better protected its forests, with measures to conserve and conserve natural resources more effectively, despite some challenges. Cambodia has set the direction of "maintaining standing trees for income", which includes the sale of carbon credits and eco-tourism.
At the same time, Cambodia is committed to halving deforestation by 2030 and achieving zero emissions in the forestry sector by 2040.
The Ministry of Environment said that the carbon-neutral long-term development strategy was approved and submitted to the Secretariat of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) on December 30, 2021.
The submission of this strategy is in line with the commitment of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the "United Nations Climate Ambition" Summit in December 2020 to launch this strategy by the end of the year. 2021.
This strategy is an important step for Cambodia as a country to support multilateral action in climate change to achieve carbon neutrality by 2050, based on the principle of "shared responsibility but different levels based on individual capabilities." Under the UNFCCC.
BREAKING: Ministry of Health issues guidelines to strengthen the implementation of standard procedures for the management, care and treatment of Kovid 19 at home
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on the morning of February 13, 2022, issued a directive on strengthening the implementation of standard procedures for the management, care and treatment of 19 Kovid disease at home. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News.
Kovid-19 positives are required to stay in a clean, well-ventilated area with their windows wide open and must report to local authorities in their area of residence.
* Maintain personal hygiene by implementing 3 protective measures (wear a mask, wash hands frequently, keep a personal safety distance of more than one and a half meters) and do not touch or use items or bathrooms with family members. Separate personal items are essential and must not be carried out indefinitely, even for short periods of time, to avoid transmission of the Kovid-19 virus to family members and to others.
* Continue to implement 3 preventive measures and 3 non-thorough measures, even during or after treatment, in order to prevent the spread of code-19 virus.
* Patient waste should be stored tightly packed and set aside and follow the instructions of the local authority or medical team in the area where you live to avoid contamination.
* Please refer to the instructions dated January 21, 2022 to make the practice of home treatment appropriate and responsible for patients and their families. If you do not follow the instructions correctly, you may face the implementation of legal measures in force in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
All local authorities and sub-national administrations must thoroughly monitor the implementation of standard operating procedures for the management, care and treatment of KVD-19 patients in this home and take appropriate action in accordance with the law.
The Ministry of Health states that, in receiving this instruction, all citizens are kindly requested to participate in effective implementation to ensure that the home treatment is correct and completed safely, as well as to avoid transmission of Kovid-19 virus to family members and to you. Others in the community.
