(Svay Rieng): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, on the morning of February 12, 2022, disseminated the contents of the 29th General Assembly of Monks in Svay Rieng Province. There was the participation of Preah Mekun, Preah Anukon, officials, monks and Preah Thera-Nuth Thera, as well as leaders and local authorities at all levels.
She also mentioned the role of monks in Cambodian society today, as a supporter of culture, literature, religion, tradition and as a helper to orphans, homeless people. On the other hand, Khmer Buddhist monks are representative of purity in society, role models in behavior, morality, society and society.
She added that Cambodian Buddhist monks from generation to generation have shown their prestige and ability in the international arena. In fact, on February 11, 2022, the Cambodian monks were recently welcomed and given a great honor to deliver a speech on the road to world peace in Korea, a national pride of Khmer history. Invaluable in the history of the Techo era.
In order to contribute to the dissemination of the contents of the 29th National Congress of Priests in Svay Rieng Province, Ms. Kittisangha Bandith provided six recommendations:
* First, monks at all levels must strictly abide by the provisions of the Constitution. Existing laws and regulations, such as the Royal Decree, the Royal Kram, the Sub-Decree, the Prakas, the Declaration, the Decision, and the NCC of the Office of the Council of Ministers - must also be strictly enforced to become an important driving force for the promotion of God. Buddhism to be stronger and better.
* Second, monks at all levels must cooperate better in accordance with the rules and regulations in order to strengthen the unity and solidarity in Buddhist institutions as a good example for Buddhists and contribute to moral education to society.
* Third: Monks at all levels must maintain better cooperation with the provincial Department of Cults and Religions, authorities at all levels to work together to achieve better results with mutual understanding and tolerance. .
* Fourth: The Provincial Department of Cult and Religion and the Provincial Council must pay attention to strengthen the quality of Buddhist schools at all levels to become a training ground for Dharma, Pali, Sanskrit, general knowledge and a good professional skills in the society.
* Fifth, the Provincial Department of Cult and Religion and the Provincial Hall must pay attention to strengthen the work of pagoda administration and spread the Dharma by various means to help Buddhists to do good deeds, adhere to social truth and avoid all kinds of sins.
* Sixth: All Buddhist monks and nuns must be vigilant and prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus into the community, especially the Omega type, which currently has a high infection rate in the world, including in Cambodia. The number of copies has been increasing day by day.
