Samdech Techo Hun Sen shares his personal experience of decades of civil war in Cambodia during the 2022 Sun Hak Peace Prize in South Korea (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Shared Samdech's personal experience of growing and progressing through decades of civil war in Cambodia.
The sharing of experiences took place on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen receiving the "Peace Sun Hak" Award, which was held at the Global Arts Center in Seoul, South Korea on the morning of February 12. This year 2022.
Samdech Techo described that he was forced to drop out of school in 1970, when Cambodia had been severely divided and war had erupted. Samdech's childhood and adolescence, which should have been happy if the country was peaceful, but Samdech suffered only hardships and pain.
"At that time, I was very desperate for my future and the future of my country," he said. Since then, I have sacrificed my life to seek peace for my country, Cambodia. "It took me almost three decades to achieve my dream, as I had to endure all the hardships, including risking my life, in this peace-building process."
Samdech Techo was injured and lost one eye. Samdech was forced to flee on foot to Vietnam in the middle of the night, crossing mines and crossing borders with large numbers of troops. Moreover, Samdech left his wife at Kandoch Kandeng, where Samdech Kittipritthbandit was pregnant in Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia has maintained peace for more than 20 years. At the same time, we are committed to further safeguarding and promoting peace.
"Through Cambodia's experience of going through war and building peace, I would like to emphasize that there is no peace, no hope. No peace, no development. "There is no peace, no respect for human rights and no democracy."
Samdech Techo agreed with the views of Mr. Sun Myung Moon and Dr. Hak Jahan Moon, who stated that "peace is a practical action, not a vague dream."
"This is why my government has made peace a high priority, sending thousands of Cambodian troops to participate in UN peacekeeping and demining operations in Africa and the Middle East, hoping to be able to do so," he said. "Contribute to the restoration of peace in those areas."
He added that even though Cambodia is small, Cambodia has contributed to the process of finding peace in the region and the world with goodwill, responsibility and honesty.
