Ministry of Economy: Auction mechanism for importing live pigs supplied to Cambodia, designed to protect both local breeders and pork eaters
(Phnom Penh): In order to ensure clear understanding and avoid confusion about the purpose of the initiative to organize a tender mechanism for importing live pigs to supply to Cambodia among the public, the Ministry of Economy and Finance on 11 February 2022. Issued a press release explaining clearly that the auction mechanism for importing live pigs supplied to Cambodia is designed to protect both breeders and consumers (pork eaters).
A press release obtained by Fresh News stated that the auction mechanism for importing live pigs supplied to Cambodia will be implemented only in case of shortage of pigs. In principle, the government always encourages local farmers to be able to supply enough pigs with reasonable prices without importation.
If there is a need for imports to meet domestic demand as well as keep pork prices at a reasonable level, this mechanism will rely on the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, which is the institution in (1): set quotas on quantities. Import, (2): Determine the qualifications of the importing company, and (3): Make bidding transparently.
In general, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries is the body responsible for determining the number of live pigs to be imported to meet market demand only when necessary. At the same time, the bidding mechanism is to attract more companies to participate in the auction of live pig imports to increase competition and ensure the supply of live pigs at a reasonable price.
With the Ministry of Economy and Finance, we sincerely hope that the media, the Breeders Association and the general public will have a clear understanding of the content and purpose of the initiative to organize a tender mechanism to import live pigs for supply to Cambodia.
Air Force Doctors Vaccinate Third Dose in Kampong Leng
(Kampong Chhnang): General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Air Force, has ordered a team of 31 Air Force doctors and medical assistants to travel to Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province to be vaccinated. To the people.
On February 10, 2022, General Soeng Samnang, together with Lt. Gen. Kong Mony, Deputy Commander, Lt. Gen. Yin Sokha, Deputy Commander, inspected the process of vaccinating the third dose to the people in Trangel commune. Po, Svay Rompear commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province.
General Soeng Samnang emphasized that based on the high-level remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to expedite the vaccination of the people, he also sent a team of Air Force doctors to vaccinate. People in Kampong Leng district, a remote area.
General Soeng Samnang said that the army doctors are working hard and working hard to get the people to be vaccinated against Kovid 19. According to Soeng Samnang, from the 9th to the 10th of February, 2,916 people have been vaccinated against the third dose. Air Force medics administered the AstraZeneca and Sinovac vaccines.
According to the observation, the people are very active, especially the elderly people over the age of 70, who came to get vaccinated with great joy. General Soeng Samnang instructed the vaccination team to prepare the vaccination site with good air and to always implement the measures of the Ministry of Health and the measures of Samdech Techo "3 protect and 3 do not".
General Soeng Samnang talked with local authorities in villages and communes to call on all people to get the third dose of vaccine to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 type omega virus that continues to spread in our community. And must implement the measures "3 protection and 3 do not" of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at all times.
General Soeng Samnang provided funds to the vaccinators working there. Afterwards, the Commander-in-Chief of the Air Force and the Air Force team inspected the construction process of a paved road in the area, which will be completed soon to facilitate the construction. Travel of people and improve their lives.
