Cambodia and South Korea in 2021 decided to sign a free trade agreement together. Currently, the Cambodian side has already prepared the draft law on free trade, with the South Korean side still in the hands of the National Assembly. It is necessary to wait for the enactment of this law before free trade between Cambodia and South Korea can work.
Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during his visit to South Korea on February 11, 2022, requested South Korean President Moon Jae-in and South Korean Parliament Speaker Park Byeong-Seung to expedite Procedures for the entry into force of this draft law and pave the way for free trade with Cambodia.
