Cambodia officially launches "Carbon Neutral Development Strategy for Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian government, headed by the Ministry of Environment, on the afternoon of February 11, 2022, officially announced the launch of the "Long-Term Development Strategy with Carbon Neutrality in Cambodia".
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Mr. Say Sam Al, Chairman of the National Council for Sustainability and Minister of Environment, and was attended by a number of stakeholders.
The development of a carbon-neutral long-term development strategy (LTS4CN) is a testament to the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to the Paris Agreement on Climate Change and presents a policy scenario to achieve its vision. A carbon neutral and resilient society for the next 30 years.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that on December 30, 2021, Cambodia expressed its commitment announced by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the United Nations Summit on Climate Ambition. Our long-term carbon neutral development strategy before the end of 2021.
"We are the second least developed country in the world and the second in ASEAN to set out this strategy with a 2050 target for zero emissions," he said.
