Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks South Korean President to Accelerate ratification of Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement (Video inside) (Korea) The President of the Republic of Korea (ROK) urges the speedy ratification of the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request was made during the meeting with Mr. Moon Jae-in during his visit to the Republic of Korea and to co-chair the 2022 World Peace Summit under the theme "Towards Peace in "Korean Peninsula."
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, stated that in this meeting, Samdech Techo also emphasized that Cambodia has now completed the internal procedures related to the free trade agreement between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea. He asked the Korean side to expedite the ratification of the free market agreement between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the President to support Cambodia's industry, especially in relation to a number of reforms, highlighting Cambodia's new investment law that encourages foreign investors.
Samdech Techo also asked the President of South Korea to support the formula 1 plus means that if Korea invests in Vietnam, Thailand can also come to invest or open a factory in Cambodia. He also asked Korea to provide support and cooperation, especially in the fields of agro-industry and processing, especially other agricultural products, for export to the Republic of Korea and third countries.
At the same time, Samdech Techo mentioned good opportunities for investment, especially through the new investment law of Cambodia. Samdech asked the President to encourage more Korean investors to come to Cambodia.
In response, President Moon Jae-in said that regarding the free trade agreement between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, Korea has completed the procedure and is sending it to the Korean National Assembly for ratification, which is expected to be completed in the near future. This face.
For this 2022 meeting, he congratulated Cambodia on its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. With regard to the new investment law with Cambodia, he hopes to work together, stating that there are about 300 Korean companies operating in Cambodia.
It should be noted that the Law on the Approval of the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and South Korea was signed by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on January 29, 2022. Previously, after passing the examination from the National Assembly and the Senate.
A free trade agreement between Cambodia and South Korea was discussed and drafted by the two countries' expert working group in 2021. The agreement was officially signed via video by Cambodian Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak and Commerce Minister of the Republic of Korea YEO Han-Koo on October 26, 2021.
The agreement will boost exports, increase gross domestic product and increase employment opportunities, and help speed up the recovery of the two economies affected by Kovid-19 by expanding liberalization. Markets in addition to the ASEAN-Korea Free Trade Agreement (AKFTA) and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
The agreement will further boost Cambodia's exports to the Republic of Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
