NBC official: The microfinance sector plays an important role in contributing to the economic and social development of Cambodia, especially reducing poverty in rural areas.
(Kratie): Mr. Men Pheakdey, Director of the Data Management and Macro Analysis Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, highlighted the importance of the microfinance sector, which has contributed significantly to the economic and social development of Cambodia, especially in reducing poverty. People living in rural areas.
Mr. Men Pheakdey made this remark on the occasion of the National Bank of Cambodia disseminating knowledge on "Microfinance in Cambodia" in Sambo District, Kratie Province on 11 February 2022.
Mr. Men Pheakdey stated that despite the difficulties caused by the spread of Kovid-19 disease, the micro-sector operations in Cambodia are still operating and operating responsibly. In fact, as of 2021, microfinance institutions, deposit-taking microfinance institutions and credit institutions are still operating throughout the country.
He added that during the period affected by Kovid 19, banks and financial institutions also reorganized loans to protect their customers.
In addition, Mr. Suon Pisey, President of the Operations Club of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, said that in 2021, the number of loans reorganized was 370,785 accounts, equivalent to $ 5.49 billion.
Mr. Men Pheakdey expressed his pride in the microfinance sector that despite the Kovid crisis, the sector has maintained its growth and continues to play an important role in contributing to the recovery and further development of the Cambodian economy in the context of living in a normal way. New.
He said that in order to strengthen the important role of the microfinance sector, the National Bank has carried out various activities and campaigns aimed at raising financial literacy to the public, promoting responsible lending and strengthening lending principles. Professional ethics. With this, he requested to help promote and educate people to borrow money from legal institutions, as well as use the loan to target and comply with obligations.
