(Phnom Penh): At the office of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on the afternoon of February 10, 2022, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, met with Mr. Hassan Zaman, Permanent Secretary. World Bank East Asia and Pacific (WB) Visiting Cambodia
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister also reminded of the good and strong cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the WB over the past two decades, which shows the importance of the partnership between the WB. In the past development process of Cambodia.
The Minister also said that the Cambodian economy is currently in a recovery phase to push the economy on the path of rapid growth, resilience and environment. Meanwhile, the regional and global situation is changing rapidly.
He said that in this context, Cambodia's progress towards achieving its ambitions as a high-middle-income country by 2030 will certainly face many challenges, however, Cambodia will be able to Yes. This requires a double effort by developing new policies and strategies.
In this regard, the Delegation requested the WB to continue to work with Cambodia in partnership to jointly review and update the financing program, as well as to provide some necessary technical assistance to adapt to Cambodia's priorities in the context. New as well as the region and the world in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis.
Mr. Hassan Zaman expressed his pleasure to pay a personal visit to Cambodia and praised the Royal Government of Cambodia's decision to reopen the country, making Cambodia the first country in the region to do so. Open borders open to outsiders, while many other countries still impose restrictions.
At the same time, he also mentioned the improvement of the macroeconomic situation of Cambodia. The regional director also said that these successes and achievements are not coincidental, but this is really due to the efforts and leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which will be the foundation. Strong for Cambodia's continued progress.
In response, Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that Cambodia is currently living with Kovid-19 and has fully reopened the country in all areas without going back.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a strategic framework and program to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth in living with Kovid-19 along the new normal path 2021-2023, which is based on three approaches, including:
* Second: Reform through the continued introduction of key structural reform measures aimed at building a solid foundation for growth, diversification and competitiveness.
