North Korea Condemns EU for Criticizing Its Missile Test (Video inside) (Seoul): North Korea condemned the European Union for criticizing its missile test in January, calling it Interference in Pyongyang's internal affairs. This was released by Yonhap News Agency on Friday, February 11, 2022.
"We strongly condemn and reject any interference in the internal affairs and sovereignty of our country," the North Korean Foreign Ministry said in a statement posted on its website on Thursday. "Increasing our defense capabilities does not pose any threat or damage to neighboring countries and the region as a whole."
In January, North Korea test-fired seven missiles, including medium-range missiles, which are banned by the UN Security Council. A series of missile tests are raising concerns that North Korea may test nuclear and intercontinental ballistic missiles (ICBMs) soon after failing since 2017.
