The United States, Australia, Japan and India on Friday pledged to jointly defend the Indo-Pacific freedoms from threats in the face of China's growing military and economic influence. This was released by Reuters on Friday evening, February 11, 2022.
The four foreign ministers of the four countries (Quad) are committed to working together on humanitarian aid, counter-terrorism, cyber security, as well as protecting the freedom of navigation and resolving issues. Face the global supply chain as well.
Mr Blinken stressed in front of his Australian, Indian and Japanese counterparts: "This includes defending the right of all nations to choose the path they want to take without coercion, and their rights. "To have the sovereignty and territorial integrity respected."
