(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association has elected a new President and Vice President to lead the association for the new mandate 2022 to 2023.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chief Executive Officer of LOLC Microfinance Institution (LOLC), with over 20 years of experience in the field of microfinance and banking, has been elected Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia (CMA) for a mandate. From 2022 to 2023, Ms. Dith Nita, CEO of Khema Microfinance Institution (CAMMA), was elected as the Vice Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association.
This election was held at the 16th Annual General Meeting of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia at the Phnom Penh Hotel on 11 February 2021, with the participation of more than 100 members.
Eleven other candidates, all of whom are leaders of major financial institutions, have also been elected to the association's board of directors for the 2022-2023 term.
