Construction of Drainage System and Wastewater Treatment Plant in Serei Sophorn City with $ 22 Million Under ADB Loan Launched
(Banteay Meanchey): The construction of sewerage system and wastewater treatment plant in Serei Sophorn City under the loan from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) was held this morning, February 11, 2022.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Vong Piseth, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Chey, Mr. Sok Chantha, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Hul Raya, Governor of Serey Sophorn and many more. Well.
One administrative building, one workshop building, one generator and one security building are located in the wastewater treatment plant. 6.8 km long, equipped with operation and maintenance equipment.
He added that the construction of sewer system and wastewater treatment plant in Serei Sophorn City is scheduled for 3 years from September 2021 to August 2024. The contractor must provide training to staff to operate and maintain. This is 6 months from the completion date of construction.
At the same time, Mr. Vong Piseth confirmed that the wastewater treatment plant has a filtering capacity of 3,500 meters per day, built on an area of about 4 hectares, including 4 buildings, including administrative buildings, workshops, generators. The security building is located in Kantuot Village, Sangkat Phneat, Serey Sophorn City.
Construction of sewer system and wastewater treatment station for the service area northwest of Stung Serey Sophorn with 110 km of pipeline and 1 main pumping station and 3 small pumping stations as well as commercial home network connection 3,779 other institutional buildings. The project will build a 2,500-meter access road to the treatment plant and a 6,885-meter rainwater drainage network.
