(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC) and IOM on the morning of 11 February 2022 held a National Workshop on National Planning for the Implementation of the Global Convention on Migration. Safe, orderly and legal at Cambodiana Hotel.
The workshop was chaired by Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC) and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, with the participation of representatives from relevant ministries, institutions, partner organizations and technical officials. Some more.
The objectives of this workshop include:
1. To present to the participating representatives of the Ministry / General Department about the position of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the implementation of the World Covenant on Migration by developing a national plan for presentation at the International Forum on Migration in 2022.
2: To support the Ministry / General Department in developing a national plan for the implementation of the World Convention on Migration through: * Small group workshops to inspire the implementation of the draft plan * Presentation of each draft plan Of the Ministry / General Department * Development of a National Plan for the Implementation of the World Covenant.
On that occasion, Ms. Chou Bun Eng stated that the importance of this workshop is to prepare a draft plan for the implementation of the World Covenant on safe, orderly and legal migration.
She added that this pact is important because Cambodia has been involved in building this pact since 2017. Cambodia then ratified the Covenant in Morocco on December 10, 2018.
