(Phnom Penh): The Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on Friday, February 11, 2022, organized an internal training workshop for the Deputy Prosecutor, the Prosecutor, and the Secretariat under the theme "The role of the prosecutor in investigating and prosecuting crimes." Money.
The workshop was conducted by the Technical Working Group to coordinate the processing of cases related to money laundering and IT crimes under the chairmanship of Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The purpose of this workshop is to support the national policies and strategies set by the Royal Government of Cambodia, together with the measures of the Ministry of Justice in the fight against money laundering and terrorist financing, to protect the financial institutions and the national economy from The effects of money laundering and terrorist financing will boost the effectiveness of investigative growth, as well as money laundering charges.
In order to achieve the above objectives and to respond to the growing number of money laundering cases, as well as the complexity of the investigation and prosecution of money laundering offenses, which are risk offenses, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has organized an internal training workshop. In order to further strengthen and increase the technical capacity of the investigation, collect evidence and decide to open criminal charges and money laundering.
In addition, Mr. Chreng Khmao praised and appreciated the efforts of the Deputy Prosecutor, the clerk and all officials, especially the technical team to coordinate the process of cases related to money laundering and cybercrime, both the prosecution and the judiciary. Who has worked hard in the past with a high sense of responsibility and a proactive attitude in the fight against money laundering.
In addition, Mr. Chreng Khmao also encouraged and encouraged the Deputy Prosecutor, Clerk and all officials who participated in this training workshop to participate with high attention and raise questions to discuss the issue. Challenges in the implementation of the task to be able to find an effective joint mechanism can solve the implementation of the task more effectively.
It should be noted that from 2017 until now, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Prosecutor's Office have handled cases related to money laundering offenses (including charges, detention, freezing and confiscation of property). A total of more than 40 cases, with the decision to freeze and confiscate, which the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has decided to charge about 10 million US dollars.
