(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on February 10, 2022, chaired a meeting of the Technical Working Group of the Ministry to inspect the construction of Thmor Da International Border Crossing in Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province. Border with Trat Province, Thailand to open this international border crossing and increase trade and tourism cooperation between the two countries.
The Thmar Da border crossing has been becoming an attractive area after the Royal Government of Cambodia built National Road 55 connecting the provincial town to that area. In particular, this area is highly favorable for a natural tourism that has been enticing tourists to visit. Nowadays, Cambodians in the area often cross into Thailand through this port to exchange goods.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the study and inspection was aimed at opening the international border between Cambodia and Thailand to increase trade and tourism cooperation between the two countries, as well as to meet the aspirations of the people. People in the western provinces of the country and investors are looking forward to seeing this port turn into an international port soon.
