(Phnom Penh): A commune chief in Oddar Meanchey province, who has been in office for more than 10 years, has claimed that his local land disputes and domestic violence cases have never been sent to court, always settled at the commune hall. Just because he does not want people to go to court.
Mr. Van Pek, Chief of Kork Khpos Commune, in the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit under the theme "Local Progress of Commune / Sangkat and the Future Direction of Oddar Meanchey Province" said that To the court, even the people themselves do not want that, because they all know that when they go to court, no one benefits.
The chief of Kork Khpos commune, Banteay Ampil district, said, “The people of my commune are very afraid of going to court to mediate, so they can solve it effectively. I did not work as a commune chief for 10 years, equal to two terms, related to domestic violence, land disputes, I never sent to court.
According to Van Peck, the method he used to solve the problem at the grassroots level focused on religious sins, as some people did not have a clear understanding of state law, meaning that only religious methods could solve the problem without a winner. There are no losers and the people are happy to accept it without losing anything.
He added that in the past, there was a case of violence that was not resolved at the commune hall and sent to the district level for further resolution and then ended at the district level.
