According to the official Facebook page of the Russey Keo district administration, in addition to detaining the illegal Vietnamese voter registrar, 23-year-old Sophanna Socheata and 23-year-old Yun Thearen, the Khan Administrative Unity Force Found and confiscated evidence related to some other crimes, such as ballot papers, ballot papers, pens, ballot papers and 50,000 Riels to send to the district police inspectorate to continue the procedure.
The Ministry of Health thanks the Fresh Holo Foundation for its contribution to reducing eye problems and blindness in Cambodia.
Dr. Youk Sambath welcomed the presence of the President, CEO and colleagues and appreciated the support for the Fred Holo Foundation's National Eye Health Program.
She thanked the Fred Hollow Foundation for its contribution to the reduction of eye problems and blindness of the Cambodian people, as well as the contribution to improving the well-being of the Cambodian people.
Representatives of the organization highlighted that from July 2021 to December 2024, it has set goals to complete 16 humanitarian missions in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Prey Veng, Siem Reap, Kampong Cham, Kampong Speu, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Thom, Kampot, Kampong Chhnang, Svay Rieng, Kratie, Sihanoukville, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Ratanakkiri. With a total budget of approximately 5,850,727 US dollars.
He highlighted key activities, including:
* 1: Improving access to high quality image correction and correction services, especially for women, the poor and the vulnerable.
* 2: Strengthen the capacity and efficiency of human resources in the field of eye health and expand service locations to remote areas.
* 3: Towards an eye health system that is accountable, efficient and sustainable.
* 4: Improve eye health results by improving the quality of cataract surgery services, image correction services.
The representative of the organization respectfully requested the support of the Ministry of Health in implementing this project.
In response, Dr. Youk Sambath thanked the organization and the FetHolo Foundation for their continued support of the National Eye Health Program.
