(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of presiding over the meeting to review the results of Customs and Excise 2021 at the National Customs Hall on February 10, 2022, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance 8 new recommendations to help increase the work efficiency for 2022 of the Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia to be more effective.
The meeting was also attended by the leadership of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, General Department of Taxation, General Department of Internal Audit, General Department of Policy, General Department of Budget, as well as direct and remote participation via video (Zoom) of the class. Lead at all levels of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia (Akor).
Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, made a report on the performance of Customs and Excise in 2021, stating that Customs collected 9,295.7 billion Riels (equivalent to about 2, 295.2 million US dollars), a decrease of about 5.1% compared to revenue collected in 2020. This resulted in 97.1% of the plan set by the Financial Law for 2021 management.
In response to the above results, Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth also highly appreciated the efforts of the management and customs and excise officials at all levels to achieve better results in all workplaces, despite the high risk of disease spread. Kovid-19 and expressed his full support to the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia for the implementation of the work in the following years.
At the same time, Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth also reminded the high guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen 5 points stated at the inauguration ceremony of the Customs Administration Building, the National Customs Hall and the Customs Museum on the 23rd. December 2021 includes:
* First, to further promote the dissemination of all stakeholders, especially the private sector, all provisions, laws and regulations to increase awareness and participation of all stakeholders in the implementation of fiscal obligations and law enforcement; and Provisions in force.
* Second: Continue to implement more effectively the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023 and the public financial management reform program, especially through the development of leadership, increase the will to implement the reform, strengthening. Ownership and care to strengthen the capacity of human resources and the use of information and communication technology systems.
Third, to continuously strengthen and improve the implementation of trade facilitation support mechanisms such as customs automation system, risk management system, post-clearance audit, and one-stop-shop system to improve the investment and trade environment in Cambodia. To be even better.
* Fifth, further strengthen the effectiveness of the prevention and suppression of tax evasion to increase revenue for the state, ensure fair competition for business, and promote compliance and fiscal culture in Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth also provided 8 additional instructions, including:
* First: Continue to simplify the procedures in accordance with the technical assistance that Akor is currently receiving from development partners in a responsible and proactive manner to further promote trade facilitation.
* Second: Improve the efficiency of prevention and suppression of crime actively in the beginning, middle, middle and end, including the crackdown on counterfeit goods, goods that violate the right to distribute, goods that can be used. As a raw material for drug production, and cooperation with relevant units to identify suspected cases of money laundering under commercial image
* Third: To expedite the examination of various legal documents related to customs in order to propose amendments and revisions in response to current requirements.
* Fourth, to strengthen customs technical work and the use of technology systems to improve efficiency and productivity.
* Fifth: Continue to promote strict and effective implementation of tax collection for existing domestic tax-free vehicles.
* Sixth: Continue to coordinate with the relevant authorities related to the prevention of tax evasion and continue good cooperation with the private sector, especially under the "D" mechanism of the Royal Government-Private Forum.
* Eighth: Continue to implement consistently and consistently health measures, especially measures 3 prevent and 3 do not to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the new normal trajectory. Lt. Gen. Nay Thol, President of the Military Tribunal, Condolences on the Death of General Vong Pisen's Mother-in-Law
