(Phnom Penh): On February 10, 2022, at the Office of the Mine Authority, on behalf of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, met with Ms. Sarah Taylor, Ambassador of Canada. Thailand, Cambodia and Laos discuss work on partnership and cooperation in the field of mine action in Cambodia.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister thanked the Government and people of Canada for their close cooperation with Cambodia in the Ottawa Convention on Anti-Personnel Mine Action Efforts and for their contribution to the humanitarian work in Cambodia. Demining for the first phase of the project to strengthen the development of agriculture and mine action and demining in villages in Battambang province.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister briefed the Canadian Ambassador on the Royal Government's efforts to address the issue of landmines and explosive remnants of war in Cambodia as a result of the country's protracted war since the beginning of the decade. 1960 and the start of humanitarian demining in Cambodia since 1992.
He added that under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the end of 1998, Cambodia achieved complete peace throughout the country, which allowed the Royal Government of Cambodia to adequately address the threat of landmines and unexploded ordnance. That is effective and fearless.
The Senior Minister added that in 2022, Cambodia will celebrate the 30th anniversary of mine clearance in Cambodia with the participation of all parties involved in mine action. Ambassador Sarah Taylor congratulated Highly appreciating the achievements of mine clearance in Cambodia for 30 years, and the Ambassador will join Samdech Techo Prime Minister in celebrating the 30th anniversary.
At the same time, the Ambassador affirmed that Canada will continue to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in demining work by 2025, as well as support the review of mine action data management, surface area research and mitigation. Land affected by landmines and munitions and technical assistance on resource mobilization for the mine action sector in Cambodia.
