The Minister of Water Resources chaired a meeting between the representatives of the Japan-Cambodia Association on measures to protect Phnom Penh from the flooding of Stung Prek Tnaot and the flooding of the Mekong River.
(Phnom Penh): On February 10, 2022, at the Ministry's office, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, chaired a meeting of the representatives of the Japan-Cambodia Association on Measures to Protect Phnom Penh from the Stung Prek Tnaot Flood and Flooding of the Mekong River.
The meeting was attended by representatives from the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Ministry of Environment, National Committee for Disaster Management, Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Takeo and Kampong Cham. Lead the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and the heads of relevant units under the Ministry through attending meetings in person and through the ZOOM system.
Welcoming the opening of the meeting, Minister Lim Kean Hor, on behalf of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, thanked Koji Kanzaki, an old friend with extensive experience in dam and road construction, for coming to Cambodia in the 1960s as a Techniques for construction of Stung Prek Tnaot Dam in Kampong Speu Province.
The Minister spoke about the management of water resources that the Ministry has implemented so far and plans for the future within the framework of the whole country, especially the measures to protect Phnom Penh from the floods of Stung Prek Tnaot and the floods of the Mekong River, which are often encountered. Past.
In his presentation to the meeting, Mr. Kochi Kansaki informed the proposal as a measure to consider the effective management of floods that have been encountered in the past for the present and in the future to prevent accidents and damage. Caused by floods in Stung Prek Tnaot, including the Mekong floods.
After listening to the introductory remarks and comments of the Minister, which highlighted the issues raised and the work as well as the plans of the Ministry have been implemented and planned in the future, the meeting appreciated:
* First: the results of the research presented, which is an important input * Second: Achievements in the field of water resources that have been achieved so far and future plans for more effective water resources management, flood prevention and use For the benefit of supporting the lives of the people and socio-economic development both now and in the future.
He stressed that the effectiveness and success of flood management depends on the joint will, operational resources and cooperation of all stakeholders. Please be informed that regarding the flood management of Stung Prek Tnaot, the Ministry has already completed the study and at present, part of the Stung Prek Tnaot Dam has been rehabilitated by the Chinese side.
It should be noted that Stung Prek Tnaot, which flows from the Oral Mountains in Kampong Speu, through Kandal and Phnom Penh in 2020, caused severe flooding in Phnom Penh, and in 2021 also flooded, but not as severely as last year. 2020. Another 763 vehicles were inspected and fined on February 10, 2022
