Mr. Yeon Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said this morning, February 10, 2022, in a press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, it was stated that only over 200 million cubic meters of water was used for the people of Oddar Meanchey Province. In the dry season, more than 500 million cubic meters remain.
According to Yeon Kuon, the remaining water in the large reservoirs of Oddar Meanchey province is distributed to people in Siem Reap and Banteay Meanchey provinces for daily use.
He said: "All in Oddar Meanchey can store up to more than 700 million cubic meters, but the use in Oddar Meanchey, I say only the dry season, we use only more than 200 million cubic meters. The other three large reservoirs, which store more than 500 million cubic meters, are distributed to Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap and are now being distributed to the people.
The director of the Department of Water Resources stated that with the consideration of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology as well as the department itself, Oddar Meanchey is currently working to restore and build many irrigation structures and so far the province. Restore more than 90 irrigation systems so that people do not have a shortage in the dry season, both for daily use and farming.
The official added that due to the irrigation system and sufficient water for irrigation, it can make people grow dry rice up to three times a year.
He added that clean water for daily use is available in the cities in the five districts of Oddar Meanchey province, which takes raw water from the reservoir. Separately, the water supply in the community is also about 6 places, while the province is also considering and studying to expand further. Lok Chumteav Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An would like to express his condolences on the death of General Vong Pisen's mother-in-law.
