International Analysis: What is behind the sweetness between Xi Jinping and Putin?
BEIJING: As some Western countries, led by the United States, boycott diplomacy against the Winter Olympics, Beijing, China and Russia have taken the opportunity of celebrating the big event to show steady growth. Of the bilateral relations of their countries.
Russian President Vladimir Putin posted several photos with Chinese President Xi Jinping on the opening day of the 2022 Beijing Winter Olympics. Putin also declared a strategic partnership without borders to counter NATO's growing influence, and called on the West to abandon Cold War ideology.
In a joint statement, Putin and Xi Jinping also said that NATO must respect the sovereignty, security and interests of all countries and adhere to an equal attitude towards the peaceful development of all countries. Why can China and Russia achieve such good relations today?
According to most experts, China and Russia have good relations because they consider the West, especially the United States, as a "common enemy" and take such a stand, making it clear that the two countries have had ideological conflicts. Cold War-era scholars were on the verge of turning their relationship into an allied system.
* Most military cooperation between China and Russia involves politics
Western experts see military cooperation between China and Russia as political rather than ready for joint military action. In recent months, Moscow has expressed its support for China's use of military force as a means of putting pressure on Japan and South Korea.
In October 2021, the Chinese and Russian navies conducted joint patrol operations around Japan, and in November 2021, the two countries' strategic bombers participated in the third air patrol operation. Above the Sea of Japan and the East China Sea, it is seen that China and Russia want to show their intention to work together to resist the US-Japan alliance.
But Beijing does not seem to be following Russia, as they are reluctant to show direct support for Russian military action in Europe. The Chinese military did not take part in the Zapad-21 military exercise organized by Russia and Belarus. Instead, Russian troops participated in joint military exercises in China.
China's reluctance to show direct support for Russia's military action in Europe could be attributed to China's fear that it would bring the EU closer to the United States. On the other hand, while Russia supports the one-China policy on Taiwan, China has never stated specific intentions regarding the Ukraine issue.
