The following is a letter from Minister Thong Khon to the Capital and Provincial Governors: Francophonie plans to hold an Asia-Pacific Economic and Trade Mission in Phnom Penh
Chekou Usuman expressed his intention to organize the Francophone Economic and Trade Mission in the Asia-Pacific Region during a working meeting with Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak on Wednesday afternoon, February 9, 2022.
Chekou said the economic and trade mission is aimed at boosting economic ties between French-speaking OIF member countries from Asia, Africa, Europe and North America. In addition, the event aims to strengthen the historical and cultural ties of all OIF member countries, which are key factors in the current global context facing global pandemics.
The economic and trade mission event is expected to bring together about 85 economic operators from all continents who will travel to Hanoi, Vietnam as the starting point and Phnom Penh as the end point of the mission.
The Minister of Commerce expressed his support for the organization of this economic and trade mission and encouraged the necessary cooperation with the Ministry of Commerce to organize this event successfully and fruitfully. Especially for the benefit of businessmen and investors of both parties.
It should be noted that in this meeting, Minister Pan Sosak warmly welcomed the presence of the OIF Representative in the Asia-Pacific region and mentioned the excellent cooperation between Cambodia and the OIF with the countries. Member of Francophone.
The Minister highlighted Cambodia's trade potential and readiness to welcome businessmen and investors from the Francophone countries. In addition, the Minister of Commerce informed about the efforts of the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Commerce in reforming institutions and building laws and regulations aimed at improving the business and investment environment in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy Phase II. 4.
The Minister also requested and encouraged the connection and strengthening of business, trade and investment relations between Cambodia and OIF member countries in more potential areas of Cambodia in the future.
Chekou Usuman also praised Cambodia's efforts to facilitate trade and investment and noted Cambodia's potential in trade, which could attract businessmen and investors from Francophone countries.
