Ministry of Commerce Holds a Meeting to Review and Ask for Recommendations on Draft Law on Rules of Origin
(Phnom Penh): This morning, February 9, 2022, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, chaired a meeting to review and comment on the draft law on the rules of origin, with the participation of the management and the working group. Draft laws and regulations on the rules of origin.
The Minister stated that Cambodia has promised to build the above law in accordance with the Agreement on the Rules of Origin under the World Trade Organization (WTO) and to comply with the approval of the work program of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Under the WTO framework, which also includes the development of laws and regulations on the rules of origin, which is a joint task between the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Ho Siewyong, Director General of the General Department of Commercial Services, gave a brief presentation on the progress of the drafting of the Law on the Origin of Goods, including the purpose, justification, necessity, background benefits and functioning of the drafting process.
With the input and comments of the Secretary of State, the Minister recommended that the working group prepare and extract the best points to compile in this draft law to be more comprehensive, consistent, in accordance with the agreement. And the provisions in force as well as strong arguments in defense of this draft law.
The Minister of Commerce encouraged and commended the working group on drafting laws and regulations on the rules of origin, as well as the leadership and the inter-ministerial working group, WTO and UNCTAD experts, who provided input, input and experience. Preparation for drafting this law. The Ministry of Interior issued a decision to establish a working group of the Secretariat under the Digital Government for Information and Communication Technology.
