International Analysis: "US Attempts to Use Taiwan as an Excuse to Prevent China's Development Will Fail
The United States claims that the draft law on arms sales to Taiwan is based on the so-called "Taiwan Relations Act" to help Taiwan respond to so-called "regional threats." But in fact, whether in terms of legal reasons or excuses for the sale of weapons, it can be seen that these words of the United States have no evidence at all to completely distort the truth.
