Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Urges to Install Street Cameras in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, urged the installation of street cameras in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap.
Samdech Krala Hom's urging was made during the meeting to review the results of road traffic safety work in 2021 and work direction in 2022 at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on February 9, 2022.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng advised to continue to tighten the enforcement of the law on land traffic to be more effective and sustainable in connection with technical measures such as the installation of speed cameras or traffic signal violations, to prepare law enforcement patrols on highways, withdrawal Driver's license scores strengthen the practice of drunk drivers and strengthen the training of officials in terms of legal, technical, operational and ethical skills.
According to the report, most of the deaths due to traffic accidents in 2021 were in Phnom Penh, Kandal and Kampong Cham provinces. Causes of accidents totaled 38% speeding, 24% disrespect, 14% overtaking, 8% overtaking, 8% drunkenness, 4%, 3% motor vehicle and 1% drowsiness. The total accident rate compared to 2020 was 509 fewer deaths, 149 fewer injuries and 1,071 fewer injuries.
In relation to this traffic situation, Samdech recommended that all components of the National Road Safety Committee increase education and dissemination of traffic safety laws and standards in all forms and to further strengthen the quality of driving schools, increase the installation of traffic lights, signs and Traffic signs and find new ways to strengthen law enforcement and reduce traffic accidents.
Prince Norodom Chakravuth Defends FUNCINPEC for Immortality
(Phnom Penh): After the Extraordinary Congress of the FUNCINPEC Party unanimously decided to elect Prince Norodom Chakravuth, the eldest son of Prince Norodom Ranariddh, as the party's president this morning, February 9, 2022.
