Please read the instructions below: Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Drugs become a traditional problem that is difficult to eradicate as Cambodia seeks to neutralize drug addicts on what is being done (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior said that the drug problem has become a traditional problem that is difficult to solve despite the continuous crackdown on distribution, trafficking and consumption.
On the occasion of chairing the meeting to review the work of road safety 2021 on the morning of February 9, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng claimed that currently out of nearly 40,000 detainees, there are more than 20,000. 54.52% were involved in drug offenses.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said, "Public health related to drugs is very difficult because it is a traditional problem that we all know. Therefore, we need to pay attention to continue to crack down on this drug crime in accordance with the existing principles.
In addition to cracking down on drug offenses, the Royal Government of Cambodia is also working to address two other issues related to drugs, namely: overcrowding in prisons, most of which are drug inmates, and second, employment. Rehabilitation for drug addicts. This is according to what Prince Sar Kheng highlighted.
According to Sar Kheng, drug users are not convicted, demanding rehabilitation, unlike drug users who have been jailed for drug trafficking.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also claimed that professional institutions are also studying together to find ways to neutralize drug addicts in addition to what is being implemented. But the prince sees that drug eradication is nothing more than a labor requirement, and this is what he is trying to use. However, the use of various anesthetics is still practiced.
In connection with this rehabilitation work, Samdech Krala Hom also called for the support of stakeholders, especially non-governmental organizations, etc., which are only suggestions and did not actually participate with the Royal Government to solve social problems.
Koh Ker Temple, Noodles and Bokator Request for Registration of World Heritage and Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia is requesting the inscription of Koh Ker temple, noodles and bokator into the UNESCO World Heritage List and the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list.
This is according to Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, speaking at the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and the work direction for 2022 of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts: on February 9, 2022 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated that "the Ministry has continued to prepare and co-prepare documents to request the inscription of Koh Ker, Noodles, and Bokator to the UNESCO World Heritage List and the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity."
Please be informed that Koh Ker Temple is located in North Srayong Village, Srayong Commune, Kulen District, Preah Vihear Province. Koh Ker temple was built during the reign of Jayavarman IV, dedicated to the Brahmin religion. This temple was originally called Chok Koki or Koki land area, now called the former capital of Koh Ker, with an area of 16 x 16 kilometers, including 98 temples. This temple has 7 floors, 35 meters high.
Bokator is a martial art like a lion, using fighting force like a lion. Bokator is considered to be the master of Khmer martial arts, which is believed to have originated in the Khmer dynasty of King Suryavarman II, a powerful king who established an army rule that divided the army into infantry. The spear, the cavalry, the elephant and the arrow ... these are the roots of the creation of the Angkorian Empire in his reign.
