(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a press release on the closing of training courses on the registration of candidates of political parties and the election campaign.
The three-day training on the registration of candidates of political parties and the election campaign was concluded on the morning of February 9, 2022 at the NEC office under the high presidency of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the Committee. National Election Committee (NEC).
During the closing ceremony, Mr. Prach Chan emphasized that the NEC has already held four Commune / Sangkat Council elections. For the preparation of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022, political parties wishing to contest the election must manually submit the registration of candidates of political parties to the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission, as political parties used to Applied so far.
Mr. Prach Chan also mentioned that the technology used by the NEC for voter registration was getting good results and now the NEC has introduced another new technology, the candidate registration management program. Of political parties, the issuance of identification documents for the election and the program to monitor, verify and summarize the election results.
At the same time, the NEC Chairman continued that the three-day training is very important, which requires election officials, political parties, associations, non-governmental organizations and all parties involved in the election to have high knowledge and technical skills. In carrying out the election work clearly and correctly in accordance with the laws and regulations and procedures of the NEC.
He also instructed the chairmen of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) and the heads of the 25 secretariats of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) to take high responsibility in Organize training courses for election officials at all levels to ensure the successful implementation of roles and responsibilities.
Mr. Prach Chan hopes that all political parties, parties involved in the election and the Election Commission at all levels will pay close attention to good cooperation to promote the upcoming Commune / Sangkat Council elections.
Participants in the training organized by the NEC were election officials from the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (PEC) and the Secretariat of the CEC (PEC). 25 representatives of 16 political parties, representatives of 12 associations and non-governmental organizations with approximately 136 participants.
According to the calendar of Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate 2022, the application for registration of candidates of political parties will run for three days, from March 4 to 6, 2022, and the application Please register the candidates of this political party at the office of the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission.
