Ministry of Economy launches user feedback mechanism through information technology nursery business registration system
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a press release on the implementation of the user feedback mechanism through the business registration system in the information technology nursery. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on February 9, 2022.
The first phase of the Information Technology Nursery Business Registration System was officially launched on June 15, 2020 and covers package registration including business registration. Ministry of Commerce, tax registration of the General Department of Taxation and issuance of enterprise opening announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
In the past 1 year and 7 months, the number of approved registration applications was 11,077.
In line with the support and coordination mechanism aimed at improving the experience of using and strengthening the business registration services in the information technology nursery, a new function "Feedback Mechanism" has been developed and launched from February 8, 2022. Continue.
This feature will allow businesses and users to express constructive feedback or report specific issues on any application case.
Any feedback received will be an important input in enabling the team to be able to support, edit and continue to develop the business registration system in the information technology nursery more easily and efficiently. FUNCINPEC, led by new president, launches nine new policies to restore popularity
(Phnom Penh): FUNCINPEC, which has just elected a new president, has launched nine new policies to restore the party's popularity.
The direction was set during the Extraordinary Congress on the morning of February 9, 2022 to elect Prince Norodom Chakravuth, the son of Norodom Ranariddh, as party president.
FUNCINPEC Royalist Party also announced nine new policies, including the following:
First, to change, preserve, protect and promote the constitutional monarchy and liberal, multi-party democracy and to abide by the spirit of the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991.
Second, to urge the establishment of the National Congress by giving the King the highest presidency and respecting the King's prerogative to grant amnesty.
Third, strengthen the independent and neutral judiciary to ensure that cases are resolved fairly and equitably.
Fourth, to promote and support the development of all sectors to provide jobs for people with jobs everywhere.
Fifth, create study loans so that students can continue their studies and build buildings to provide appropriate accommodation.
Sixth: Determine and strengthen professional ethics in the field of health sciences with high efficiency.
Seventh: Guarantee the discount of all kinds of goods and fuel, lower the price of electricity. Increase the wages of workers and increase the salaries of civil servants and the armed forces in accordance with market conditions.
Eighth: Guarantee the market for selling agricultural products and guarantee the price of agricultural products according to the free market price and international market.
And 9th, stop leasing economic land concessions along the border to foreign countries, expand the area of social land concessions for distribution to the poor. Eliminate people's land grabbing and exploitation of natural resources, deforestation, illegal mining and illegal fishing. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng sets out some work priorities to reduce traffic accidents in 2022
(Phnom Penh): In the meeting to review the work of the Road Safety Committee this morning, February 9, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee. That in 2021, traffic accidents in Cambodia will decrease compared to last year.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that although the number of traffic accidents has decreased, some destinations such as Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Cham and Sihanoukville still have high accident figures.
With the same concern, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also set out some work directions for the relevant institutions to work together to reduce traffic accidents, including:
* First: The first subcommittee must pay more attention to the following necessary tasks:
* Increase education and dissemination of traffic safety laws and standards in all forms to the community and back home in high-risk areas. In addition, educational content on standards for the use of expressways and one-way roads must be developed in order to disseminate public awareness and participate in the proper implementation from now on to avoid possible accidents in the use of these roads.
* Need to strengthen the quality of driving schools by urgently reviewing three factors: 1: reform the capacity of teachers, 2: reform education (curriculum, study materials, training facilities) and 3: reform the quality of Driving test for the purpose of improving the quality and ability of all drivers to have a deep understanding of both theory and driving to become a driver who respects the law and has a high level of understanding and tolerance.
* Continue to install adequate traffic lights, signs and markers to ensure safe traffic and continue to support the installation of stationary cameras on national roads by incorporating this equipment into construction projects or Road repair
* In the face of the continuous growth of vehicles, continue to find new measures to prevent and curb traffic congestion that is occurring in some areas in Phnom Penh and may occur in other areas in the future.
* Continue to enforce laws to prevent overcrowding in a more efficient, transparent and sustainable manner.
Prepare to patrol the law enforcement on the highway, control the camera, monitor the speed, remove the points on the driver's license, while trying to prevent the driving of vehicles under the influence of drugs with a strict punishment. Upcoming amendments to the Road Traffic Law.
Third, the Capital and Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee must continue to promote the implementation of the following important tasks:
* To promote the installation of road safety equipment, including traffic lights, signs and traffic signs on the roads for which the Capital and Provincial Administration is responsible. In particular, in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap, must continue to cooperate with the installation of street cameras according to the project of the Royal Government and be assigned to manage, use and maintain in accordance with technical standards.
* Strict restrictions must be placed on the business of transporting sand, gravel, must be covered closely and roads should be cleaned regularly, and strict administrative and legal measures must be taken for violations.
* Must continue to manage the vehicle assembly and maintenance garage on the documents prescribed by law and ensure the correct assembly and installation of vehicles in accordance with technical standards.
* Must manage the land for road construction by preventing the construction or illegal use affecting traffic safety and the construction and expansion of road infrastructure.
Fourth, all mechanisms under the NCDD must be involved in the prevention and control of Kovid 19 by strictly implementing the "Three Prevention, Three Prevention" health rules and promoting vaccination control for everyone. And regular testing.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his strong hope that based on the work experience and responsible spirit of all ministries, competent institutions, authorities at all levels, we will be able to successfully prevent and reduce traffic accidents in the year. 2022, as well as maintaining the order of road traffic to improve gradually.
