18 Former Siem Reap CNRP Leaders and Members Join CPP
(Siem Reap): Former leaders of 18 former members of the Cambodian National Rescue Party (CNRP) in Siem Reap have volunteered to join the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) after waking up and clearly understanding their qualifications. And the great achievements of the Cambodian People's Party to the nation and the people.
Former leaders and former members of the Cambodia National Rescue Party in Siem Reap who surrendered include: Mr. Sao Yoeng, former Provincial Councilor, Chief of Finance of Siem Reap Province and Chairman of Puok District Working Group, Mr. Ros Samnang, Former Councilor of Kork Chak Commune, Mr. Tep Chen Former Kork Chak commune councilor, Ms. Chan Somaly, former chief of Kork Chak first commune, as well as former members who are all active activists of the former CNRP in Siem Reap.
The inauguration ceremony of the new members of the Cambodian People's Party, the former leadership of the former members of the National Rescue Party, was held at the CPP headquarters in Siem Reap, presided over by Mr. Tea Seiha, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and President of the Cambodian People's Party, Siem Reap Province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. You Serey Vuth and some working groups of the Cambodian People's Party.
On that occasion, Mr. Tea Seiha as well as Mr. You Serey Vuth warmly welcomed the new members and considered the participation in the political life of the former leaders of the former members of the National Rescue Party in Siem Reap is the right decision to unite. With the Cambodian People's Party, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as President, build and develop a more prosperous Cambodian society and bring harmony, prosperity and prestige to the nation and its people.
Mr. Sao You Eng, Former Member of Siem Reap Provincial Council, Chief of Finance and Chairman of Puok District Working Group from the former CNRP, on behalf of other members, expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party. That allowed him and former commune councilors, youth activists in Siem Reap to participate in political life with the Cambodian People's Party.
Mr. Sao Youeng highlighted that there are two reasons why he and other members volunteered to live with the CPP. The first two reasons are to see the leadership, conscience and many achievements that the CPP has built for the motherland, the second reason is to be fed up with the poison, tricks and dangerous political ideology of the past. CNRP.
Mr. Sao Youeng and his team promised to work honestly and mobilize former members of the National Rescue Party to return to live with the CPP.
