Mine Authority and Army Command Meet on Strengthening Partnership and Cooperation on Demining and Explosive Remnants of War
Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chief of the Mine Authority and Lieutenant General Dr. HUN Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Video meeting on the dissemination of the letter of the Council of Ministers No. 07 S.C.N. And strengthening partnerships and cooperation on demining and explosive remnants of war.
The meeting was attended by the Provincial Governor, the Deputy Governor, the Provincial Mine Action Committee (PMAC) and the Mine Action Plan (Mapu) Working Group of 15 provincial administrations, which have mines and explosive remnants of war along the border. Participation of Deputy Commanders, Commanders-in-Chief, Regional Commanders, Brigade Commanders, Brigade Commanders and officers under the Army Command.
The Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude to Lt. Gen. Hun Manet for his valuable time in serving the motherland to chair the meeting.
At the same time, the Senior Minister praised the efforts of the sub-national administration to coordinate and manage the mine action area in its geographical area, which has achieved successful results for the past 30 years. 1992 Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace, and throughout his life he sought only peace and security for the Cambodian people.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet congratulated and highly appreciated the achievements of demining work in Cambodia for the past 30 years and considered the demining work as very important in contributing to the reduction of population danger and development. The nation as well as the rehabilitation of former battlefields for development.
