The program is organized in two parts, the first part is the DEY program board visit at TVET, a program partner and at the company where the students benefit from the program, and the second part is the program board meeting of the program. DEY.
The third meeting of the Board of Directors of the Youth Employment and Decent Employment Program in Cambodia (DEY) Phase 2 was organized for three purposes:
* Reflect the results of the program during the first two years of the second phase and discuss challenges and solutions to achieve the expected results.
* Review and approve the program work plan for 2022.
* Discuss innovative solutions for getting more contributions from the Royal Government of Cambodia and the private sector for program sustainability.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that although Cambodia has been severely affected economically and socially due to the global spread of Kovid-19, the project is still able to continue its activities. Its going forward.
He added that during the two years of implementing the second phase of the DEY program, a good foundation has been built to help young people acquire new skills in a quality way to meet the needs of the labor market. As a catalyst to encourage young people to have access to decent and productive job opportunities.
As a result of this third meeting, the Board of Directors decided:
* Agree to identify strategic solutions to address current challenges encountered during program implementation.
* Approved a work plan for the implementation of the 2022 program, which focuses on young people negatively affected by the Kovid-19 epidemic in order to support them in overcoming challenges. They experienced during the outbreak of Kovid-19 and were better prepared for recovery after Kovid-19.
* Set strategic directions for program sustainability.
