Both sides say they are awaiting a final political decision from the other side to resume the nuclear deal.
According to the Digital Government of Cambodia Policy 2022-2035, in 2021, there will be about 17.65 million registered Internet users, of which about 17.35 million registered mobile Internet users.
At the same time, about 37% of the young people are able to capture and use digital technology quickly, while the business of using digital technology has increased with the emergence of digital business companies.
Cambodia has about 46,000 km of fiber-optic cable network and two submarine fiber optic cables, of which the first submarine fiber cable connects Cambodia to Thailand and Malaysia and the second cable connects Cambodia to 18 countries. In Asia, Africa and Europe. However, this telecommunications infrastructure does not yet cover the whole country, as the 4th generation (4G) mobile network is providing services to about 80% of the population.
The government has a strategy to strengthen and expand the mobile and high-speed internet infrastructure by strengthening the quality and expanding the coverage of the 4th generation (4G) mobile services to reach the 5th generation (5G) mobile services and promote Build fiber-optic infrastructure under the seabed and build high-speed internet infrastructure to all communes.
Please be informed that in 2020, Cambodia earned from the telecommunications sector about 1.1 billion US dollars, equivalent to about 4.2% of GDP, which is a high rate compared to developing countries.
