This morning, the Minister said that the Ministry has been implementing the cash subsidy program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age who have been living in poverty as a permanent program since last month. June 2019. The program is funded by about 250,000 pregnant women and children at a total cost of about $ 17 million.
For the cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age who are poor, a total of 760,000 Riels will be provided during pregnancy, childbirth, postpartum and post-vaccination. Health center or public hospital.
In addition to implementing programs to help pregnant women and children under the age of two, the Ministry of Social Affairs is also carrying out a major task: providing cash assistance to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19.
This program is a non-permanent program, launched in June 2020. From the implementation of the program until now, there are around 700,000 beneficiary families with a total budget of 562 million dollars.
