The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Tourism: The pagoda, which is 70 years old, has changed its face with the beginning of the construction of the first luxurious entrance gate of the pagoda. Each
(Preah Vihear): A poor pagoda in the remote countryside at the foot of the mountain in Samlanh village, Tbeng Muy commune, Sangkum Thmei district, Preah Vihear province has changed its face by starting to build the entrance gate of the pagoda with luxurious design for the first time after This pagoda was built 70 years ago as of today.
Venerable Noeum Kimsan, the chief abbot of Thaksin Kiri pagoda, also known as Wat Samlanh, said that the pagoda was 70 years old, according to the village elders. He added that the reason why this pagoda is not as developed as other pagodas is because this pagoda is in a remote rural area at the foot of the mountain, which in the past was not as developed as it is today, there are not many people passing by. .
The chief abbot of the pagoda said that while the country was completely peaceful and developed in all areas, both in terms of empire and Buddhism, Wat Taksinki, also known as Wat Samlanh, began to change its face with the participation of Leaders as well as Buddhists near and far have been involved in the construction of infrastructure in the pagoda.
The entrance to the pagoda, which for 70 years has never been built in such a luxurious way, was also built for the first time with the support of Mr. Samleang Try, Chairman of the Provincial Working Group to Sangkum Thmey District and Team 50% deposit. He added that "without Samleang Tri as a position to build, he would have dared to build, because the cost of building this gate is $ 22,300."
