The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) entered into force on January 1, 2021. These two agreements have become important drivers of greater trade, goods, services and investment, especially providing additional markets for hundreds of new items for export from Cambodia.
The Regional Comprehensive Trade Partnership Agreement (RCEP) is attended by 15 countries, including the 10 ASEAN member states, and five other free trade partners - Australia, China, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand, which were first established in 2012 in Phnom Penh.
(Phnom Penh): Two experts in the field of microfinance have explained the number of reasons why borrowers fail to use their loans indirectly or use loans only for materialism.
Mr. Soeung Simon, General Manager of Sambath Finance Microfinance Institution, mentioned five factors that make borrowers fail:
Factor 5: Most start-ups start from the younger generation, starting with a desire and not having a full analysis, and starting a big business beyond their capabilities.
Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy, Director of the Public Relations Department of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated that the factors that make clients successful are good habits in budget management, as opposed to unsuccessful clients generally do not have clear habits in managing budgets and savings.
In addition, Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy pointed out that the majority of customers who are in debt and take out debt to fail are mostly related to private debt, which is usually customers borrowing private debt or in some cases take both official debt and private debt.
He explained that the official institutions and banks need customers to have clear documents and letters because they want to protect customers to avoid credit failure, which is part of the mechanism of the institution.
Looking at private loans, they do not care about the documents and letters of customers, which makes customers easy to fail to borrow, especially private loans are high interest rates.
Some customers who fail him borrow money from financial institutions, but when there is a problem, they do not find a solution, they run to the private sector, which has a high interest rate to pay off the official debt, increasing the debt.
According to both experts, in order for a loan to be successful, all customers must have a clear financial plan as well as their business before going for a loan, especially to seek credit at institutions and banks that are officially avoided. Private with high interest.
