This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurates Nearly 100 Kilometers of National Road No. 7 in Kratie Province
(Kratie): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, co-chaired the inauguration ceremony of National Road No. 7 from Monday morning, February 7, 2022. The 93.56-kilometer-long Tiger Roundabout from Kratie City to Romat Village, O'Kreang Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province was built with the assistance of the Chinese government.
According to the Senior Minister, the length of the road is 39.35 km, 9 cm thick AC concrete and 54.21 km long, 5 cm thick AC concrete. The width of the road is 11 meters, divided into two lanes for cars, each lane is 3.5 meters wide, and the lane for motorcycles has two lanes, each lane is 1.50 meters wide, and the red sidewalk is 0.50 wide on each side. M.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the project to improve the quality of National Road 7 is a grant from the Chinese government to the Royal Government of Cambodia, which began construction in November 2016 and completed during the month. In December 2018, the construction period was 24 months, built by Shanghai Construction Company (SCG) and technically inspected by Guangzhou Wanan Technical Consulting Company at a cost of 33.37 million US dollars.
The Senior Minister said, "This new achievement is an invaluable and precious bond that arises from the steel friendship and cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of China to the people of Kratie Province." "As well as people across the country for general and long-term use."
According to Sun Chanthol, National Road No. 7 is a potential road connecting Phnom Penh through major provinces such as Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kratie, Stung Treng and towards Cambodia's fourth economic pole in the northeastern region of the country. Which serves the traffic for economic, trade and tourism exchange activities in the country.
