(Kratie): The newly constructed section of National Road No. 7, nearly 100 kilometers long, connects Kratie City to O'Kreang Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province, has become a new economic artery and has also turned a quiet area into a bustling area. Living and farming as well.
A section of National Road No. 7, more than 93 kilometers long from the Tiger Roundabout in Kapo Village, Sangkat Or Russey, Kratie City to Romat Village, O'Kreang Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province, was constructed as a two-layer paved road (DBST) between 2004 and 2007. . This is a brand new road in Kratie province.
Prior to the construction of this section of the road, the settlements of the people as well as other crops were scarce. Residents on both sides of the road claim that during the 1990s the area was quiet because there were no roads.
But after the Royal Government built this section of National Road 7, the situation in this area is not as quiet as in the past. Currently, the presence of this section of road has led to more people settling on both sides of the road and increasing the number of people coming to farm on both sides of the road.
The presence of this road not only attracts the settlement of the people, but also contributes significantly to improving the lives of the people.
Mr. Ho Sokun claimed, "It's time to have such an easy road and it is very convenient for me, the planter. For the transportation of agricultural products, and traders come to buy, it is expensive because the road is easy.
Both the Governor of Kratie Province and the people living on both sides of this road expressed their happiness for the precious bond of the Royal Government on this road and expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, who always takes into account the difficulties of the people and built this section of road.
The provincial governor and the people living on both sides of the road highly valued Samdech Techo's leadership, which brought peace, national unity and national development, which is rare in the history of Cambodia's leadership.
It should be noted that the section of National Road No. 7 from the Tiger Roundabout in Kapo Village, Sangkat Or Russey, Kratie City to Romat Village, O'Kreang Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province, which has been upgraded, will be officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on February 7, 2022.
