(Kampong Chhnang): 70 fishing tackle devices have been returned to the authorities by the people in Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, and a contract has been signed to stop illegal fishing activities.
This decision was made after Dr. Sok Touch researched the loss of fish species in the Tonle Sap Lake due to the use of illegal fishing gear, especially electric gear, which caused serious damage to fish species.
Under the guidance of the provincial governor, Kampong Leng district has encouraged and announced to the people who have all kinds of fish-eating inductors to be alert and voluntarily handed over to the specialized authority of the District Administrative Unity Command.
As a result of the promotion of the above district administration, as of February 4, 2022, local people in Kampong Leng have signed a contract to stop the use and hand over a total of 70 electric shock inductors, including 63 types of hot shock. 7 units and types of cold shock.
