On January 24, 2022, eight civil society organizations, including the Cambodian Center for Human Rights, the Adhoc Human Rights Defenders Association, submitted a joint letter to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court requesting to visit eight union representatives once a month. As of January 2022, but the request was rejected by the court.
Mr. Kim Santepheap added, "Individuals who are not authorized by law or who are involved in any illegal activities of detainees who are within the jurisdiction of the court are subject to the denial of access." No detainees! ”
He said that in Cambodia, there is no article in the law that stipulates the right of civil society to meet with detainees, so the decision of the judge to refuse to allow representatives of civil society to visit detainees is a jurisdiction. The law of the courts of Cambodia and the proper implementation of the procedures of Cambodian law.
The spokesman urged civil society to study its role and rights set out in the law and to exercise its rights within the bounds of the law.
(Svay Rieng): A group of three thieves armed with rifles robbed people's houses in the early evening, taking a gold bracelet weighing 5 grams and about $ 200.
According to the authorities, the robbery happened at 6:30 pm on February 4, 2022 at Russey North Village, Kral Ko Commune, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province.
According to the authorities, the owner of the house, Chet Phorn, 40 years old, and his wife Un Thida, 30 years old, lived in the above-mentioned village-commune. Sources confirmed that before the incident, the victim's family was sitting in the basement of the house when a group of 3 thieves wearing leotards with long arms in their hands came to the husband and threatened to take him. Give them gold and silver.
Frightened, the victim's wife took a handbag containing a 5g gold bracelet and $ 200 to the thieves, which contained a Cambodian identity card and a vaccination card. Protect Kovid-19 as well. Immediately after taking the gold and silver, the thieves escaped.
Authorities said that after the incident, the victim called the team at Command 117 of the National Police to intervene. After receiving the information, Lieutenant-Colonel Srey Sithon, Command Team 117, sent the information to Mr. Bou Saren, Deputy Commissioner of Svay Rieng Provincial Police for immediate intervention.
Police said that after receiving the information, the Deputy Commissioner of Svay Rieng Province led the police to the scene to find that a group of suspects armed with two unknown weapons and a bamboo pole about 80 wheels long. SOM threatened to take 5 grams of gold, 200 dollars and a mobile phone from the owner of the house. Currently, the competent authorities are searching for the above thieves to be punished according to the law.
According to Mr. Kork Vanthan, Chief of Krol Kor Commune, Svay Chrum District, on the morning of February 5, 2022, he and his team visited the same victim, Chet Thean, 40 years old, and his wife Un Thida, 38 years old. In the northern village of Russey, which was robbed at 6:30 p.m.
