(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 5, 2022, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and President of the Cambodian Muslim Intellectuals Union (CMIU), presided over a closing ceremony with Cambodian Muslim intellectuals. 450 domestic and international studies.
The ceremony was held at the Modern 5 Center in Phnom Penh with the participation of Khmer Muslim leaders, senators, members of the National Assembly, Secretaries of State, Undersecretaries of State, government advisors and many Muslim intellectuals.
He added that the Muslim community is not very educated in the field of social sciences. And according to the study until 1970, we were still very small, and from 1970 to 1975, we were still small because our country was engulfed in war from 1975 to 1979. Some Muslim intellectuals were killed, as were innocent people, with Pol Pot killing more than two million.
Starting from 1979 until 1990, the Muslim community began to have some proud students for our Islamic community. From 1990 to the present, we have a large number of intellectuals graduating in foreign countries, creating human resources in the Islamic community to contribute to the Royal Government in building the motherland with fellow citizens. All nations and all religions.
The Senior Minister emphasized that the Islamic community has not been as successful as it used to be. The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, has provided many policy opportunities to the Muslim community, such as Honor the role in government and alleviate the hardships of the Muslim community without racism and religious discrimination.
He added that Cambodia under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has made Cambodia grow in all areas, which should be a source of pride for all of us after the policy. Victory without bloodshed brings complete peace, which unites the Cambodian people in maintaining peace.
Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, confirmed that the process of negotiating the export of fresh Pailin lentils to China has reached the final stage, with both sides agreeing and waiting. Only the day of the upcoming protocol.
He expects that the technical ceremony on the export of fresh Pailin lentils from Cambodia to China will be possible in the near future.
According to the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, there is currently a Pailin cleaning, disinfection and packaging facility for export, one in Pailin province, while the other is under construction in Sihanoukville to serve more exports. In Cambodia, there are about 8,000 hectares of Pailin longan plantation.
Mr. Tom Sophoan, Administration of Mien Pailin Association, expressed his appreciation that Mien Pailin can officially export to China this year, which he expects to be able to save the losses of farmers who face the market in recent years. The latter.
He said that the Mien Pailin Association is ready to export Pailin Mien to China, in which the members of the association have started to cultivate longan in accordance with the export market, and about 70 plantations have already registered good agricultural practices with the Ministry of Agriculture. More is being promoted to encourage other plantation owners to register as good agricultural practices.
He said that during the harvest season this year, the market in Pailin is not very good, while the price is also low, the price has dropped to about 1,200 riel per kilogram.
Meanwhile, after Mean Pailin, Cambodia is examining the possibility of negotiating the opening of markets for fragrant coconut and other potential crops such as durian, pepper and dragon fruit.
Mr. Ngin Chhay stated that fragrant coconuts will soon be able to be exported to China, and now the Ministry of Agriculture is training more techniques for farmers and plantation owners to grow fragrant coconuts so that they can grow in accordance with export standards.
