(Kampong Speu): Mango, turmeric is a crop that Cambodian farmers grow because it is easy to grow and get high yields.
Most of Cambodia's fresh mangoes are exported to neighboring countries such as Vietnam and Thailand. In May 2021, Cambodia's fresh mangoes, a high quality and standard mango, were first exported to China, opening up new markets for Cambodian mangoes and boosting Cambodia's exports. Subsequently.
However, new markets do not seem to be helping farmers to cope with the market. During the harvest season, farmers are still facing market problems such as falling prices and waste.
"Rich Farm, we can also visit and we can talk in cooperation to provide ideas and techniques, provide input and make a contract to help collect from them," he said. "Most importantly, we want them to comply with the standards, so we can help collect from them for export."
The bigger the mango market, the more farmers are encouraged to increase their quality cultivation.
At the same time, in order for Cambodian monkeys to be able to export in all seasons and get high prices, he urged farmers to make off-season mangoes that are harvested during October and November, the months when mangoes are more expensive in China.
Mr. Kim Laom, a mango and turmeric farmer who owns 16 hectares of mango land in Kampong Thom province, said that after the outbreak of 19 diseases, he faced market problems because there were no traders from Vietnam to collect as before. This has led to a sharp drop in mango prices this year as fertilizers and pesticides and labor costs have risen sharply.
He said that if there is a clear market, he will consider investing in cultivation in line with export markets.
According to experts in cultivating mangoes, both seasonal and out-of-season mangoes, to meet high standards for export, farmers need to set up proper irrigation systems, care, scheduling, packaging and harvesting, especially plantation owners. Mangoes must be registered with the Ministry of Agriculture for Good Agricultural Practices (CamGAP).
Dr. Mey Kalyan, Senior Advisor to the Supreme National Economic Council, said that Cambodia must not rely on the Chinese market alone, but on market diversification. He added that currently, in addition to the Chinese market, Cambodian mangoes have gradually started to be exported to Russia, and the visit of the German Ambassador to Cambodia will be able to promote Cambodian mango exports to Germany and Europe.
After Cambodian mangoes were officially exported to China, there are now five export companies that have a facility for cleaning, packing and killing pesticides registered with the Ministry of Agriculture, and farms that follow the principles of good agriculture registered with the Ministry of Agriculture. There are 50 farms covering more than 20,000 hectares out of a total of more than 100,000 hectares of mango plantations.
