Vladimir Putin meets face-to-face with Xi Jinping amid rising tensions with the West
BEIJING: Chinese President Xi Jinping on Friday held his first face-to-face meeting with world leaders in nearly two years, meeting with Russian President Vladimir Putin. He praised the ties between the two neighbors as tensions with the West escalated. This was released by Reuters on Friday, February 4, 2022.
Xi and Putin met in the Chinese capital, Beijing, as the two countries sought to deepen ties amid growing criticism from the West. During the face-to-face meeting, Putin said that Moscow's relations with Beijing are steadily developing on the path of friendship and strategic partnership, and that it is an example of a dignified relationship.
For Xi Jinping, he has not left the country since early 2020, when the COVID-19 virus was rampant in China. However, on the occasion of the start of the Beijing Winter Olympics, Xi will be busy with diplomatic activities, with leaders from more than 20 countries traveling to the opening ceremony of the International Games.
