Thirteen old houses almost 100 years old in Phsar Krom in Kampong Chhnang are being demolished
(Kampong Chhnang): Thirteen dilapidated stone houses, 91 years old, in Phsar Chhnang village, Sangkat Phsar Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang city, have been demolished. It is a French colonial building built in 1931.
A man in charge of demolishing the 13 stone flats on the morning of February 4, 2022, said that his company had been in the process of demolishing the stone houses for three days. And in about 10 days it will be ready.
The man also confirmed that for the reconstruction of the 13 stone houses, the landlord has not yet negotiated the price with the company to rebuild the apartment.
Separately, sources from people near the apartment said that the cost of demolishing the 13 stone houses, each apartment costs about $ 1,700.
Hing Phop Mina, deputy governor of Kampong Chhnang city, said last week that provincial authorities had issued a permit for the 13 landlords to rent out the demolition company, with the landlord negotiating a fee with the company. .
