General Knowledge: In the 18th century, two scholars fought a war of words until their deaths.
(Phnom Penh): The 16th to 19th centuries were a time of the emergence of a series of famous scholars, some of whom discovered new discoveries, some of whom developed various philosophies, but at the end of the century 18 War broke out between two scholars over differences of opinion.
Rousseau opposed class inequality, while Walters opposed freedom of expression and religion. There are still social contracts and many other things that make this war of words continue until the two of them die respectively.
However, these two scholars have changed the mindset of our people in the future. They both share the same views on the anti-traditional mindset, but differ on the modern mindset.
