Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Meets Gasoline Station Representatives to Discuss Electric Vehicle Charging
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has been working towards achieving the ambitious goal of promoting the use of electric vehicles in Cambodia to help the environment and reduce pollution.
On February 3, 2022, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol met with representatives of major gas stations in Cambodia such as Sokimex, Total, Tela, Caltex and PTT to discuss the preparation of electric vehicle (EV). Charging Station). The design of electric vehicle charging stations is an important element to encourage the use of electric vehicles.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister briefed on the current implementation of EVs, a joint project between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) regarding the installation of EVs charging stations, planning. The main support for the use of EVs under the auspices of UNDP and the provision of 30 electric motorcycles for testing.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also highlighted Cambodia's commitment to achieving zero carbon emissions by 2050 and submitted a master plan for the use of electric vehicles. The United Nations has set a target of 40% for electric vehicles and 30% for electric motorcycles.
