(Phnom Penh): Mr. Plong Sihak, Director of the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Khan Por Senchey and Chairman of the 6th Field Team of the Phnom Penh Land Administration Sub-Program, continued to urge his subordinates and staff to pay attention, accelerate and strengthen In addition, the land registration is systematic for the people.
This acceleration is in response to the leadership of Mr. Hem Darith, Special District Governor, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Plong Sihak continued to accelerate and strengthen the work of his subordinates and staff in the January review meeting and set the direction for the resumption of work for February of the systematic land registration on February 2. February 2022.
Land registration and issuance of title deeds have two procedures: registration at the request of the landowner, which is called lump sum registration, and one commune-sangkat registration as determined by the Royal Government. The so-called systematic registration.
After the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, all land titles throughout the country were lost. The law provides for the abolition of all pre-1979 ownership regimes. In order to prepare for the re-registration of land titles and the issuance of land titles nationwide, the law sets out to establish a special procedure, "systematic land registration."
Systematic land registration is a land registration that takes place on the initiative of the Royal Government without the request of the landowner. The government determines which villages or communes are to be registered for land registration.
This systematic land registration procedure is divided into five main stages:
* Stage 3: Dissemination The authority must make a public posting of the cadastral plan and the list of land owners so that the relevant people can inspect and protest for correction if there is a wrong place.
It should be noted that in this registration process, if there is any dispute such as border dispute, the parties to the dispute can ask the Administrative Commission to help resolve and mediate without having to go to court.
* Stage 4: Judgment and decision of this stage is relevant only to state institutions. After the 30-day protest period, the competent official shall examine the cadastral plan and the list of land owners to be registered in the land register. Any land that is not in dispute and does not belong to the state will be registered in the land register and the director of the provincial / municipal land department will sign the final title deed.
* Stage 5: Distribution of cards is the final stage. After the authorities sign and issue the cards, these cards will be distributed to the landowners. The landowner has to go and get the title deed in person and this card is a final title deed.
It should be noted that although the systematic registration is not yet completed across the country, separate registration at the request of the landowner is still possible at the same time.
Separate for land registration: The land registration can be applied for by the owner, but it is expensive according to the price set by the Ministry depending on the location of the land and most of the people. Many are not able to keep this card unless there is a need to sell it.
This piece of land registration can be divided into 3 main stages or 5 stages:
1. To apply for land registration, the land owner must first apply to the District / Khan Land Office through the Commune / Sangkat Chief where the land is located. Commune / Sangkat chiefs will have to confirm some points of the land owner and the identity of the land use.
3. Posting to the public: In the construction of this cadastral plan, the district-Khan hall must make a public announcement. After the cadastral plan has been drawn up, the land title and landlord identity will be made public again for 30 days to give stakeholders the opportunity to object or protest.
4. Examination and decision officer If there is no protest, the district-Khan authority will prepare a report to the provincial-municipal cadastral office for final decision.
