BANGKOK: The Bank of Thailand plans to allow more than one commercial bank to acquire commercial banking licenses, including virtual banking licenses, which are also set to pave the way for the country's digital economy. According to the Bangkok Post.
This reorganization of the financial sector requires achieving the right balance between driving innovation and risk management, as well as allowing for flexibility in dealing with sudden changes.
The Bank of Thailand is open to input from all sectors to ensure that guidelines and policies serve the needs of all stakeholders. The public hearing is scheduled to continue until February 28.
Roong Mallikamas, Assistant Governor of the Bank of Thailand in charge of the Financial Institutions Policy Group, said in the advisory document that the Bank of Thailand provides greater flexibility for traditional banking operations and welcomes new innovators, including financial technology companies. Digital banking, virtual banking and more.
