(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has signed into law the ratification of the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and South Korea on the 29th. January 2022, after passing the examination from the National Assembly and the Senate.
The promulgation of the Law on the Approval of the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and South Korea paves the way for Cambodia and South Korea to fully implement free trade between them.
The agreement will further boost Cambodia's exports to the Republic of Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has strongly expressed his belief that this free trade agreement will be a major driving force in boosting trade and investment flows between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
Please note that in addition to the Free Trade Agreement with the Republic of Korea, Cambodia also has free trade with China and with economic partners in all areas of the RCEP. Free trade agreements with China and RCEP partners have already entered into force.
Samdech Techo once considered the establishment of these free trade as helping to breathe a better picture of the Cambodian economy and expand the market for Cambodian products even bigger.
