The Ministry of Education completes the forensic examination and decides to keep the result intact with the closing of all protests
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on February 2, 2022 decided to close the examination on the results of the high school diploma exam on December 27, 2021 after complaints from candidates, parents and caregivers. Students are skeptical of that outcome.
In a press release obtained by Fresh News, the Ministry of Education claimed that the forensic commission had found that the results of the high school diploma examination on December 27, 2021 had not changed. On this basis, the Ministry would like to announce the end of receiving applications from candidates and the end of the process of reviewing and resolving protests from the date of this press release.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has confirmed that:
In response to the candidates 'requests and complaints about the results of the exam, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has set up a "forensic committee" to examine and resolve the above issues to ensure that the candidates' parents, guardians and the public trust the exam results.
After completing the forensic examination, the forensic committee found that the results of the high school diploma examination period: December 27, 2021 did not change. On this basis, the Ministry would like to announce the end of receiving applications from candidates and the end of the process of reviewing and resolving protests from the date of this press release.
For students who fail the exam, the Ministry encourages them to study hard with the support of teachers, parents, guardians and the community to succeed in the exam in the coming year.
