(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the program to deduct points on illegal driver's licenses has been completed and has been put into trial operation. The program is also scheduled to be officially launched in the near future.
The senior minister explained that the driver's license clearance program that when there is a traffic offender, traffic police officers will arrest and check the driver's license and just put a scanner will immediately release all information related to the driver's license. If a police officer sees any errors, just click on the machine, it will automatically add and subtract points. Not only that, but also the cost of the fine.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol added, "When the driver's license violates all 12 points and the machine will jump red, indicating that the score is exhausted, which requires the driver to have to re-test the driver's license."
The establishment of a driver's license deduction program for illegal drivers is another effort by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the National Road Safety Committee to encourage drivers to obey traffic laws and reduce accidents. Traffic.
