The ecotourism community continues to change its face under the auspices of the relevant ministries and development partners.
(Kampong Speu-Koh Kong): The Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Rural Development, as well as relevant partner organizations, have been working to promote government, environment and sustainable management of natural resources in Cambodia's protected areas through an innovative management system. Accountability and accountability, within the framework of institutional improvement, and coordination between various stakeholders.
Mr. Khin Meng Kheang said that the Ministry of Environment continues to examine the possibility of providing technical support to strengthen the infrastructure in the ecotourism community, such as hospitality, tour guides or accommodation, tents and other collaborative work. With relevant ministries, especially the Ministry of Tourism.
According to Mr. Khin Meng Kheang, the protected area community has received many benefits from participating in the conservation of natural resources, they can also collect annual non-timber forest products such as: honey, fruits, mushrooms, vegetables, etc., which can provide additional income. To the people.
Mr. Touch Mak, President of Community Protection and Ecotourism Area, Chambok Commune, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province, said that Chambok Ecotourism Community was established on January 9, 2003 and covers a total area of 3,451 hectares. 637 families are grouped together as community members. Previously, no community was formed in this area, which is full of about 400 coal-fired kilns, which destroy nearly 1 million cubic meters of forest per year.
He said that in the past, 19 communities in the Chambok protected area and ecotourism area received more than 10,000 national and international visitors, earning between $ 25,000 and $ 30,000 a year. Access roads to community areas are also easier under construction by the Ministry of Rural Development.
The Royal Government of Cambodia also intends to turn some protected areas with tourism potential into eco-tourism areas to meet the growing demand for tourism and the needs of the people for tourism.
With the right policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the community will prosper in the future. You will make the right decision for the future of the community.
