German Agriculture and Diplomatic Officers in Cambodia Urge Farmers to Strengthen Mango Growing Techniques for Export to Europe (Video inside) (Kampong Speu) In accordance with the standards and quality, especially increase the planting of mangoes out of season to increase exports in all seasons and increase value added, as well as to export to the European market.
German officials and ambassadors and mango exporters made such a visit during a visit to the Mang Rich Farm in Kampong Speu province on 31 January 2022 with the participation of the German Ambassador to Cambodia. Department of Agriculture and Mango Growers from 5 provinces in Cambodia.
Oknha Hun Lak, CEO of Richfarm Asia, said that after the German ambassador to Cambodia visited the mango plantation this morning, the ambassador was interested and wanted to try exporting to Europe and Germany. Therefore, he urged mango farmers to change from conventional mango cultivation to modernization in accordance with the standards required by the export market, so as not to worry about the lack of market at harvest time.
He said that each year, Cambodian mangoes produce more than 1 million tons or nearly 2 million tons, but those mangoes do not seem to meet the standards yet, especially mangoes that are exported to Europe.
"The reason we have to do this is because we want high quality mangoes to export to the international market, so today we have a model to present to the embassy as well as the board," he said. Delegates as well as farmers' communities from 5 provinces, 25 representatives directly inspected, and we have a presentation on the mango season, as well as management of the use of agricultural inputs. Dont we call this good farming Cam Gap.
Christin Berger, German Ambassador to Cambodia, said that the Rich Farm Mango Farm is the only mango plantation in Cambodia that grows mangoes using modern techniques and modern irrigation systems. He wants farmers to change their habits to grow good agricultural crops to make this mango has a high standard for export to the European market, especially the visiting plantation owners who have now experienced the problem of falling mango prices and no. Sales market.
Mr. Ngin Chhay, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, urges farmers and investors to strengthen and increase mango cultivation according to technical standards, especially more off-season mangoes, in order to expand the market to Europe in addition to the Chinese market. .
He added that in the past, Cambodian farmers have also tried to grow mangoes out of season, but have not been very successful due to weather conditions that require additional technical studies.
He encourages farmers to unite as a community to facilitate training and to connect with the private sector to facilitate processing for export.
According to the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, the area under mango cultivation in Cambodia is more than 100,000 hectares and yields about 2 million tons per year.
