Hav Viseth, Deputy Director General of the Fisheries Administration, said that the Chinese side had temporarily agreed to allow three fish farms and one fish processing facility to be able to export, but that the shortcomings required by the Chinese side must be corrected before the division. The two signed a joint protocol to allow Cambodian trout to go to China.
He pointed out that the three farms and one processing plant that have been inspected and evaluated by the General Administration of Customs of China must be prepared to improve according to the shortcomings raised by the Chinese side and make a report showing the improvement before the day. February 25, 2022 Non-compliant farms will not be registered by the Chinese Customs for export to China.
He urged the owners of the three fish farms and one fish processing plant to hurry up and fill in the missing report in time to send it to China.
"Whether or not fish can be exported this year depends on the documents provided by the farm from the processing plant provided by the Chinese side in a timely manner," he said. "Hopefully, Cambodian trout will be able to export only if the two sides sign a joint protocol to export fish from Cambodia to China."
A meeting between the working group of the Fisheries Administration and the delegation of the General Administration of Customs of China to monitor and evaluate the safety, quality and hygiene requirements of Cambodian trout for export to China was held on video starting from 20 to January 28, 2022.
During these 9 days, inspected 3 fish farms, inspected and evaluated 2 national laboratories and 2 fish processing facilities and met with representatives of Phnom Penh Autonomous Port and Customs at Sihanoukville Port Release fish to ensure that both rearing, processing and transportation are safe, hygienic and of good quality.
He said that for farms that want to export to China, they need to apply for registration for inspection and evaluation next time.
He said that if Cambodian trout are allowed to be exported to China, it will open the market for Cambodian aquaculture and be a favorable opportunity for Cambodian aquaculture because Cambodia is a favorable location for fish farming in both climate and water. This sector promotes national economic growth and provides additional employment to Cambodians.
"In order for this Cambodian trout product to be good, it is necessary for Cambodian agriculturists to abide by the guidelines for good aquaculture practice, to manage breeding work, to provide good quality feed, water and environment in a hygienic manner. "As for the processing plant, when the fish reach the factory, it has to be of good quality, safe and hygienic." Mr. Hav Viseth further confirmed.
