BEIJING: Looking at the flow of global trade and investment in recent years, the idea of severing ties with China is baseless.
Some of China's economic data and multilateral economic and trade achievements in 2021, released in a series of recent releases, also confirm this. Prominent "scores" of China's trade process in 2021 fully show that China has always fulfilled its promise of openness and closer ties with the world.
This further shows that China and the United States, two of the world's largest economies, are increasingly dependent on each other in trade. The so-called China-US economic and trade secession is untrue and ridiculous.
On the other hand, the stable recovery of the Chinese market has provided greater investment opportunities for enterprises around the world. Over the past two years, the Chinese market has been the "highlight" of the financial statements of many international enterprises. This is also the real reason why the United States has raised tariffs on Chinese goods in recent years, and has not been able to prevent US enterprises from investing in China.
