Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a flyover on National Road 5 near Freedom Park
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, January 31, 2022, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will open the construction site of a new flyover in Phnom Penh to facilitate and relieve traffic congestion that is growing rapidly.
It should be noted that along with the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the flyover, the Russey Keo cable-stayed concrete bridge crossing the Tonle Sap River connecting National Road No. 5 to Chroy Changva Satellite City as well as National Road No. 6 has been completed.
According to the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, as of January 2022, the reinforced concrete cable-stayed bridge of the Russey Keo cable across the Tonle Sap has reached nearly 64 percent. The bridge is scheduled for completion in March 2023.
The reinforced concrete cable-stayed bridge across the Tonle Sap River has a modern style. There are 4 large pillars up to 40 meters high for hanging cables. The bridge is expected to cost about $ 35 million. The bridge is 922 meters long and 20.5 meters wide.
