2021 Despite 19 Kovid Crisis, Tycoon Try Pheap's Nine Companies Remain Strong With More Than 2,000 Employees
(Phnom Penh): 2021, both in Cambodia and in the world, is a year that suffered a severe social and economic crisis due to the epidemic of Kovid 19. Despite the hardships caused by the global epidemic, the nine companies of Tycoon Try Pheap remain strong with more than 2,000 employees.
This weekend, Try Pheap Group held a meeting to review the work of 2021 and 2022 under the chairmanship of Duke Try Pheap, General Director of Try Pheap Company and with the participation of the leaders, team leaders and divisions of the nine companies.
The conference reviewed the achievements and the challenges and issues that have arisen in 2021. The conference also reviewed the work plan for 2022 to improve the company's operations.
At the conference, the company highlighted some of the company's challenges posed by the 19 Kovid outbreak. But under the strategy of Duke Try Pheap as CEO, accompanied by careful participation, the company was able to overcome all the difficulties.
Tycoon Try Pheap said that his nine companies that are currently operating are road construction companies, transportation companies, oil companies, rubber plantations and tourism companies.
According to Tycoon Try Pheap, the best-performing company is a rubber plantation company with an area of about 6,000 hectares in the district between Preah Vihear province. The duke said most of the rubber was exported and the prices were still good.
