There are 7 candidates who passed the exam for each capital-province by passing the QCM writing test and general knowledge interview related to the election and who have the following positions:
First: Chairman of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission Second: Deputy Chairman of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission Third: Member in charge of Administration Fourth: Member in charge of Finance Fifth: Member in charge of Election Operations and Technique 6: Member in charge of Legal Services, Dispute and Electoral Security, and 7th: Member in charge of Education, Information and Public Relations.
In this selection exam, a number of NEC civil servants working at the Capital-Provincial Election Secretariat (LEC) applied for the exam and passed as the Chairman or Vice-Chairman or a member of the Capital Commission. Provincial Election Commission (CEC), which is why some of the Capital-Provincial Election Secretariat vacancies.
Pursuant to the spirit of Article 23 of the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the National Election Committee, the NEC shall appoint the Chairman and Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (NEC) by assigning duties to the Secretary General. NEC Secretary in preparing this composition.
In the process of preparing the above composition, the Secretary General of the NEC shall give priority to the Chief of the Division of the CEC who is not included in the composition of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) or, if necessary, the Secretary General The NEC may review the composition of the candidates for the position of Chairman or Vice President or any member who has sufficient qualifications, qualifications and abilities to fill the vacancy.
The 175 members of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission will be on duty from Tuesday, February 1, 2022 to Thursday, June 30, 2022 for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election.
