Despite the challenges, China will be able to successfully host the 2022 Winter Olympics
The official opening ceremony of the 24th Winter Olympics will be held on February 4, 2022 in Beijing, China. Beijing will be the first city in history to host the Summer Olympics and the Winter Olympics.
About 3,000 athletes from about 90 countries will compete in 109 different sports, which will run until February 20, 2022. Receiving the right to host such a world sporting event certainly brings pride to the host country, but at the same time it brings burdens and challenges.
But as the Games draw closer, we also see the emergence of new challenges for China. The emergence of a new Kovid-19 virus, Omikrong, that has spread around the world is posing a new threat to the hosting of the World Games. However, past experience in preventing Kovid-19 and high vaccination rates among the Chinese population will help China overcome this challenge successfully.
In other words, the United States and some of its allies are using the Winter Olympics as a tool to hinder and hinder China's progress, especially to tarnish China's image and isolate China on the international stage. In fact, the Olympic Games are a forum for all nations to participate in the cause of sports, peace, friendship and community together, regardless of political interests.
