Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Vaccination is a key measure to end the crisis of Kovid 19 and re-launch socio-economic activities (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, said that vaccination It is a key measure to control the spread and escalation of the Kovid 19 crisis and the resumption of socio-economic activities in a safe and normal way.
According to the "National Strategic Plan for Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign to Create Socio-Economic Immunity in Cambodia by 2021", launched in May 2021 by the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Launched a plan to find 19 vaccines against Kovid to be delivered to the people by 2022.
However, the vaccine alone will not end the global epidemic. Continued implementation of public health measures to prevent the spread of the disease remains essential, such as testing, adherence to precautionary measures, wearing a mask, hand washing and keeping a safe distance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this remark on the occasion that he and the Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia presided over the reception and handing over of 300,000 doses of Kovid 19 AstraZenica vaccine with the assistance of the Government and the people. Polish people on the morning of January 30, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "In fact, vaccination is a key measure to control the spread and the end of the Kovid 19 crisis and the resumption of socio-economic activities along the way. "New normal, safe."
Regarding the vaccination process, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also mentioned, for example, that with the vaccination rate of about 90 percent of the total population of 16 million people as of January 20, 2022, Cambodia can control Outbreaks reduce hospitalizations and mortality rates to a minimum and maintain socio-economic activity.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as a result, although Cambodia experienced the community event of February 20, 2021, which just closed on December 20, 2021 recently, the success of the national vaccination campaign has made Cambodia's economy is growing faster than expected.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia highlighted that, in fact, the Cambodian economy is projected to grow to 3% by 2021 and is projected to continue to grow by more than 5% in 2022 through full national opening and return to normalcy. The normalization of socio-economic activities in all sectors.
As of the night of January 29, 2022, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of National Defense vaccinated 14,351,805 Kovid 19 vaccines to civil servants, citizens and the armed forces across the country. Including:
The Prime Minister made this remark on the occasion of receiving the 300,000 doses of 19 strains of AstraZenica with the help of the Polish government and people on the morning of January 30, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that "As the chair of ASEAN for 2022, Cambodia is ready to promote cooperation in all areas of friendship and solidarity between Cambodia-Poland and ASEAN-Poland and between Cambodia. "The European Union and ASEAN - the European Union to be stronger and more cohesive."
He added that Cambodia would like to encourage the Republic of Poland and the European Union to continue to support Cambodia and ASEAN and encourage Polish businessmen and investors as well as the European Union to increase business, trade and investment, especially in the agricultural sector. The education and tourism industry in Cambodia as well as in the entire ASEAN region.
Cambodia and the Republic of Poland are old friends who have had diplomatic relations since 1967. For more than 50 years, Cambodia and the Republic of Poland have maintained good diplomatic, educational, socio-economic and trade relations.
Taking this opportunity, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia expressed his gratitude to the Republic of Poland for always providing assistance and support to Cambodia as well as the entire ASEAN region in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
