This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Receives 300,000 Doses of Vaccine to Assist the Polish Government at the Peace Palace
(Phnom Penh): The 300,000 doses of Kovid 19 AstraZenica vaccine, funded by the Polish government and people, arrived in Cambodia at 00:08 am on January 30, 2022. This was confirmed by Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health to Fresh News.
The handover ceremony was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia on the morning of January 30, 2022 at the Peace Palace. The vaccine was scheduled to arrive in Cambodia on January 25, but was delayed until today due to weather conditions.
The Kovid 19 vaccine is an essential tool in addition to health measures to combat the Kovid 19 pandemic and to protect the lives of people from global communicable diseases in the 21st century. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Commander-in-Chief of the Battle of Kovid 19, has decided to vaccinate the people of Kovid 19 as the most important task for overcoming Kovid 19 and protecting the lives of the people.
The advent of a large number of vaccines has enabled Cambodia to successfully vaccinate its people ahead of schedule. As of January 28, Cambodia had vaccinated more than 14 million people, according to the report. Of these, nearly 14 million were injected in two doses, more than 5 million were injected in three doses, and more than 420,000 were injected in four doses.
Through the rapid vaccination of the people, Cambodian society has become more integrated, and by continuing to adhere to the implementation of health measures, Cambodia has effectively reduced the spread of the virus and opened up social activities. All sectors again in November 2021.
The rapid vaccination, the overcoming of Kovid 19 and the re-opening of Cambodia's socio-economic activities have led to the appreciation and appreciation of the leadership of the Royal Government and the participation of all citizens by the organization. World Health, development partners and friendly countries.
Ms. Ly Ilen, President of the World Health Organization in Cambodia, once praised the right decision of the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia to order and make enough vaccines for people to inject. She also praised the Cambodian people who have a high spirit to participate in the fight against Kovid 19, especially the spirit to get vaccinated as determined by the Royal Government.
The vaccine will be handed over and received by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the morning of January 30, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
