In response to calls from Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky for Western leaders not to panic over the massive deployment of Russian troops near the border, Putin and French President Vladimir Putin Emmanuel Macron has agreed to try to ease tensions in Eastern Europe.
However, neither Vladimir Putin nor his European counterparts or even the United States are seen to have shown the same intentions in easing the weeks-long heatwave. Putin also stressed in a telephone conversation with McCormack on Friday that Russia "has no plans to invade" Ukraine.
However, Biden claimed that the United States would send small troops to help increase the presence of NATO forces in Eastern Europe as the overall situation remained fragile. The United States already has tens of thousands of troops in Eastern Europe, and the Pentagon has announced that the number of Russian troops and weapons deployed now could pose a threat to Ukraine as a whole.
