Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Receiving 300,000 Doses of Vaccine to Assist the Polish Government at the Peace Palace
The handover ceremony was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia on the morning of January 30, 2022 at the Peace Palace. The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Techo on the occasion of receiving the vaccine:
* Cambodia considers Kovid-19 vaccination as a strategic priority and highly appreciates the sharing of vaccines with each other in an effort to accelerate global vaccination.
In this spirit, I always take the time to personally receive the Kovid-19 vaccine to express my gratitude and appreciation for the humanitarian kindness of the friendly country.
On this occasion, on behalf of the people and the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to thank the gift of the vaccine, which reflects the noble care and commitment of the people and Government of the Republic of Poland in the fight against the epidemic of Kovid. -19 in Cambodia as well as in the whole world.
In fact, vaccination is a key measure to control the spread and escalation of the Kovid-19 crisis and to re-launch socio-economic activities in a safe and normal way.
* For example, with a vaccination rate of about 90% of the population of 16 million as of January 20, 2022, Cambodia can control the epidemic, reduce hospitalization and mortality. At a low level and able to maintain the process of socio-economic activities.
As a result, despite Cambodia experiencing the community event of 20 February 2021, which just ended on 20 December 2021, the recent success of the National Vaccination Campaign has boosted the Cambodian economy beyond expectations. Leave.
* In fact, the Cambodian economy is projected to grow by up to 3% in 2021 and is projected to continue to grow by more than 5% in 2022 through the full opening of the country and the return to normalcy. Socio-economic activities in all sectors.
In this context, vaccination will continue to be a key measure, and the assistance of the Kovid-19 AstraZeneca vaccine of the people and government of the Republic of Poland will now make a significant contribution to the fight against Kovid-19, especially in the national dosing campaign. Encourage the Cambodian people throughout the country.
* I would like to remind you that Cambodia and the Republic of Poland are old friends who have had diplomatic relations since 1967. For more than 50 years, Cambodia and the Republic of Poland have maintained good diplomatic, educational, socio-economic and trade relations.
Taking this opportunity, Cambodia would like to thank the Republic of Poland for its continued assistance and support to Cambodia as well as the entire ASEAN region, both within the bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
* As chair of ASEAN for 2022, Cambodia is ready to promote cooperation in all areas of friendship and solidarity between Cambodia-Poland and ASEAN-Poland, as well as between Cambodia-EU and ASEAN-EU. More robust and cohesive.
* Cambodia also encourages the Republic of Poland and the European Union to continue to provide support to Cambodia and ASEAN, and to encourage Polish businessmen and investors, as well as the European Union, to increase business, trade and investment, especially in the agro-industry and education sectors. And tourism in Cambodia as well as in the entire ASEAN region.
