Cambodian diplomat tells UN Security Council that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Nay Pyi Taw is a mission to break the deadlock
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, in his capacity as Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair, briefed members of the United Nations Security Council (UNSC) on the current situation in Cambodia. Myanmar, made on video on the night of January 28, 2022.
While briefing on the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Myanmar, the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair highlighted the main objectives of the visit, including:
* (1): Re-engage with Nay Pyi Taw to find ways towards the implementation of the ASEAN Five-Point Consensus Agreement. An end to the violence and the continuation of the ceasefire by all parties are essential to building trust and creating a conducive environment for dialogue.
* (2) To ensure that the first visit of the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair to Myanmar can take place to facilitate the facilitation of dialogue by stakeholders.
* And (3): To ensure the safe and prompt delivery of humanitarian assistance to the most needy people in Myanmar.
