The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) is studying the connection of water transport from Tonle Bassac to the sea in Kep province (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, revealed that the Ministry has been studying Connect water transport from Phnom Penh to the sea, Kep province. This connection to facilitate the transportation of goods abroad by sea without passing through Vietnam.
At the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year and work directions for the new year on January 28, 2022, yesterday, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol revealed that the project to connect water transport from the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port to the sea in Kep province has already studied and he has already informed the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In addition, there were discussions on legal aspects with the Ministry of Water Resources regarding the Mekong River law, and there were no problems.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized, "We want to see progress in water transport, and some provinces, such as Takeo, will benefit from water transport from the Bassac River to the sea."
The transportation of goods into and out of Cambodia by sea from the sea to the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port is currently through Vietnam, the pottery, which requires the completion of procedures and is an obstacle for the transport by Waterways as well.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that the connection of the waterway from Tonle Bassac to the sea in Kep will bring many economic benefits for Cambodia. In particular, the connection of inland waterways to international markets.
The senior minister said the connection was to use existing natural waterways and the digging of new waterways to connect the sea to a distance of about 5 km.
However, this connection is still under study. But for Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, he wants to see this waterway network appear because it provides more benefits for Cambodia's transportation. International Analysis: The Beijing Winter Olympics are not a stage play for American politicians
