The United States, which could not appeal the decision, called it "extremely disappointing" and said it was still calling for WTO legal reform. Saying these laws are being used to "protect" China.
The figure is reflected in the WTO's 87-page arbitration ruling on the level of countermeasures that Beijing could propose in its dispute with Washington over a subsidized import duty (CVD). Of the United States on some Chinese products.
The dispute erupted in 2012 when the WTO set up a task force to try to resolve a lawsuit filed by China over what the country calls unjust tariffs by the United States on Chinese goods.
Washington has defended its additional tariffs on Chinese products ranging from pepper to tires and solar panels, saying they were being sold at a discount to help Chinese companies capture market share.
The WTO's dispute settlement body ruled in China's favor, and the ruling was upheld by an appeals verdict in 2014 that paved the way for China to withdraw its retaliatory tariffs.
(Oddar Meanchey): Cassava products of farmers in Oddar Meanchey province are seen as a market, as officials claim that at the beginning of 2022, cassava exports to Thailand will be close to 100,000 tons throughout the year. By 2021, exports will be close to 260,000 tons.
According to Mr. Sot Sisok Kheang, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of January 28, 2022, that by January 2022, cassava of farmers in Oddar Meanchey province has been exported to the country. Thailand through O'Smach international port in Samrong city and Choam international port in Anlong Veng district, 80,000 tons, while the whole year 2021 exports 257,014 tons.
