He said that wet cassava costs 270 to 290 riel per kilogram, while dry cassava costs an average of 740 riel per kilogram to nearby areas due to transportation costs.
Mr. Sot Sisokkheang spoke with interest about the increase in cassava yield compared to last year. He said that the increase in cassava yield this year is due to the change of varieties in the past, farmers have problems due to mosaic disease on cassava crops across the country, farmers planted to fall yields.
The director of the department said that through cooperation with GIZ in the region, new varieties that are resistant to mosaic disease have been planted on outstanding farmers so that they can produce seeds for sale in the area and now Made everywhere in Oddar Meanchey to sell trees to farmers in the district in Oddar Meanchey.
