Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth recommends 10 points for the Ministry of Public Works to continue to implement effectively for 2022
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, closed the meeting to review the work of public works and transportation in 2021 and the work direction in 2022, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance. Issued 10 important recommendations for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to continue to implement effectively in 2022.
The closing ceremony of the meeting was held at the Ministry on the evening of January 28, 2022, with the participation of Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister, Minister of Public Works and Transport, as well as other relevant officials.
The 10 main recommendations of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth include:
* Fifth, continue to push for the completion of the sub-decree on the management of railway land and the crossing point between the railway and the road in order to effectively manage the railway land and avoid encroachment and continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Land Management. Urbanization and construction to promote land registration of the remaining railway stations.
* Sixth: Continue to push for the completion of the draft law on inland waterway and port to improve the efficiency of comprehensive management and promote better inland waterway transport operations and port business, including Continue to push for the completion of the draft sub-decree on the establishment of the National Committee in response to the oil spill.
* Seventh: Continue to pay attention to the enforcement of road traffic laws by using the program to remove driver's license points and fine road traffic offenses on mobile phones, and continue to promote the development of software (APP) to monitor information management, history Means, progress and evaluation of project implementation from the opening of the construction site to the official inauguration.
* Eighth: Continue to cooperate with development partners and relevant ministries and institutions to expedite the development of policies, laws and regulations related to the public and transport sectors and logistics, which are required by the conditions of globalization and internal integration. In the country and in the region.
* 9th: Continue to promote the training and development of human resources in higher education and technical skills in public works and transport and logistics through Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport, including the strengthening of the capacity of infrastructure construction experiments in construction and public laboratories. And so on.
* 10th: Continue to improve the quality of services to the people and push public services closer to the people, as well as continue to introduce and implement automation systems for new public services. Under the control of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
He added that although Cambodia has made some good progress, the Kovid 19 crisis has disrupted some important work, especially some important projects that have not been completed as planned. The public works to address challenges and accelerate a number of other tasks that are strategically important for the complete and timely rehabilitation and promotion of national economic growth.
