Ministry of Tourism: Chinese New Year this year, resorts and tourist destinations must not be overcrowded
(Phnom Penh): In order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 during the Chinese New Year in 2022, tourist resorts and tourist destinations must not be overcrowded.
According to the circular issued on January 28, 2022, the Ministry of Tourism has instructed the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to continue to strengthen the management of resorts and tourist destinations in case of overcrowding. The storage capacity of the Department of Tourism must be reported to the Ministry of Tourism and the Capital-Provincial Administration immediately to take measures to temporarily suspend the activities of the resort and tourist destination.
The circular of the Ministry of Tourism states that "In case of accumulation in excess of the storage capacity at resorts and tourist destinations, the Department of Tourism must immediately report to the Ministry of Tourism and the Capital-Provincial Administration to take measures to suspend the activities of those resorts and tourist destinations." "Temporarily."
In addition to the above guidelines, the Ministry of Tourism also instructed the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to promote the strict and strict implementation of all measures set by the Royal Government to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially measures. 3 Protect and 3 not be consistent.
According to the Ministry of Tourism, the Capital-Provincial Departments of Tourism must strengthen the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum operating standards (SOP) procedures in accordance with the new normalization route introduced by the Ministry of Tourism on tourism businesses in order to maintain business stability and Ensure safety for national and international tourists.
In addition, the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism must encourage business owners and tourist destinations to organize incentives for vaccinated tourists, while all staff must be vaccinated according to the Ministry of Health. .
The Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism shall cooperate with traders and tour operators to improve the quality of tourism products, maintain the environment-hygiene and maintain the prices of products and services appropriately. All prices for accommodation, food and other services must be clearly written in the table to inform guests in advance to avoid excessive pricing. In case of non-compliance with the posted schedule, the business owner shall be liable before the law in force.
The Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism shall set up a working group to disseminate and promote the implementation of this circular in a comprehensive and comprehensive manner to tour operators, and to compile a summary report of tourist statistics at various resorts and destinations and send Come to the Ministry of Tourism on time every day.
Please be informed that in 2022, the traditional Chinese and Vietnamese New Year will be held from January 31 to February 3.
