(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, sees that the possibility of a war between Russia and Ukraine, a territory under Russian rule in the past can not explode.
In the face of the tense situation between Russia and Ukraine, as well as NATO in recent days, the Royal Academy of Cambodia, one of the research institutes of Cambodia, has organized a roundtable discussion on "Tensions between NATO and the Russian Federation."
The forum, which was held on the morning of January 28, 2022, was attended by four expert speakers, including: Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament of Cambodia and two other veteran journalists. Mr. Pen Bona and Mr. Puy Kea.
The four speakers, historians and geographers, discussed issues related to the Russia-Ukraine conflict, NATO intervention and examined the possibility of a war between Russia and Ukraine.
"Now the confrontation between NATO and the Russian Federation is in the red line," Pen Bona said.
The journalist noted that NATO saw Russia's adversary, Nato, move closer to Russia, reclaiming some of the former Soviet-occupied territories. As a member, Russia is deeply concerned about its national security and must work to prevent NATO expansion.
"Russia, he understands that his national security is under threat, so Russia, he must determine. Recently, NATO is also annexing Ukraine, which is attached to the Russian fence. "Thus, the red line that Russia must draw now is that NATO cannot take Ukraine as its member because Ukraine is Russia's national security front." This is Mr. Pen Bona's confirmation.
As a graduate of Russia, Dr. Sok Touch Hak is well aware of Russia's problems with Ukraine. Sok Touch sees Russia's current reaction to Ukraine as a way to prevent Ukraine from joining NATO, which is a major threat to Russia's national security.
Sok Touch seems highly optimistic about Russia's ability to arm and military. For Sok Touch, if a war breaks out, NATO will not be able to defeat Russia, because Russia's weapons technology is very modern.
However, Sok Touch believes that the war between Russia and Ukraine can not happen. Mr. Sok Touch stated that "the war in Ukraine can not happen because the United States and Europe know very well how to cook shrimp. "The victims are Ukraine."
Pen Bona also saw that the war between Russia and Ukraine could not take place, he saw many efforts to reduce the heat between Russia and Ukraine.
"We see clear efforts to resolve the issue, despite the tensions, but I believe that all parties do not want to go to war because he understands that this war will lead to war," he said. "All losses."
With just one week to go, the world-class Winter Olympics, the Beijing Winter Olympics, will be grandly inaugurated in Beijing, a city of both traditional and modern style. China is the only city in the world today that hosts both the Summer and Winter Olympics.
Although China is a major sporting country, winter sports are not a traditional Chinese sport, as many areas in southern China do not have snowfall, so the population is not very high. It is not popular to play winter sports or snow sports, and there are not as many athletes who specialize in snow sports as in summer sports.
Therefore, when proposing to host the 2022 Winter Olympics, Chinese President Xi Jinping proposed a goal, or rather a contract for China, through the hosting of the China Winter Olympics. Will encourage and encourage 300 million Chinese people to participate in snow sports
It is noteworthy that all the stadiums for this event are powered by wind power, which is 100% green, a new record in the history of the Olympics. On the other hand, many stadium facilities will be permanently reserved for athletes' training and as a public venue for the first time in the history of the Winter Olympics. Well.
It is true that in the run-up to China's Olympics, some Western politicians have boycotted diplomacy or found all sorts of excuses with the intention of disrupting, but the overwhelming voice of truth opposes sports politics politics. And support the protection of the purity of the sport and the Olympic spirit echoed around the world.
