Ministry issues decision on minimum standard operating procedures (SOPs) along new normal trajectories in markets
(Phnom Penh): With the support of Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Combating Kovid-19 Ministry of Tourism, the National Commission for Clean City Assessment on January 28, 2022 issued a decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for four types of markets: supermarkets, small markets, public markets, and unregulated markets.
Issued a Decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for four markets in order to ensure that all market businesses ensure the safety and public health of suppliers and consumers. Effective in delivering customer confidence and satisfaction.
The minimum standard operating procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for the four markets are:
1: Decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal path for large-scale supermarkets.
2: Decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for small markets.
3. Decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for the public market.
4: Decision on Minimum Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for erratic markets.
