(Kep): Mr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province, said that in 2021, when Cambodia faced the Kovid 19 crisis, the authorities have not solved enough problems for the people, but the team will continue to work hard to help. Citizens, while some problems that can not be solved will be submitted to the head of the Royal Government for further resolution.
Mr. Som Piseth made this remark during a meeting to review the results of the work of the Royal Government Working Group in Kep Province to review and support the implementation of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Political Program and Strategy for 2021 and to set the direction for the implementation of the year. 2022 Presided over by Mr. Chin Bun Sean, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kep Province on January 27, 2022.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Chin Bun Sean expressed his support and approval for the report of Kep Provincial Administration and commended the efforts and attention to perform the duties and responsibilities in accordance with the relevant laws and regulations in a responsible spirit and achieve appropriate results. Proudly, although the response to the needs of local people is not 100 percent.
But responded to and addressed in a timely manner the priority needs of a large number of people as well. In particular, for the remaining issues that have not been resolved, the team will continue to resolve.
Mr. Chin Bun Sean also introduced 5 important points, including:
* First, the Board of Governors of districts, communes, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, and village chiefs must increase their responsibility for providing public services to the people in a transparent, accountable, non-political manner, promoting better and more effective local development.
* Second: The Board of Governors, districts, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, village chiefs must cooperate to prevent all kinds of gambling, drug problems, theft, gangsters for the safety of villages, communes and sangkats.
* Third: All Royal Government working groups must be strengthened at the local level every 1 or 2 months to study and understand the well-being of the local people.
* Fourth: Commune / Sangkat chiefs, village chiefs must check any people who have lost their ID cards or have not yet made ID cards, it is recommended to get ID cards in time for the 5th mandate election on June 5, 2022. This.
* Fifth: Disseminate and educate local people to know how to maintain hygiene in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health in measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 must be advised to vaccinate everyone.
