WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States on Thursday called on China to use its influence to persuade Russia to pursue a diplomatic solution to the Ukraine crisis, which is at risk of war. This was released by Reuters on Friday, January 28, 2022.
The call came after US Secretary of State Antony Blinken met with Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi by telephone on Wednesday night, with the Chinese side urging him to do so. All parties involved should exercise restraint and refrain from any actions that could aggravate the situation.
"We call on Beijing to use its influence to push Moscow to follow the mechanism," said Victoria Nuland, Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs. "Diplomacy because any conflict in Ukraine is not a good thing for China."
