Speaking to Fresh News on January 27, Oknha Sin Chanthy, President of the Cambodian Logistics Association, said that at present, the freight by rail is still limited because there is no connection from the train station to the container terminal. The current speed of the train is still limited, while the cost of transport by rail and by car is similar, which makes the carrier choose to use the car.
If Cambodia's railways are to be developed into highways in the future and connect from the production site to the port, it will encourage freighters to return to the railways to reduce costs and time savings.
"Using the railway, we have to take the goods or containers from the factory or production place to the station, so we have to use a car, and when we go to Sihanoukville, we have to take the car to transport the container from the station," he said. "Going to another port to do other inspections takes a long time."
