WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US government on Wednesday issued a warning to companies to be careful about doing business in Myanmar on the grounds that they could be at risk of involvement with Myanmar's military government. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, January 27, 2022.
A statement signed by six relevant US ministries stated that companies involved in businesses run by the Myanmar military regime could be at risk of engaging in activities that put them in serious trouble. Financial and legal reputation.
Investors and traders are especially warned to stay away from state-owned enterprises, gems and precious metals, real estate and construction projects, and arms-related businesses, according to the industry statement. All of these are considered to be the main sources of economic resources for the Myanmar military regime.
It should be noted that the above statement is not a regulation to be followed, it is just a guide. But the warning comes as many large foreign companies investing in Myanmar have begun to withdraw in the face of military rule.
