MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian troops will leave Belarus when joint military exercises between the two former Soviet territories close in February. This is according to the Belarusian Ministry of Defense, quoted by Reuters on Thursday, January 27, 2022.
In a statement issued on Thursday, the Belarusian Defense Ministry briefly stated that "once the joint military exercises end, the Russian army will leave Belarus."
The deployment of Russian troops to Belarus has been accused by the West of being part of Moscow's escalation of military influence amid fears that Russia could use Belarusian territory to launch attacks on Ukraine. The United States has warned that this could happen in mid-February.
