The Royal Government of Cambodia and development partners discuss and evaluate the macroeconomic situation and the global and regional economic outlook, this year the Cambodian economy will recover by 5.6%.
Minister Vongsey Visoth said that the current talks are aimed at consulting with Cambodia's development partners on the assessment of the global environment and economic situation in the region and in Cambodia, which is in the process of living. New patterns after the global epidemic of Kovid-19 declined.
This assessment is a foregone conclusion, without delay, to prepare the necessary policies and response measures for Cambodia's economic recovery in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as To withstand and address risks and challenges as well, based on the principle of best preparedness to ensure that Cambodian ships can cross the coast safely in the medium term.
He stressed that in order to build a more competitive and resilient Cambodian economy, Cambodia needs strong, intelligent and clean state institutions to lead in-depth reforms in all areas effectively and efficiently.
The representative of the development partners pointed out that the global economy started to recover in 2021 after a sharp contraction in 2020 and is estimated to achieve a growth rate of 5.9% in 2021 due to the introduction of supportive policies. Continuing and continuing vaccination at the global, regional and national levels aims to mitigate the effects of the Kovid-19 crisis.
In addition, development partners also provide key inputs to take into account the Royal Government's priority policy direction to contribute to the promotion of socio-economic development in order to achieve strong growth as before the crisis and strengthen resilience. The resilience of the economy as a whole.
The key sectors that should be a priority for boosting Cambodia's economic dynamics in and after the Kovid-19 context include: health, education, skills development, logistics, infrastructure, small and medium enterprise development. , Digital sector, green development and social protection system, especially the continuation of public administration reform.
(Dubai, United Arab Emirates): Cambodia's Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak has asked Russia to encourage Russian investors to invest in Cambodia to boost the economy and trade between Cambodia and Russia. Mr. Pan Sosak highlighted some important areas that want Russian investors to invest in Cambodia, including: agricultural vehicle production, food production and processing, transportation - logistics and technology.
The Minister of Commerce made the request during a meeting with the Deputy Minister of Commerce and Industry of Russia on January 26, 2022 in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, where the Minister is leading a delegation to celebrate National Day. Cambodia at the World Expo 2020.
Mr. Pan Sosak spoke about Cambodia's economic growth over the last two decades, as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia's policy to promote trade activities, attract investment and negotiate new market openings under regional trade agreements. For example, the recent bilateral free trade agreements that Cambodia has reached include the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement.
The Minister also highlighted that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has achieved immunization of about 90 percent of the country's population, which is a motivating factor for the Royal Government of Cambodia to start all economic activities. Sectors and reopening the country to attract investment and tourism to restore economic activity after the Kovid-19 crisis.
In response, the Russian Deputy Prime Minister accepted the Cambodian Minister's request, promising to bring the Cambodian proposal to the Russian Federation's tourist business to visit and invest in Cambodia.
He added that Russia will continue to cooperate with Cambodia in a number of key areas, requesting relevant sectors such as science, technology, automotive, agriculture, transportation and logistics, and education to work directly with the ministry. Relevant institutions of Cambodia.
The Deputy Minister also congratulated the Royal Government of Cambodia on the achievement of the vaccination campaign against Kovid-19 and praised the attractive Cambodian pavilion. From the beautiful and long-standing cultural traditions of Cambodia.
At the same time, the Deputy Minister requested for direct communication between the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce and Industry of Russia to strengthen trade activities between the two countries for sustainable growth for the benefit of both peoples. Two countries. The Deputy Minister also invited the Cambodian Minister of Commerce to visit the Russian Federation at an appropriate time in the near future.
In conclusion, the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia accepted the proposal to visit the Russian Federation in the near future to strengthen economic, trade and investment relations between the two countries to achieve good results and achieve the expected results.
The senior minister stated that the registration of 5,291 special license plates earned 38 billion riels and the registration of 27,437 special license plates earned more than 30 billion riels.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also stated that since the opening of the registration of personal special license plates through the automation system on January 7, 2020 until the end of December 2021, the Inter-Ministerial Commission has registered 9,007 badges and received Revenue more than 71 billion riels.
It should be noted that on January 7, 2020, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport launched its own special license plate to create more options to use license plates for car owners and to raise more revenue for the nation. This license plate is different from other license plates in that the car owner can set the letters and numbers as he wants and is a unique license plate.
This "personal special license plate" can be purchased for life by simply deleting the name when selling the car or they can sell the license plate when selling the car. The owner of the license plate can also keep the license plate for the children by simply exchanging information about who will continue to control the license plate.
