(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council has decided to reject the complaint related to the removal of names from the voter list because the plaintiffs did not appear in the hearing held this morning, Thursday, January 27, 2022.
Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council and President of the Trial Chamber, this morning held a hearing to review and decide on the complaint regarding the removal of names from the voter list, which was filed by Mr. Duong Vichet and Chea. The other four representatives are: Un Sokunthy, Duong Chenda Mony, Duong Virak and Duong Visal.
The above four people were upset after the National Election Committee (NEC) removed their names from the voter list in Phsar Chas. They complained to the NEC, but the NEC upheld the decision, so they appealed to the Constitutional Council.
Due to the absence of the plaintiffs, the Trial Chamber of the Constitutional Council decided to dismiss the complaint dated 22 January 2022.
According to the National Election Committee (NEC), the decision to delete the names of the five citizens was in accordance with the NEC's legal form and procedures.
The NEC has stated that according to Article 46 of the Law on the Election of the National Assembly, these five people did not meet the conditions of residence or lodging in the commune where they were to vote.
The NEC added that according to Article 51 of the Law on the Election of the National Assembly, the names of the five citizens were included in the voter list, which will be removed from the voter list because they Relocated from Sangkat Phsar Chas to Sangkat Stung Meanchey I.
