Samdech Techo Hun Sen Provides 150 Digital Digital Talent Scholarships for Bachelor of Digital Technology
(Phnom Penh): In the new academic year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to provide 150 scholarships to outstanding students to study for a bachelor's degree in digital technology through the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
In the academic year 2020-2021, this program has provided scholarships to 100 outstanding students, selected from a total of 2,938 students who applied for the exam.
According to the number of applications submitted last year, we see that this scholarship program is very attractive and attracts a lot of young people to study digital technology, a skill that is in high demand in the current job market and necessary. In the economic development and digital society in Cambodia.
This special scholarship program provides many benefits to students, including tuition, accommodation allowance of 320,000 riels per month for 4 years, as well as a laptop for study.
Eligibility Requests Candidates must have a high school diploma with an A or B or C, and a C with a A in science (mathematics and physics). Candidates must pass the exam in Mathematics, Logic and English. The scholarship is aimed at poor students from remote rural areas and female students.
