The taxman explained the reasons for the collection of tax revenue in 2021 to reach 2,781 million dollars, 24% higher than the plan of 538 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, explained the strategic plan and implementation of some important programs that make the tax collection in 2021 to receive 2,781 $ Million exceeded the plan by more than 24% to $ 538 million.
Confirmation of Mr. Kong Vibol in the meeting to summarize the results of tax collection for December and the year 2021 and the direction for further implementation of the General Department of Taxation this morning, January 26, 2022, chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance.
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister pays close attention to the management of tax revenue, always leading with wise guidance and sharp planning on the implementation of major reforms and strategic measures in the past. Which promotes and promotes fiscal compliance and ensures fair competition among the investment environment.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that in 2021, the General Department of Taxation has implemented its work and achieved important results such as:
* Developed and launched an electronic filing system to receive applications for administrative documents and documents by taxpayers simply scanning and submitting documents online to reduce the risk of the spread of Kovid-19 and as an additional option. To taxpayers who cannot afford or have trouble filing tax returns online
* Developed and launched a system for requesting tax certificates and tax certificates online without having to go directly to the General Department of Taxation. Value added and income tax exemption permit, etc.
* Participated in the preparation and effective implementation of the Royal Government's intervention measures related to the tax sector to continue to manage the impact on key sectors of the economy in the context of the crisis, the rehabilitation and promotion of Cambodia's economic growth during and after the crisis of disease. Covid-19
* Contributed to the successful and effective implementation of the 2021 plan within the framework of the 2019-2023 revenue collection strategy and the Royal Government's public financial management reform program.
Mr. Kong Vibol added that for 2022, the General Department of Taxation has set out the following important measures and strategies:
* Continue to strengthen the implementation of necessary measures as set out in the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023
* Continue the preparation of the new fiscal law by launching discussions at the relevant ministries and institutions to ensure that the organization is comprehensive and interconnected, as well as to respond to the growth of the national economy to ensure clarity, efficiency, legitimacy and consistency of Tax Revenue Management
* Continue to strengthen the implementation of measures to collect long-term tax debt and respect the decision to the Ministry of Economy and Finance in case of stubborn enterprises refuse to come to pay tax debts
* Continue to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection in potential sectors to ensure efficiency, transparency and fair competition.
* Encourage enterprises in the field of commercial gambling (casinos) to enter the tax registration and implement tax obligations properly in accordance with the laws and regulations on taxes and laws governing commercial gambling.
* Continue to modernize information technology systems and applications through the development and updating of new systems and applications.
* Continue to reform human resources and continue to strengthen the implementation of labor laws and regulations, and be gentle but firm, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and tax revenue management.
(Phnom Penh): A man who is a bus driver of the Phnom Penh City Bus Autonomous Public Transport Authority was called by his work unit to correct his mistake and required him to sign a contract to stop his immoral behavior after an argument With street motorcyclists. This is according to the press release of the Public Transport Authority, which was received by Fresh News on January 26, 2022.
According to a press release issued by the Public Transport Authority of Phnom Penh, on the afternoon of January 25, 2022, there was a case of a bus driver named Mao Sophal, a male bus driver with license plate number 37 3-0218. Argued with a motorcyclist on a public road around Total Petrol Station, 30 meters from Borey Santepheap 2, Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Sen Chey.
According to the press release, the cause was that the bus driver blew the horn to the motorcyclist who was driving in the middle of the road while the lane was a lane for traffic and also made the motorcyclist angry. Also ride and use some insulting words on the bus driver. At that time, the bus drivers could not control their anger and argued to overcome each other by using inappropriate gestures and words.
The statement added that the rude behavior and gestures of the driver had damaged the reputation of the public transport service unit, especially the ethical dignity of other bus drivers.
Phnom Penh City Bus Authority has promised to strengthen the discipline of the above driver by calling an employee named Mao Sophal to provide education and guidance and to make a contract to prevent him from committing such acts again. .
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Autonomous Public Transport Authority also called on all motorcyclists to contribute to the lane of traffic for vehicles to avoid accidents.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth sets out nine recommendations for the General Department of Taxation to implement more efficient revenue collection in 2022
This meeting was held at the National Tax Hall of the General Department of Taxation this morning, January 26, 2022, with the participation of Dr. Chou Vichit, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, as well as many other officials.
The nine main recommendations of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth include:
* First, encourage the General Department of Taxation to consider and make recommendations to the Ministry of Economy and Finance regarding policies, both in terms of revenue and aspects of social and economic promotion, in order to balance revenue management, and encourage The General Department of Taxation plays an active and proactive role in addition to the operator role in revenue collection management.
* Second, continue to improve the provision of services to taxpayers and evaluate the provision of services to taxpayers by reviewing and receiving feedback from taxpayers to reduce the maximum grievances from taxpayers.
* Third: Continue to organize and further improve the information technology system of the General Department of Taxation to be more efficient and more quality in order to make it easier and better for taxpayers and promote public services. Cell interface with relevant ministries and institutions
* Fourth: Continue to promote and mainstream the culture of paying taxes, strengthen the dissemination and implementation of new tax-related regulations to taxpayers and the public to explain and solve the difficulties and questions of the people.
* Sixth: Continuing cooperation and promoting consultation with relevant sectors as well as public opinion
* Seventh: Continue to strengthen and build the capacity of institutions and officials, as well as strengthen the code of ethics, discipline and work ethic to ensure efficiency and better service to taxpayers.
* Eighth: Strengthen and expand cooperation with other units under the Ministry of Economy and Finance and within the inter-ministerial-institutional framework and facilitate and create a better environment for business and business activities.
Ninth: Support and promote the continuation of the negotiation of agreements on the avoidance of double taxation (DTA) with the tax administrations of various countries and continue to enhance international tax cooperation relations.
Kandal Provincial Governor Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a Concrete Drainage System on National Road 21 and Street 210 in Takhmao City
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, on January 26, 2022, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of drainage and concrete system on National Road 21 and Road 210 in Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
According to the Governor of Kandal Province, the concrete drainage pipe that is under construction is 1.5 meters in diameter, 762 meters long, with 34 meters of 3 meters by 3 meters regulators along National Road No. 21, and the construction of steel fiber drainage 1 meter long, 232 meters long and 1.8 meters by 1.8 meters, 14 places along National Road 210.
The construction of the Luo and Rega roads along these two roads will cost about 2 billion riels or 600,000 dollars, which is the budget of the new Phnom Penh Borey.
On that occasion, the provincial governor thanked Mr. Oknha Bun Hay, General Director of Borey Phnom Penh Thmey, for responding to the call of the provincial administration to participate in these achievements, which is a good gesture and a good example. Invest in Kandal province and participate in the development of public works, construction, arts to serve the public.
At the same time, he also called on all people to understand and tolerate the impact when the construction site works and please cooperate with technical officials to make this construction site successful.
The Minister of Labor assigned the Kratie and Provincial Departments of Labor to recruit 20,000 workers to work for a large agricultural company in Kratie.
(Kratie Province): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, recommended to the Kratie Provincial Labor Department and other neighboring provincial labor departments to help recruit about 20,000 workers to work for Thagriko. (THAGRICO) which is in need of labor supply to process the harvesting chain and export packaging.
This recommendation was made during a visit to the production chain to visit workers and promote the implementation of the National Employment Policy at THAGRICO on the afternoon of January 25, 2022.
Thagriko is a large agricultural company in Snuol district, Kratie province, processing a variety of agricultural products, including bananas, mangoes, jackals, etc., mainly exported to the Chinese market.
During the visit of Minister Ith Sam Heng on that occasion, the representative of Tha Grico requested the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to help find 20,000 more workers to supply the needs of the harvesting chain and export packaging.
In response to this request, the Minister welcomed the need for manpower to work in the company, he recommended the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Kratie and other Departments of Labor and Vocational Training nearby to help promote the recruitment of labor. Meets the needs of the company.
The Minister also asked the company to help train more workers through the work and learning.
On the other hand, for foreign skilled workers with a quota of more than 10%, the company must submit a request to the Ministry stating in detail the foreign professional skills required and the reasons for the need to use foreign labor on 10 This%.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also asked the company to better comply with the working conditions and labor laws of Cambodia to reduce labor disputes leading to the harmonization of industrial relations between workers and companies.
