(Kampot): Kampot Provincial Administration cooperated with LAC on January 26, 2022 to hold a meeting on the implementation of the Media Law, which was held at Kampot Provincial Hall.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Ing Chhay, Deputy Governor of Kampot Province, Mr. Ok Samnang, Director of Kampot Provincial Information Department and Mr. Run Saray, Executive Director of LAC, and was attended by relevant government officials and journalists.
Mr. Ing Chhay said that the implementation of the law on journalists in Kampot province in the past has been good. Journalists have played an important role in helping to improve some of the issues related to the performance of duties and the role of officials in serving the people.
On that occasion, Mr. Run Saray said that LAC is a non-partisan, non-profit organization. The organization receives UK funding to provide legal services to help the poor in Cambodia.
Regarding the discussion on the media law, LAC has already implemented it in the capitals and provinces three times, in Phnom Penh, Battambang and Siem Reap in order to focus on three main points, including:
* First, strengthen the capacity of journalists to respect the law and professional ethics as journalists. * Second, to improve the field of journalism to be accurate, fair and accurate every time news is published. * Third, train journalists to understand the law on the media.
