Ms. O Vandin Receives USAID Delegates to Focus on Fighting HIV / AIDS, Malaria, Tuberculosis and Recent Infectious Diseases
The main purpose of this meeting is to learn about the Cambodian health system, discuss cooperation to strengthen health and fight against infectious diseases such as HIV, malaria, tuberculosis and other new infectious diseases.
The Secretary of State briefed the delegation on the status of Kovid-19 and the necessary and important campaigns that have been carried out in the past to control the epidemic and reopen the country in a new normal path.
This proud result comes from the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, through the launch of the Kovid-19 Strategic Plan and the Kovid-19 Vaccination and Irrigation Plan. .
At the request of Ms. O Vandin, USAID will continue to support the strengthening of the health sector, as well as examine the possibility of cooperation in digital health, transmission and non-communicable diseases.
The Secretary of State thanked USAID for its continued support of the Ministry of Health in implementing the Health Strategic Plan to promote the health of the people to global health coverage without leaving any population behind.
Under Joe Biden, the United States considered China its greatest geopolitical rival in the 21st century. The United States is currently in a difficult situation to protect its European allies in the event of a conflict with Russia and to monitor the actions of China and North Korea.
The fall of the Western-backed Afghan government at the hands of the Taliban has led some experts to speculate that China or Russia may be waking up to US influence. For example, President Vladimir Putin is well aware that Biden is now focusing on China, and China is happy that the United States is fighting Russia in Europe.
So the difficult question to answer here is what should the United States do if Russia attacks Ukraine and China attacks Taiwan at the same time?
Russia and NATO are on high alert, with each side stepping up troop deployments and weapons, as well as military exercises in the area, flexing their muscles. The Ukraine-Russia crisis is widely seen by experts as determining the fate of Joe Biden's US presidency and the Allies' confidence in the United States.
