18 Unexploded Ordnance Found in Svay Chek District, Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): 18 unexploded ordnance left over from the war era were found by villagers plowing in Ta Doul village, Phkam commune, Svay Chek district, Banteay Meanchey province on the morning of January 26, 2022 and reported to the authorities. To be destroyed to avoid danger to the people.
Colonel Chea Sloh, Svay Chek District Police Inspector, said that the owner of the rice field, who found 18 unexploded ordnance left over from the war, was 35-year-old Saing Chay, a resident of Ta Doul Village, Phkam Commune, Svay Chek District. Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Athikar continued that according to the explanation from the people who own the fields, he said that he plowed the fields every year, but this year, with the intention of expanding the fields, he also used a tractor to plow the land. In the field, there was a bigger plot of land, so they found the bullets and reported to the Phkam commune police station.
According to the Svay Chek district police inspector, upon receiving information from residents, the Phkam administrative police station also provided information to the CMAC group to dismantle these war remnants and destroy them in the future.
