Ministry of Commerce plans to open pottery and stone sculpture development centers in Pursat and Kampong Chhnang provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce plans to launch a pottery development center in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province and a stone carving development center in Pursat city in 2022 to promote pottery and stone carving in Cambodia. Attract national and international tourists. This was confirmed by a senior official of the Ministry of Commerce, who told Fresh News on January 26, 2022.
Mr. Reach Ra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that the establishment of this center to promote marketing and improve the livelihood of the people engaged in the field of pottery and marble sculpture to preserve the cultural heritage, talent and geographical identity of the province. Two and create a business environment in the field of pottery and stone carving.
On January 24-25, 2022, the working group of the Ministry of Commerce led by Mr. Reach Ra inspected the progress of the development process of the pottery sector and studied the status of the stone carving business in Kampong Chhnang and Pursat provinces to support and promote the process. Establish the Cambodian Pottery Development Center, a commercial location linked to traditional cultural tourism, and continue to promote the Ministry of Commerce's strategic planning initiatives.
In the field of stone carving, there are a total of 55 producers and sculptors, of which there are 18 suppliers and 36 family-owned enterprises. The sector was also affected but retained orders from domestic and foreign markets including India, Myanmar, Sri Lanka and Thailand.
