Neak Oknha Kith Meng Receives Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council from Brunei and holds the 91st Meeting of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on Wednesday morning, January 26, 2022, held a ceremony to transfer the position of Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council from Brunei to Cambodia and the 91st Meeting of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council under the chairmanship of Mr. Pich Rithy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, represented Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, took over the chairmanship of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council in 2022, succeeding Ms. Yan Ty, Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council 2021 in Brunei, who ended her term.
After the official handover ceremony, Duke Kith Meng chaired the 91st Meeting of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, which took place on the afternoon of January 26, 2022. This meeting is the first meeting for the year 2022.
The meeting discussed the adoption of the minutes of the 90th meeting, the remaining issues from the 90th meeting, the approval of the agenda of the 91st meeting, projects and programs to be implemented during the host Cambodia. , Updates from the ASEAN Secretariat, Updates on projects being implemented by member countries, Cooperation with the Joint Business Council and other issues.
Members of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council warmly welcomed and welcomed Duke Kith Meng, Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council. The meeting had a lively discussion and input on each of the above agendas.
The 91st Meeting of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council was held successfully and fruitfully in a friendly and fraternal atmosphere.
Please be informed that the ASEAN Business Advisory Council was established in 2001 by the ASEAN Heads of State / Government. The Council is tasked with providing input and reporting from the private sector to help drive ASEAN's efforts towards economic integration.
The invitation was made during a video conference between the two heads of state on January 25, 2022.
