Senior Minister Kun Kim proposes to speed up the construction of roads, digging wells and canals for veterans in Santuk district
(Kampong Thom): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, requested the Ministry of Rural Development and the Ministry of Water Resources to expedite the construction of roads, wells and canals for Cambodian veterans living on land concessions. Social work in Kraya commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province to facilitate their livelihood and cultivation.
On Wednesday, January 26, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chief of Staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, paid a visit to inspect the living conditions and cultivation of Cambodian veterans. Living in Kraya commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
Cambodian Veterans, who have been a great benefactor for the motherland during the social crisis of the war, about 150 families were organized by the Cambodian Veterans Association to live in the above location by the Royal Government granted a land concession of 1.5 hectares. Habitat and cultivation. In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen built houses for all 150 families.
"Our veterans came to live here happily with the light of a new life under the high care of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. "Our brothers are satisfied with this new life and have worked hard to build a better life." This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
However, the lives of Cambodian veterans in the area continue to suffer from a lack of infrastructure such as roads, wells and irrigation systems. In response to this, Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen had instructed the Ministry of Rural Development to help build a 12-kilometer road, to dig water wells, and also to the Ministry of Water Resources to prepare a canal system for water extraction. To irrigation as well.
Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed hope that the Minister of Rural Development and the Ministry of Water Resources will speed up these activities to facilitate the livelihood and productivity of veterans.
During the visit to inspect the lives and cultivation of veterans in Kraya commune, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and appreciated the honorary president of the Kampong Thom Veterans Association for caring for veterans by mobilizing departments and institutions in The province has formed an alliance with the Veterans Village and has formed a movement to support the lives of veterans.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always consider the lives and livelihoods of veterans in all circumstances.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that veterans from all over Cambodia remember in their hearts the merits and generous spirit of both Samdech.
