Ratanakkiri Governor Receives Swiss Agency for Skills Development and Cooperation
(Rattanakiri): On the morning of January 26, 2022, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province, received a delegation from the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) at the Provincial Hall.
She added that the Skills Development Program (SDP) aims to help disadvantaged youth and low-skilled workers in five provinces of Cambodia (Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kratie, Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri) so that they can get decent jobs. And revenue growth, and the program has two main objectives, including:
* First: Support the Cambodian Technical Vocational Education and Training System (TVET) to be more effective in the target provinces * Second: Improve the employment and income of disadvantaged youth and low-skilled workers through technical skills Soft skills and entrepreneurial skills.
In addition, she also thanked all stakeholders who worked well together to make this project work well, she observed that at the provincial vocational training center, many female students came to study. Both indigenous students and students from poor and disadvantaged backgrounds came to school equally and acquired the same skills.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun welcomed and expressed his deep gratitude to SDC for supporting the Ratanakkiri Vocational Training Center to train human resources, develop skills and generate income for the people.
The Governor also requested the Swiss Agency for Skills Development and Cooperation to continue to support the Provincial Vocational Training Center with technical materials for use in teaching and to train new skills in electrical and construction skills. Air conditioning and equipment repair skills and car repair skills.
Taking this opportunity, the provincial governor also highlighted the potential of Ratanakkiri province, which has three main areas, including ecotourism, agro-industry and mining, which are an important part of the development of Ratanakkiri.
