Duke Kith Meng has been appointed Chairman of the East Asia Business Council 2022 from South Korea and chaired the 53rd East Asia Business Council Meeting.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on Wednesday morning, January 26, 2022, held a ceremony to transfer the position of Chairman of the East Asia Business Council from Korea to Cambodia and open the 53rd meeting of the East Asia Business Council.
The event was attended online and in person by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, leaders, members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, members of the 13 East Asian Business Council members, representatives of the Asian Business Council partner organizations. East Many national and international guests.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, took over as Chairman of the East Asia Business Council in 2022, succeeding Haki Chou, President of the East Asia Business Council in 2021, who ended his term.
Speaking at the handover ceremony, Duke Kith Meng, President of the East Asia Business Council, thanked all the members of the East Asia Business Council for attending the official ceremony and supporting the Duke as Chairman. The duke stressed that taking over the chairmanship of the East Asia Business Council this year comes at a challenging time as the global economy is being hit hard by the Kovid-19 crisis.
In this regard, for the new term of 2022, the East Asia Business Council has set the theme "East Asia Connectivity for Renewable Energy, Environment and Sustainability" and has launched three major joint support programs. Contains:
1: Adjusting the scope of regional trade through trade facilitation and promoting the implementation of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which will serve as a mechanism for economic and business recovery in East Asia.
2: Responding to the Kovid 19 Crisis through the Benefits of the Efficiency and Productivity of Digital Innovation for the Regional Business Sector
3: Rebuilding the production chain of crisis-resistant areas and restoring cross-border travel for smooth and safe business at the same time also helps promote people-to-people connections. People and business activities.
After the official handover ceremony, the President continued to chair the 53rd Meeting of the East Asia Business Council, which discussed the following key points:
Members of the East Asia Business Council congratulated and warmly welcomed Duke Kith Meng, President of the East Asia Business Council. The meeting had a lively discussion and provided input on each of the above agendas. The 53rd meeting of the East Asia Business Council was held successfully and fruitfully in a friendly and fraternal atmosphere.
