(Phnom Penh) - Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, met with Mr. Nasser BOURITA, Minister of Foreign Affairs, African Cooperation and Immigration of Morocco on January 25, 2022.
The two foreign ministers agreed to expedite the negotiation of an agreement not yet signed, an agreement on aviation services between the two countries, and to consider the signing of a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation between the two countries. Both countries aim to boost tourism.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon thanked the Moroccan side for providing scholarships to Cambodian diplomats and Cambodian students to study in Morocco. For cooperation between the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations (NIDIR) Cambodia and the Moroccan Academy of Diplomacy (AMED). The Deputy Prime Minister requested the two institutes to find ways and means for the cooperation between the two institutes to emerge.
Regarding regional cooperation, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon briefed his counterpart on Cambodia's priorities as chair of ASEAN 2022 in response to emerging strategic challenges in the region, including effective management of the region. The Kovid-19 epidemic and the environmental recovery process, the management of existing and traditional issues, and the strengthening of ASEAN's cohesiveness, centrality and resilience.
Mr. Nasser BOURITA expressed his strong commitment to support Cambodia as ASEAN Chair this year and reaffirmed Morocco's commitment to serve as a bridge between Cambodia and Africa and the Middle East to promote cooperation. Bilateral with Cambodia as well as ASEAN countries.
