(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and chair of ASEAN in 2022, said that the current Myanmar leader, Senior General Min Ong Lang, will be invited to attend the 2022 ASEAN Summit if the ASEAN member states make progress. In implementing the five points of consensus reached by ASEAN leaders in April last year.
ASEAN has set out five principles, three of which were initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen in response to the political crisis in Myanmar, and include:
In a meeting with the Prime Minister of Malaysia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also spoke about ASEAN affairs and affairs, as well as the crisis in Myanmar. Samdech Techo spoke about the purpose as well as the results of a recent working visit to Myanmar and outlined the measures to be taken next.
The prince stated that the visit to Myanmar is to find out about the actual situation and want to know what are the main issues, what can Myanmar do? To implement the five points that have been agreed so far. In addition, the visit also brought humanitarian donations to the people of Myanmar. Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to work with the Myanmar government to resolve the issue in Myanmar.
Another result is a dialogue that is based on the five points that were unanimously agreed upon. "The situation in Myanmar is very complicated and difficult, so it cannot be resolved in the short term, but the important thing is that we do our best to negotiate a solution and send humanitarian aid," he said. Reach out to the people of Myanmar in need.
Samdech Techo also informed the Malaysian Prime Minister that after his visit to Miami, Aung San Suu Kyi was sentenced to four years in prison and the use of aircraft in military operations. Samdech Techo said that he will meet with Mr. Min Ong Lang in a video discussion tomorrow to find out more about all this work.
Samdech Techo also informed the Prime Minister of Malaysia about his request to establish two mechanisms to find a way out of this work, including:
* Mechanism 1: ASEAN mechanism - to facilitate and monitor the progress of the implementation of the five points of unanimous agreement, with Cambodia, the current ASEAN chair, Brunei as the former chair of ASEAN and Indonesia as the chair of ASEAN after Cambodia, plus the Secretary-General. ASEAN as well.
In response, the Malaysian Prime Minister stressed the importance of resolving the issue in Myanmar, which requires inclusiveness, especially within the framework of the ASEAN Charter. He also called for the release of all political prisoners in Myanmar, including Aung San Suu Kyi. The Malaysian Prime Minister also spoke about humanitarian aid through food centers to make sure that it reaches the people of Myanmar.
In this meeting, the Prime Minister of Malaysia said that he accepted all the remarks made by Samdech Techo as well as the request made by Samdech Techo, especially the request for ASEAN Foreign Ministers and ASEAN Senior Officials to meet. Discuss. As for the ASEAN Special Envoy, he supported to make sure that the Special Envoy implement the five points that have been unanimously agreed upon in the past.
"Our efforts to build the ASEAN Community are constantly moving forward, what we have achieved and what we must implement," said the Malaysian Prime Minister. He will continue to work to build the ASEAN Community under the leadership of Cambodia, which holds the ASEAN chairmanship in 2022, and if the situation improves, he will be invited to attend the ASEAN and related meetings directly in Cambodia.
