(Phnom Penh): Speaking at a press conference on the Clean Air Plan of Cambodia on the morning of January 25, 2022, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment stated that air pollution is becoming an environmental challenge in the region and the world. Its impact is indefinable, and it is not a national issue, but it is a common problem for the region and the world that requires the participation of all parties.
The press conference was held at the Ministry of Environment with the participation of Chea Sina, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Pak Sokharavuth, Acting Director General of the General Department of Environmental Information, Mr. Thiv Sophearith, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Environmental Information, Mr. Chea Nara Head of Air Quality, Sound and Vibration Management Department, as well as many other journalists.
"Air pollution is becoming an environmental challenge in the region and the world, the impact of which is indefinable," said Pheaktra. The scope of the effects of air pollution is large because air pollutants can spread far and wide and cause cross-border pollution. "Air pollution can not be considered a national problem, but it is a common problem for the region and the world that requires the participation of all parties."
He added that the implementation of measures to reduce pollution due to Circular No. 1 on measures to prevent and reduce public air pollution has contributed to significantly reduce emissions, especially PM2.5 PM10 and CO have been reduced by half. By 2030, compared to the basic scenario.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that the Ministry of Environment has initiated the Cambodia Clean Air Plan as a strategic plan aimed at reducing emissions in Cambodia and providing benefits to Cambodia, including:
* First: Provide data on the current air quality situation and trends for the coming year.
* Second, develop a joint analysis of pollutants, greenhouse gases and short-term pollutants to identify areas that are the main sources of air pollution now and in the future.
* Third: Identify and introduce measures to reduce greenhouse gas emissions in line with reducing greenhouse gas emissions, which will promote public health, the environment and sustainable economic development and are an important part of Reduce climate change
* Fourth: Demonstrate Cambodia's position on international cooperation for regional air pollution control and the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.
