Two Ministries Collaborate with the World Bank to Organize Protected Products and Services in Protected Areas in Kampong Speu and Koh Kong Provinces
(Kampong Speu-Koh Kong): The Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Rural Development, in collaboration with the World Bank and NGOs, organized a four-day study tour on protected products and services in protected areas in Kampong Speu and Koh Kong provinces from May 25. Until January 28, 2022.
The purpose of the project development is to improve the management of protected areas, promote ecotourism opportunities and non-timber forest product value chains in the Cardamom and Tonle Sap landscape. This project is managed by the Ministry of Environment and co-implemented by the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Rural Development with incentives to help the Royal Government of Cambodia achieve its sustainable development goals.
