Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, told the media after the meeting that during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed the Prime Minister of Malaysia about his intention to visit Myanmar and the work to be done on the issue. Of Miyama.
In that, Samdech Techo emphasized that Samdech's visit to the Union of Myanmar to find out the real situation and also want to know what are the important issues and what Myanmar can do to implement the 5 principles of ASEAN unanimity. During his visit, he discussed two key principles: compliance with the ASEAN Charter and the five-point principle of ASEAN's unanimity, which was reached at a special meeting in April 2021 in Indonesia.
Samdech Techo told the Malaysian Prime Minister that the key solution in Myanmar was to stop the violence that was happening in and out of Myanmar, and he tried to work with the Myanmar military regime to stop the fighting. Not only that, there are opportunities to provide humanitarian assistance to Myanmar that the people need.
In addition, dialogue between the ASEAN Heads of Government must be promoted, which is part of the decision. Although nothing has progressed yet, Samdech wants to break through this gap by telling Myanmar to implement the five principles.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized, "Samdech Techo frankly said that the situation in Myanmar is very complicated and difficult, so it can not be resolved in a few days, it takes more time to move forward. Can count the years. "Can move from one ASEAN chair to another ASEAN chair."
"Samdech Techo reiterated that the ceasefire, cessation of violence and the avoidance of the humanitarian crisis in Myanmar are important issues that we need to address in order to deliver this humanitarian aid to the people," he said. "Myanmar without discrimination."
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also highlighted that Samdech tried his best to make humanitarian aid reach the hands of the people.
In this meeting with the Prime Minister of Malaysia, Samdech Techo also stressed that to solve the problem of Myanmar, if not work with the military regime, which is in power in Myanmar to find a solution, who to work with?
In response, Malaysian Prime Minister Ishmael Sabribin Jacob said he understood the recent visit of Samdech Techo to Myanmar and that it was important for Myanmar as well as for ASEAN and the international community. .
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized that "His Excellency stressed that the situation in Myanmar requires an urgent joint solution. And especially under the framework of the ASEAN Constitution, which is an urgent need to address how to return the situation to normal. "In particular, do not continue the violence and encourage dialogue with all parties involved."
According to Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, the Malaysian Prime Minister called for the release of all political prisoners in Myanmar, including Aung San Suu Kyi.
In addition, the Prime Minister of Malaysia supported the appointment of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as the new Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair, and requested that the Special Envoy be able to meet with all parties in Myanmar.
The Malaysian Prime Minister also reiterated his position on inviting the Myanmar side to attend the ASEAN Summit. The Prime Minister stressed that as long as there is no progress in the implementation of the five-point principle of unanimity as decided by the ASEAN Heads of Government, the Myanmar side attending the ASEAN Summit must be a non-partisan party of Myanmar.
The Malaysian Prime Minister reiterated that Myanmar is still a member of the ASEAN family, but a peaceful solution for the people of Myanmar is necessary to implement these five unanimous principles. General Vong Pisen Leads a Delegation to Congratulate Vietnamese Ambassador and Military Attaché to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the Vietnamese New Year celebrations, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, led a delegation to congratulate HE Nguyen Huy Taing, Ambassador of Vietnam and Special Colonel Nguyen Thanh Chinh. Vietnam Military Attaché to Cambodia on January 25, 2022.
