Phnom Penh Military sends a suspect to court in connection with an attempted rape of a minor girl
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 25, 2022, the competent authorities of the Anti-Human Trafficking Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie sent a suspect to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for sentencing in accordance with legal procedures related to attempted rape. The girl is a minor.
The suspect, 34-year-old Khun Khong alias Loy, was born in Tbong village, Khchas commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province, and currently resides in a pure water production house in Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey.
The military police of Po Sen Chey district said that after receiving information through the telephone number 1291 of the Phnom Penh Military Police Operations Command, there was a case of attempted rape of a minor girl.
Under the coordination of Mr. Kim Hong San, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the Armed Forces intervened at the scene and arrested one suspect, Khun Khong alias Aloi, 34 years old, in front of the warehouse. Selling unbranded pure water on concrete road, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, sent to the Anti-Human Trafficking Office for further questioning.
After hearing the answers of the suspect and the victim girl, it was found that they were in line with the real accusation. About 150 million cubic meters of dams could be built in Kampong Speu province, with coverage in Phnom Penh and three other provinces
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Chan Yutha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, this morning, January 25, 2022, led a working group of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and related partners to study a new dam. Located in Ta Sal Samaki Commune, Oral District.
According to the provincial governor, the construction of the Stung Khleach dam, if not changed, could start in 2024 at a time, with a storage capacity of 150 million cubic meters.
According to the experts, if the dam is completed, the beneficiaries will include Kampong Speu, Kandal, Takeo and Phnom Penh, but the project will require a study by experts on the impact and environment of the dam. Dam first.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, explained in detail about the commercial transactions that are obliged to pay value added tax.
Mr. Ken Sambath stated that the taxpayer refers to: 1. Non-resident taxpayers (taxpayers who do not have a head office in the country) who supply digital goods or digital services or any e-commerce activities into Cambodia. Which is required to register the VAT.
2. A self-declared taxpayer who receives a supply of digital goods or digital services or any e-commerce activity from a non-resident taxpayer.
Value-added tax applies to the supply of digital goods or digital services electronically or to any e-commerce activity carried out by a resident expatriate supplier to Cambodia and to a resident resident taxpayer. Obtaining the supply of digital goods or digital services or any electronic commercial activity from a non-resident taxpayer.
For non-resident taxpayers also includes e-nursery operations. An e-Nursery transaction refers to a non-resident taxpayer who provides digital payment services and digital services to electronic buyers. As a non-resident taxpayer, you must also be obliged to register and become a taxpayer.
Mr. Ken Sambath said that online business operators in Cambodia are not subject to VAT because they are taxpayers who can register in Cambodia at any time of business. Goods from other countries are also not obliged to pay value added tax as this is an individual item that is shipped via ship or post and paid through the General Department of Customs.
For digital goods, the emphasis is on intangible goods, such as downloading other programs for watching TV, etc. These are obliged to pay value added tax.
