The following is the statement of the National Assembly of Cambodia:
General knowledge: Malacca, a colonial heritage city
(Malaysia): Malacca, the center of the Malay Peninsula, was once a major port area and was formerly occupied by Portuguese, Dutch, British and Japanese colonies, leaving behind a diverse culture between the colonists and the Western colonies.
* A Brief History of Malacca
* Malacca in European colonial times
The world also reached colonial times and spread to India and Southeast Asia. After conquering the Indian kingdom of Goa, the Portuguese army continued to reach Southeast Asia and launched the first invasion of Malacca until its victory in 1511. From then on, the kingdom of Malacca fell under Portuguese colonization.
Malacca was ceded to Britain under the 1824 Anglo-Dutch Treaty in exchange for Bencoolen on Sumatra. From 1824 to 1942, Malacca fell under British rule, first under British East India Company and then under British colonial rule.
During World War II, Malacca was briefly under Japanese rule from 1942-1945. After 1945, Britain also came to rule Malacca and other states of Malaysia as well as present-day Singapore. Senior Minister Osman Hassan Donates More Than $ 10,000 to 104 Orphans
