The President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Prosecutor request all subordinates to make efforts to provide justice services to the people based on the principles of the law in force
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court and representatives of the Prosecutor's Office accompanied the court on the morning of January 24, 2022, to hold a meeting to review the work results in 2021 and raise work targets in 2022.
Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, opened the meeting by saying that the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and the direction of administrative work in 2022, the eighth meeting was organized in accordance with the spirit of Article 34 of the law. On the organization of the judiciary for the following purposes:
* First: Demonstrate the achievements of hard work and achievement * Second: Identify the challenges that arise and find the right solution for those problems through exchange of experiences * Third: Set the direction of the action plan. It is clear in the future that the activities that contribute to the political program, legal reform and justice system of the Royal Government to achieve a glorious fruit.
Mr. I Rin, Director of the Administrative Secretariat of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, read out the draft report on the results of work activities in 2021 and proposed the work direction for 2022 to the meeting, and the meeting agreed on the draft report in full.
"I urge all judges, deputy prosecutors, clerks, clerks, bailiffs and all officials of the Secretariat of Administration to work hard to fulfill their duties in accordance with the law, professional procedures, conscience and solidarity to achieve their goals," he said. "Administrative work set out for 2022 and to gain the trust of the people in providing justice to them."
Before concluding the meeting, the President of the Court of First Instance requested all officials to continue to support and implement the strategic plan of the Royal Government, including:
* First: Strengthening the proper implementation of the law * Second: Strengthening the cleanliness and professional ethics of law enforcement officials * Third: Strengthening the mechanism of labor discipline and modernization of the administration of justice * Fourth: Improving the provision of legal services / Strategies to improve the provision of legal services * Fifth: Strengthening and improving dispute resolution mechanisms that can respond effectively to the realities of society.
