(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of receiving a courtesy call and discussing with the delegation of the Cambodian Automobile Industry Federation (CAIF) to discuss support policies for electric vehicles (EV) in Cambodia, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport Transport is committed to promoting the widespread use of electric vehicles in Cambodia to help reduce carbon emissions into the Earth's atmosphere.
The meeting was held on January 24, 2022 at the Ministry's office by a delegation of the Federation of Automobile Industries of Cambodia, led by Mr. Tan Monivann, President of the Federation and Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and accompanied by the General Director of Automobile Companies. Another number as well.
In addition, the Senior Minister also highlighted the leading role and the high responsibility of the Ministry in promoting the widespread use of electric vehicles and added that the Royal Government is open to Both local and foreign investors are investing in the development of infrastructure for electric vehicles.
On that occasion, the delegation of the Federation of Automobile Industries of Cambodia requested the Ministry to help review and coordinate the technical work related to the installation of common standard equipment (that is, the same type) that allows all types of electric vehicles to charge EVs. At any charging station, a policy for electric vehicles has also been proposed.
In response, the Senior Minister also instructed the Federation to work closely with relevant officials under the Ministry to address the issues raised by the Federation to encourage the widespread use of electric vehicles and attract attention. High sentiment from the private sector as well as the general public.
