Cambodia Credit Guarantee Corporation and two other institutions jointly promote investment in large-scale biogas technology in Cambodia
Under the framework of the Memorandum of Understanding, the two sides agreed on joint objectives to identify opportunities for collaborative activities and programs to help promote biogas technology and promote investment through appropriate risk-sharing mechanisms and to benefit from This defined collaboration to bridge the knowledge gap of the biogas value chain among partners and stakeholders.
Such cooperation will enable farmers, rural communities and agribusinesses to improve their livelihoods and increase the profitability of their businesses effectively and sustainably.
"As agriculture is the second largest source of greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions, it will lead to climate change such as subsequent monsoon rains and higher temperatures, which will have a negative impact on the sector," he said. "This is why climate change mitigation is critical to the sustainability of the agro-processing industry and the livestock sector."
"In addition to our strategic partnership with commercial banks, we are honored to have the opportunity to work closely with the CGCC, a government-run credit guarantee institution, to provide innovative financial solutions to support Development and use of biogas technology for agribusiness. This is according to Mr. Lolly, the director of BTIC.
"This MOU will allow all key players, including BTIC, CGCC and its banking partners, as well as other stakeholders, to work more closely and effectively on a number of key priorities to respond," he explained. To the needs of Cambodian businesses to adopt this biogas technology to solve the problem of effective waste management.
"We believe that this partnership will drive long-term growth in animal production and agro-processing by promoting renewable energy and proper waste management, as well as contributing to the commitment of "The government in the fight against climate change."
Mr. Sok Narin, UNIDO Country Representative in Cambodia, emphasized the importance of cooperation in contributing to past efforts to develop a favorable investment environment to address the financial challenges that investors face in Invest in large-scale biogas projects.
"I am pleased that the CGCC is showing that our financial sector is willing to learn, adapt and be more flexible," he said. Innovation in setting up financing mechanisms is very important in supporting many development projects.
The innovation of this financing mechanism will encourage more investment in large-scale biogas technology in agribusiness, which is an important breakthrough for investors in embracing and applying renewable energy technologies to their business practices. This type of clean energy investment will bring many economic, environmental and social benefits to consumers, farm owners, investors and society.
This Memorandum of Understanding is in line with the efforts of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to update the Biogas Policy for 2021-2030, as well as many other objectives set by the Royal Government in the Partnership Program. UNIDO Country (PCP) to promote sustainable energy and a revolving economy.
