General knowledge: History of international trade
(Phnom Penh): The history of international trade has a long history, as historians show that it dates back to the time when people lived as tribes. What is the history of this business?
Archaeologists have found that the world's first international trade network dates back to about 3,500 BC, appearing in Mesopotamia in present-day Iraq and Iran. In ancient China, the emergence of the Silk Road network during the years 2000-1000 BC is also considered an international trade network.
At the beginning of the Christian era, as the influence of the ancient Greeks waned, the Romans also built their own empire with the expansion of trade to present-day Britain and other parts of northern Europe. The collapse of international trade in the region has also slowed.
From the 5th to the 15th century, Arab merchants continued the tradition of international trade from Europe, establishing large trade networks around the Persian Gulf, Africa, India, and Southeast Asia, thus boosting trade. Karma between China, India, Java, Malay, Khmer, Burmese, Jama, later also Siamese and Vietnamese.
After this colonial period, the world also reached the era of World War II, 1939-1945. Since then, the world has formed a series of trade organizations to reorganize international trade.
