Sok Raden, chairman of the board of directors of the Cambodian Fishermen Association, expressed such optimism that the large number of trout raised in Cambodia could meet the demand of the Chinese side. The rearing is all raised with high quality and standard.
Mr. Sok Raden urged farmers to pay more attention to fish farming techniques, phytosanitary hygiene and quality standards so that their fish can be exported to China.
He also said that due to the fall in the price of trout this year, farmers have reduced their production, but the farmers will increase their production to produce for export to China.
Please be informed that on January 20, 2022, the Technical Working Group of the Cambodian Fisheries Administration and the General Department of Customs of the People's Republic of China started the first online discussion to evaluate the phytosanitary, fish, aquaculture, aquaculture and fish processing enterprises. Before the Chinese side decided to allow Cambodian trout to be imported to China. The meeting will last for 9 days and will end on January 28, 2022.
On December 6, 2021, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vintian announced that the Chinese side had decided to study and assess the phytosanitary risks of Cambodian longan and trout through a remote video system. As an important measure, so the export of trout will be able to export in the near future.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also said that the acceleration of the export of lentils and trout is a major achievement from the meeting between Samdech and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes to see the presence of Khmer trout food on the Chinese table, and Samdech Techo considers that the import of trout from China will provide more opportunities for trout farmers.
