(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce and PTT (Cambodia) have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to pave the way for the sale of Cambodian products at PTT gas stations. This is another effort of the Ministry of Commerce to find markets and promote the sale of Cambodian products.
The Ministry of Commerce emphasized that the MoU is to promote Cambodian products in the domestic market, develop the Cambodian business sector on the basis of transparency and community interests, promote the use of local products, increase and build entrepreneurial capacity, as well as create business opportunities for Participate in the development of the trade sector and promote the Cambodian socio-economic environment.
The Ministry also stated that this cooperation will contribute to the development of trade and economic development, especially to promote the use of domestic products more widely in the masses, as well as promote a rich market for domestic products. .
In addition to the completion of the seven-day pilot project, PTT (Cambodia) will implement three other sub-projects, which will be held in May, August and November 2022, with a total of 63 vendors participating in the sale of Cambodian products.
This project will be sold on Friday, Saturday and Sunday at some PTT gas stations, such as: in the second quarter of 2022 at 16 stations along National Roads 2, 3 and 4, in the third quarter at 10 stations along National Road 6 and in the fourth quarter at 5 stations along National Road 5.
