Questions and answers related to the study at "Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport"
(Phnom Penh): "Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport" is the first training center in Cambodia that trains in public works and transportation skills. The institute is under the control of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, with Senior Minister Sun Chanthol as its Minister.
With the opening of the new school year, Mr. Hoeun Samneang, Director of "Techo Sen Public Works and Transport" Institute of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on Friday morning, January 21, 2022, came out to explain and answer. Questions related to studying in this institute through live broadcast on the Ministry's Facebook page.
The following are some of the questions and answers that were asked and interpreted in relation to the study at the Institute:
Q: Does the institute have a 100% scholarship? Answer: 100% scholarship is given to 50 outstanding students with high scores (regardless of male or female students). 50% scholarship is given only to female students who will automatically receive 50% scholarship. Tuition $ 600 per year.
Scholarships are offered for one academic year only, meaning that scholarship winners must work hard to maintain and maintain a good academic record (at least 85% of their total annual results) in order to continue receiving scholarships. Next year. This assessment is made by the Institute management.
In addition to studying well, students must come to school regularly, set a good example for other students, have good attitudes and morals, and participate in volunteer activities that benefit the same students. In doing so, the institute aims to cultivate the seeds of human resources with capacity, knowledge and good attitude.
Q: Do all the skills have to be taken in the exam or just buy the words to be able to study? Answer: All majors are required to take the entrance exam. Not all students with A, B or C scores can take the exam. Pass the exam, need to choose good seeds to enter the school. Want to see Cambodian children become experts in the field of infrastructure in Cambodia, believe that Cambodian children can do it.
Q: When does the institute open for the first generation of students? Answer: Held on January 31, 2022 for the first generation. The second generation will open on March 9, 2022, and will start accepting applications for the second generation from January 17 to February 11. The second generation exam on February 14 and the results will be released on February 15. Register for the second generation from February 15 to March 9.
Q: Can the 2019 and 2020 bankruptcies apply for admission to the institute? Answer: You can apply and take the same entrance exam.
Q: The development of public infrastructure is to boost the national economy. Does the institute have the skills of road analysis to determine the appropriate speed, safety and development? A: There are Transportation Surveillance Techniques and Transportation Surveying and Forecasting subjects, majoring in Economics and Transportation Management.
Q: Does the institute have any training other than undergraduate training? Answer: Intermediate training for senior technical skills such as: skilled workers, senior skilled workers, vehicle technicians, heavy machinery drivers, garage management skills, etc. Soft skills such as: leadership and communication skills.
