(Sihanoukville): The 40th ASEAN Tourism Forum held in Sihanoukville has organized a tourism product exhibition to give tourism operators and entrepreneurs the opportunity to showcase and sell their tourism products.
Hoteliers, hoteliers, tour operators and tour operators are showcasing their services at a major event in Sihanoukville this week.
The tourism industry that participated in the ASEAN Expo welcomed the organization of the expo and hoped that through this expo it would contribute to the tourism sector in Cambodia, which has suffered from cholera for two years. And that's improved.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association of Travel Agents of Cambodia, brought about 30 members of its association to participate in the ASEAN Tourism Fair. Participating companies include caterers, tour operators, tour guides, travel agencies and package designers.
She said that in this exhibition, the participants had a conversation to find partners with tour operators from different countries and met to cooperate in doing business in the tourism sector.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin emphasized, "This forum has given Cambodia, we have shown the potential of tourism in Cambodia, show the culture, show the customs, show the traditions, show the Cambodian character, the smile of Cambodia to the world." See. We have the opportunity to promote what Cambodia has. ”
The Empress Angkor Hotel, a five-star hotel in the heart of Siem Reap, has been struggling to cope with the difficult Kovid 19 crisis for the past two years, also seeking opportunities to gather guests from the ASEAN Expo in Sihanoukville.
Mr. Sou Say, General Manager of Empress Angkor Hotel, said that Empress Angkor Hotel has up to 391 rooms and provides accommodation, food and shakes. He said the two years of the 19-epidemic of Kovid had put the hotel in crisis, but the hotel had put in place strategies to find guests and cope with the crisis.
Mr. Sou Say welcomed the organization of the ASEAN Expo in Sihanoukville. The general manager of the five-star hotel in the center of Siem Reap hopes that the ASEAN Expo will be an event that contributes to the revitalization of the hotel sector.
"Of course, this ASEAN tourism event provides a lot of opportunities to meet with buying agents from all countries, especially in ASEAN, as we have scheduled him to discuss tourism exchanges," he said. "Especially the tour packages of the companies he joined."
Another hotel in Siem Reap, a hotel that has struggled to cope with the crisis of the Kovid 19 crisis, the Star Angkor Hotel also participated in the ASEAN Expo.
Ms. Seng Srey Rith, Head of Sales and Marketing for Starry Angkor Hotel, said that Starry Angkor Hotel has started to receive guests gradually since the Royal Government opened to travel widely in November 2021. Ms. Seng Srey Rith considers the ASEAN Expo as another opportunity for Star Angkor Hotel to seek out guests as well as partners.
Thorn Sinan, president of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association, also led about 20 members of the association to attend the fair. He also expressed his pleasure at the organization of the ASEAN Expo.
"This is a great opportunity because at this ASEAN Tourism Forum, Cambodia has broken a world record," said Thorn Sina. So for me, it is very valuable that in the 10 ASEAN blocks, no country has the courage to organize this international exhibition, only Cambodia has the courage to organize the exhibition. Thus, this is a platform for providing knowledge exchange, communication and business exchange platform.
Both the association and the tourism industry participants who participated in this exhibition expressed their hope that this event will bring about an improvement in tourism in Cambodia from the Kovid 19 crisis.
Ms. Seng Srey Rith said, "What we expect from this event is to redesign our hotel and we hope to have a return flight."
"We have high expectations that tourism will be transformed from now on, and I believe that tourism will more or less resume," said Thorn Sina.
Spokesman: EU to return to Afghanistan for humanitarian purposes
The European Union (EU) said on Friday that it would return to Afghanistan for humanitarian purposes, but stressed that the EU had not officially recognized the Taliban-led administration. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, January 21, 2022.
It is the first proclamation by a Western power since Kabul fell to the Taliban in August 2021, as the 27-nation European Union and other governments have withdrawn staff and diplomats. Its out of Afghanistan.
"The European Union (EU) has begun to re-establish a small EU delegation in Afghanistan to facilitate humanitarian assistance and monitor the humanitarian situation," said Foreign Ministry spokesman Peter Stano.
A Taliban foreign ministry spokesman confirmed in an earlier Twitter message that his officials had reached an agreement with the European Union for the official reopening of the embassy in Kabul and that operations had indeed begun.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday night, January 21, 2022, issued a special message to change the treatment conditions of 19 Kovid patients with omega virus infection after seeing the infected patients. Not serious.
Earlier, during the surveillance phase of the Kovid 19 attack, Samdech Techo ordered that all Omikrong patients be treated in hospitals.
But in a special audio message tonight, Samdech Techo noted that Omi Krong, despite the rapid transmission, is not a dangerous disease compared to that with Alpha, which we allow for home treatment in By hotel and by location.
For this reason, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also issued a new regulation allowing Omi Krong patients to receive home treatment for Cambodians. Foreigners can be treated at hotels or embassies.
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued the following order:
1: For all foreigners who come to the Kingdom of Cambodia to find a positive Kovid 19, whether or not Omi Krong, ask for permission to go to the hotel for treatment at the embassy, stay at the place of their choice. . So there is no need to take foreigners into the hospital anymore.
3: Omikrong patients who are currently in the hospital, foreigners or Cambodians, if you want to leave the hospital to be treated at home or at the hotel, please leave from tonight onwards. .
Samdech Techo confirmed that this regulation will be implemented from tonight onwards. Samdech Techo requested the relevant authorities, especially in the field of health, hospitals, families, as well as those who want to leave the hospital can also leave.
The Prime Minister instructed Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, to issue additional instructions on measures to prevent transmission.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen finally emphasized that the permission to receive treatment at home is not allowed to go out at will, but just transfer from the hospital to the hotel or treatment at home or treatment in a place other than the hospital. Only.
Samdech Techo hopes that foreign guests who come to Cambodia will not worry about being hospitalized in the event of a new mutation in Omikrong.
