The following is a statement from the Ministry of Labor: Senior Minister Ieng Moly closed the 5th workshop on the implementation of the 5th National Comprehensive and Multilateral Strategic Plan on HIV / AIDS.
The consultation workshop was organized to review the progress of the implementation of the 5th National Comprehensive and Multilateral Strategic Plan on HIV / AIDS and to identify shortcomings to provide recommendations for action planning. Implemented in 2022 and 2023.
The 5th Comprehensive National Strategic Plan for HIV and AIDS Response (2019-2023) was officially launched on September 29, 2019 with the participation of representatives from ministries, institutions, capitals and provinces. Members of the National AIDS Authority, as well as representatives of civil society organizations, people living with HIV and key groups.
During the three years of implementing the Fifth National and Comprehensive Strategic Plan for HIV / AIDS, we have overcome obstacles and difficulties, especially in the phase of the global epidemic of Kovid-19 in During the last two years.
The day-long workshop heard a presentation by the Technical Advisor and discussed the findings of the review of the implementation of the National Strategic Plan, focusing on the four strategies and monitoring and evaluation. Action plan for the extension period for 2022 and 2023 to achieve the commitment of the Royal Government to achieve the goal of 95-95-95 and the end of AIDS by 2025.
He added that as we enter the final stages of the long fight against HIV and AIDS, we need to recall the need to follow the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Calling on all compatriots to join a national movement with the Royal Government of Cambodia to end AIDS by 2025.
Finally, the Senior Minister emphasized that in looking forward to future cellular and synergistic collaboration, we need to consider the different contexts of HIV / AIDS response in Cambodia.
