"First of all, Myanmar is a member of ASEAN, so ASEAN needs unity and solidarity to work together," said Kao Kim Hourn. The situation in Myanmar requires us to maintain an open dialogue. "The prime minister's visit focused on the ceasefire and asked the military leaders to maintain the ceasefire, and they also agreed to maintain it (ceasefire) until the end of the year."
Minister Kao Kim Hourn continued, "Secondly, the visit of the Prime Minister was aimed at opening the door for the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair. "Third, the Prime Minister's visit is to provide humanitarian assistance to the people of Myanmar in need."
"Of the five agreements reached by ASEAN leaders in April last year, one of them was to make sure we stop the violence as soon as possible," Kao Kim Hourn said. Start a conversation. "In particular, there needs to be an ASEAN special envoy to meet all stakeholders in a united manner and to ensure that the people of Burma receive humanitarian assistance."
"My Prime Minister has already proposed the ASEAN Troika, which includes Cambodia as the current chair of ASEAN, Brunei as the former chair and Indonesia as the next chair, and the ASEAN Secretariat to monitor it," he said. "Progress in implementing the five-point agreement." Foreign Ministry Releases Official Results of Vietnamese Foreign Minister's Visit to Cambodia
