Ministry of Social Affairs Holds Sub-National Consultation Workshop to Gather input on the First Draft Law on the Protection of Children of the Kingdom of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Khieu Borey, Secretary of State and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group for the Preparation of the Law on the Protection of Children of Cambodia and Representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, held a sub-national consultation meeting to collect items. Enter the first draft law on the protection of children of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The meeting will last for two days from January 19 to 20, 2022, with the support of USAID through UNICEF and Plan International, and with stakeholders from eight provinces, including Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh, Kandal, Pelin, Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri and Tbong Khmum and many other partner organizations.
In accordance with this international law, the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken care of and effectively addressed the field of child welfare through the implementation of laws, policies and national action plans, such as the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025. National policy on child protection system 2019-2029, Law on Juvenile Justice, Law on International Adoption and other relevant legal documents.
Ms. Khieu Borey added that due to the status of Kovid-19 disease, the drafting of this law has been slower than expected. However, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will work with inter-ministerial technical working groups and stakeholders at both the national and sub-national levels to build the draft law to meet expectations.
