International Analysis: The Hypocritical Mask of American Democracy Revealed
BEIJING, Jan. 20 (Xinhua) - On January 20 last year, in his inaugural address, US leaders vowed to overcome 19 Kovid and unite the divided United States. At the time, the pledge brought hope to the American people who had just been affected by the unrest in the US House of Representatives and the spread of Kovid 19.
But after a year now in the United States, 19 cases of Kovid have spread again, inflation has risen, politics have become more divisive, and so on. The latest Gallup poll shows that support for US leaders has fallen from 57 percent a year earlier to 40 percent.
Overall, this is an inevitable result of the American democratic system running out of power. From a political point of view, the system of separation of powers between the three parties and the balance between the two parties has already become "veto politics", causing the United States to become more confrontational and divisive. At the same time, monetary policy has disrupted the entire process of the US general election, legislation and governance.
In fact, Americans are already interested in this issue. A referendum released by the Siena Institute on Jan. 18 found that 57 percent of New York City voters said the United States was going the wrong way. But America has fallen into a strange trap: everyone knows the wrong direction, but there is no way.
