Taiwan: A woman faces the death penalty in a fire that killed 46 people
(Taipei): A Taiwanese woman is facing the death penalty on suspicion of causing one of the worst fires to try to take revenge on her boyfriend who is suspected of having another secret love affair. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, January 21, 2022.
On Friday, Taiwanese prosecutors formally charged the 51-year-old Hang woman with murder and arson, and even said she should be put to death for causing a blaze. Deliberately bad just to get revenge on her boyfriend.
Kaohsiung City Prosecutor's Office said, "The woman intended to set fire to her boyfriend, who was suspected of having an affair, but it turned out to be a catastrophe and a loss. The lives of many innocent people. "The woman did not show any remorse, so the prosecutor asked the court to use the death penalty as a warning to others."
Since Taiwan resumed the death penalty in 2010 after a four-year suspension, about 35 prisoners have been executed. At present, 38 prisoners are on death row, including a woman. Representative Chay Borin and Dr. Prof. Diep Sophal lead youth and students on a study tour of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction
(Phnom Penh): In response to the request of the youth and students of the University of Cambodia, on January 21, 2022, Mr. Chay Borin, Member of Parliament for Tbong Khmum and Dr. Prof. Diep Sophal led the youth and students on a study tour to understand the construction of the Ministry of Organization. Land, Urban Planning and Construction, one of the many achievements built during the peaceful nation era under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The study tour was warmly welcomed by Mr. Ly Raksmey, Undersecretary of State, and Mr. Seng Lot, Director General of Administration of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, on behalf of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
On that occasion, Mr. Ly Raksmey gave a presentation on the construction process of the building and explained the meaning of the construction style that combines ancient and modern architecture to the youth and students in detail.
Mr. Chay Borin and Dr. Prof. Diep Sophal said that the construction of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction will now be an important legacy for the younger generation to learn more.
He said that under the shadow of peace and under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has been developing in all areas, including urban and rural areas, infrastructure such as roads, schools, hospitals, buildings, ministries, state institutions have been rebuilt. And repair and expand to be bigger, modern, rich, easy for people to live and receive services from the state with ease and high efficiency.
