Ministry of Commerce Reduces Trademark Registration Time, Makes Cambodia the Second Fastest Trademark Registration Provider in ASEAN (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce's Intellectual Property Department has expedited registration. Trademarks By reducing the trademark registration period from five to seven months, Cambodia has become the second fastest country in ASEAN after Singapore.
In addition, by 2021, the department has completed the registration of all 4,465 congested trademarks in 2020 and before 2020 so that business owners can officially use their brand to meet their needs.
In addition, the Department of Intellectual Property is preparing and studying three other brands, such as Kampot-Kep Salt and Flower, Kep Fish Sauce, Kampot-Kep and Takeo Lobster, along with three other collective brands, such as Siem Reap Noodles, Pursat Orange and Coconut. Battambang.
He stated that the law does not force or require business owners to register trademarks with the Department of Intellectual Property of the Ministry of Commerce. However, he encourages business owners to register trademarks at the Ministry of Commerce so as not to affect business owners, because if any person uses the same trademark and registers the trademark, it will lead to disputes. Happens to the detriment of individuals who have used the brand before.
