Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration Launches 4th Vaccination Campaign for Government Officials and Frontline Members
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration on the morning of January 21, 2022, launched the fourth Kovid vaccination campaign for the fourth dose to government officials and frontline people. The ceremony was attended by Mr. Kheng Su, Chairman of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Council, Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey, as well as many relevant officials.
Mr. Oum Rath said that the Pfizer vaccine is a vaccine given to government officials and front-line officials to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and save lives by helping individuals avoid serious illness when infected with Kovid 19 and reduce treatment in The hospital.
In addition, he stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made efforts to find all these vaccines to give to all people living in Cambodia, from the first dose to the third dose to the fourth dose. In the year 2022.
The governor added that all these vaccines sold in the market are very expensive, very necessary for humanity in the world. But the Cambodian people are very lucky to have Samdech Techo as their leader and he has sought to vaccinate everyone. "There is a vaccine, we have a strong defense to fight Kovid 19 very effectively."
The provincial governor also instructed all government officials in the province who have been vaccinated and not to drop the measures of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19, especially to follow the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. 3 Do not and 3 protect "consistently.
In that, the government officials in the province and the front line who went to get vaccinated against Kovid 19 each were happy to receive the vaccine and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia for giving them priority.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit, through the press conference forum, expressed the different meanings between the Victory Day on January 7 and the commemoration of the political victory day on December 29. Included in the calendar, but no breaks are required.
Mr. Phay Siphan claimed that January 7 was the day of victory over the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which liberated the people from the massacre, and this day has universal value for humanity. He said that if there was no January 7 Liberation Day, maybe the Cambodian people would be less than today. On the other hand, probably no one can escape to the United States.
Phay Siphan further compared December 29, a day to commemorate Victory Day, to July 4, the day of US independence.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has issued a circular on the designation of the Victory Political Day on December 29 in the annual calendar without a break. This circular was signed on January 14, 2022.
1. All ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces and private public institutions shall designate the Victory Political Day on December 29 in the annual calendar with no holidays from 2022 onwards.
2: All ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces and private public institutions must prepare banners and slogans to celebrate the Victory Day, which reads, "Thank you, peace!" Thank you, politics wins! "Grateful to the founders, guides, and victorious political operators who bring complete peace and national unity!"
Ministry of Economy issues official decision to continue to provide cash to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 for the 8th round
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a formal decision on continuing to provide cash assistance to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 for the eighth round. This is according to the decision that Fresh News received on January 21.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to continue to implement the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 for another 9 months, until the end of September 2022.
This cash subsidy announcement is made in rounds, with each round lasting 3 months. So far, there have been eight rounds.
